-east Asia Sep 30 2026 21.58 EDTUS trade regulator opens investigation into AI giants including Anthropic and OpenAISep 30 2026 14.35 EDTTrump AI deal rebrands ‘artificial intelligence’ as ‘superintelligence’Sep 29 2026 19.21 EDTAnthropic ‘warns of existential AI risks to humanity’ in IPO documentSep 29 2026 06.17 EDTdouble quotation markAs AI models go rogue, do you still trust OpenAI and Anthropic to stop them? I don’t and neither should youChris Stokel-WalkerSep 29 2026 01.00 EDT…… commentsAI godfathers warn of runaway ‘intelligence explosion’Sep 28 2026 11.00 EDTAnthropic will not appear at Senate inquiry into AI and datacentres amid fallout from OpenAI hack Sep 28 2026 04.00 EDTHeads of OpenAI and Anthropic called to face Senate inquiry after rogue agent incidentsSep 26 2026 10.00 EDTdouble quotation markIt’s going to take more than an email to a public inbox to protect Australians from potential AI doomTom McIlroySep 25 2026 10.58 EDT…… commentsOpenAI’s Altman and Anthropic’s Amodei address UN security council Sep 23 2026 17.15 EDTThe Conversationdouble quotation markHow would AI actually ‘kill all humans’? Here are the top five most likely scenariosToby Walsh for the ConversationSep 22 2026 20.51 EDT…… commentsFull StoryWhat an AI deal could mean for Australian culture – podcastPodcast18:43double quotation markCan Trump and Xi cooperate to guide humanity through the AI revolution? Humanity might depend on itAlan FinkelSep 20 2026 18.00 EDT…… commentsWhy China is pushing back on US warnings over rapid AI developmentSep 20 2026 02.00 EDTAbout 160 results for Anthropic1234...","title":"Anthropic | The Guardian","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/anthropic","id":472},{"content_hash":"ad6b19c7cc2d9c69617cb890067ee5c7d9575dc0338c6d530911acebab2baf0f","domain":"www.koreatimes.co.kr","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:28:21.141690+00:00","final_url":"https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/entertainment/films","language":"","text":"'Bedford Park' director tells Korean American story she wanted to seeBUSAN — Stephanie Ahn, director of the American drama film \"Bedford Park,\" said Thursday her longing to see a film that deeply explores the Korean American experience inspired her to make her first feature. The film, which won the U.S. Dramatic Special Jury Award for Debut Feature at Sundance, portrays an unlikely bond between Korean American physical therapist Audrey (Moon Choi) and Eli (Son Suk-ku), a Korean immigrant who was adopted by a white family. \"There are so many Korean American or Asian American stories that have been made that I so admire, and they have certainly opened doors for me as well, but I felt they touched upon the Korean or Asian American experience in sort of a surface level,\" Ahn told reporters in a group interview held on the occasion of the Busan International Film Festival (BIFF). \"There wasn't a story that reached that made me feel like I was seen personally deep inside,\" she said. With a keen sense of authenticity, \"Bedford Park,\" does not gloss over the backgrounds or surroundings of the two lead characters, but lays bare their family trauma and personal w17h agoBy Yonhap","title":"Films","url":"https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/entertainment/films","id":473},{"content_hash":"dc3d498892489f4948c37f063beefc81bf04a1f9753b9625ac52ab376c1476bc","domain":"timesofindia.indiatimes.com","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:28:21.114095+00:00","final_url":"https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/astrology/horoscope/shani-pitru-amavasya-daan-by-rashi-what-each-sign-should-donate-on-10-october/articleshow/134789883.cms","language":"","text":"Shani-Pitru Amavasya Daan by Rashi: What Each Sign Should Donate on 10 October - The Times of IndiaEditionININUSGCCEnglishEnglishहिन्दीमराठीಕನ್ನಡதமிழ்বাংলাമലയാളംతెలుగుગુજરાતીWeatherSign InTOIAstrologyHoroscopeSun Sign PredictionsCompatibility CalculatorYearly Horoscope 2026Chinese HoroscopeNumerologyNumerology PredictionsPlanets TransitsGemstones Vastu & feng shuikundali dasha & RemediesReligionMonthly HoroscopeOthersToday's ePaperLiveNewsAstrology NewsHoroscope NewsShani-Pitru Amavasya Daan by Rashi: What Each Sign Should Donate on 10 OctoberTrendingHoroscope TodayAries Horoscope TodayDaily Career HoroscopeDaily Nadi HoroscopeTaurus Horoscope TodayGemini Horoscope TodayHoroscope TodayAries Horoscope TodayDaily Career HoroscopeDaily Nadi HoroscopeTaurus Horoscope TodayGemini Horoscope TodayHoroscope TodayAries Horoscope TodayDaily Career HoroscopeDaily Nadi HoroscopeTaurus Horoscope TodayGemini Horoscope TodayShani-Pitru Amavasya Daan by Rashi: What Each Sign Should Donate on 10 OctoberNeeraj Dhankher / TOI Astrology / Oct 09, 2026, 08:30 ISTSaveCommentsShareAa+Text SizeSmallMediumLargePrint On October 10, the dual observance of Sarva Pitru Amavasya and Shani Amavasya marks an important moment for charitable giving, or daan. It's a day cherished by grandmothers, who typically highlight the significance of supporting those in need. Donations may vary depending on one's Moon sign, including essentials like rice, lentils, or clothing. The sincerity and timing of these contributions are believed to greatly enhance their impact. Ask any grandmother what matters most on Amavasya, and the answer usually comes fast: daan. Giving something to someone who needs it.This Saturday, 10 October, that advice carries extra weight. It's Sarva Pitru Amavasya and Shani Amavasya on the same day. A donation made now is believed to reach the ancestors and soften Saturn's effects together.Two things suit everyone. A handful of black til, and a proper meal given to a hungry person. Beyond that, your Moon sign can guide what to add.Mesh (Aries)You're in the first phase of Sade Sati. Donate masoor dal and jaggery along with black til. Giving to a poor labourer or construction worker is especially good for you.Vrishabh (Taurus)Shukra rules your sign. Offer white rice, sugar or a white cloth to a needy family. Feeding a cow before noon helps too.Mithun (Gemini)Whole green moong and fresh green vegetables suit Budh. Give them at a temple or to someone who runs a community kitchen.Kark (Cancer)The Moon is your ruler, so milk, rice and water work best. Setting up a small water point for passers-by outside your gate is a lovely option.Simha (Leo)Ashtama Shani is running for you. Donate wheat and jaggery in the morning for the Sun, then black til and mustard oil in the evening for Shani.Kanya (Virgo)Books, notebooks and pens for children who can't afford them are ideal. Mercury favours anything connected to learning.Tula (Libra)Ghee and white sweets suit Shukra. Offer them at a temple or share them with a family that can't celebrate the upcoming festivals easily.Vrishchik (Scorpio)A red cloth, honey or masoor dal works well for Mangal. Donating blood, if your health allows, is a modern remedy many astrologers support.Dhanu (Sagittarius)Kantaka Shani makes Saturday important for you. Add yellow items like chana dal, turmeric or bananas for Guru, alongside urad dal for Shani.Makar (Capricorn)Shani is your own ruler. A black blanket, a steel vessel or a pair of sturdy slippers for a daily wage earner suits you most.Kumbh (Aquarius)You're in the last phase of Sade Sati. An umbrella, a blanket or a warm meal for sanitation workers is believed to bring quick relief.Meen (Pisces)Sade Sati is at its peak for you. Yellow clothes and chana dal please Guru, your ruling planet. Spending time at an old-age home, perhaps with fruit or a shawl, may help even more.How to GiveDonate after the shraddh rituals and before sunset. Hand items over directly where possible, with respect. Leftover food or worn-out things aren't considered proper daan.And don't worry about doing everything on the list. One sincere offering, given quietly, is believed to count far more than a showy pile.Get the latest astrology news and horoscope updates. Download the TOI App.About the AuthorNeeraj DhankherAcharya Neeraj Dhankher is a Vedic Astrologer. He is the Founder and CEO of Astro Zindagi. He has been providing Astrological counsel to individuals, corporations, and businesses for more than 29 years. His mission is to empower people through astrological guidance.Read MoreEnd of ArticleFollow Us On Social MediaHot PicksCBSE Date SheetGeorgia Medical Degree RowAparna JhaStock market crashH-1B ProgramRBI Repo Rate HikeNana PatekarWeather tomorrowUS Marines in JapanAmazon PrimeTop TrendingKyrie IrvingCristiano RonaldoJaime Chapman BoyfriendJerry JonesUS Iran WarINDIA Bloc ProtestBengaluru CJP ProtestSimone BilesCJP Chappal ProtestAEW Pac DeathTired of too many ads?go ad free nowTrending StoriesIn AstrologyEntire Website9 October 2026 Forecast: Numerologist maps 12-month journey; focus on career, loveLucky Numbers And Colours: Libra Moon links with Number 2; forecast shares timingsMoon Enters Libra: Daily lucky numbers and colours shared; guide all 12 zodiac signsBhagyank Vs Namank: Birth date or name lead; guide to reading both togetherPisces Horoscope Today: Family joy, honest love and mindful work; carry water, be sensibleFacing Change With Steadiness: Krishna’s dhira stays calm; small anchors build balanceOctober 09, 2026 Horoscope: Zodiac guide to health and money; tips on travel and familyAquarius Horoscope: Stuck money returns for natives; pause before reacting todayCapricorn Horoscope Today: Smooth progress in work, love and money; use focus to finish tasksPractise Peace Amid Problems: Dhammapada 202 urges calm now; small rests build steadinessNeighbors Challenge Estate Plans: Kelce’s Ohio fence fight widens; sewer, wildlife fears growBypoll Election Results 2026 Live Updates: Bypoll counting today for five assembly seats, one Lok Sabha seat in AssamKay Adams’ Reactions Go Viral: Clip eclipses Gronk’s Chargers take; fans ask what happenedHurricane Milton Relief Donations: Brady, Swift fuel $6.1m aid drive; app campaign matches giftsFaith Guides Wedding Plans: Gracie Hunt leans on Christian counseling; calls engagement a vulnerable timeBeauty Re