ng‘Why The Silence On Oct 7?’: Abdul El-Sayed Walks Away From Reporter; Then Rips TrumpA Very Merry Breakup Trailer​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​ : Elizabeth Guest and Timm Sharp Starrer A Very Merry Breakup Official Trailer​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​‘Not Playing This Game’: Marco Rubio Unloads On Reporter Over Kimberly Guilfoyle’s $100,000 BribeRoyal GP Murder Shock: Husband’s ‘Burglar’ Account Emerges After Hannah Cain Found DeadMusk's Team Trump Return? POTUS Resets Ties After Public Epstein Feud, Calls Him 'Modern Edison'Zohran Mamdani Grilled Over Oct. 7 Post; Reporter Asks: ‘Will You Apologize To Netanyahu?’‘Canada-EU Deal Done’: Mark Carney Slams Trump's Tariff Move In New PresserChrista HELPED Executioners? Pike Lawyers' SHOCKER Adds BIG Twist To Failed Execution MysteryRiyadh Airspace SHUT! Airlines Cancel Hundreds Of Flights After Houthis BLOW UP Saudia Airbus JetPresley Gerber’s Drug Battle Blamed For Tragic Final Chapter As Years-Long Addiction Struggle EmergeTrump-Vance Clash? POTUS Honors Microsoft CEO Satya Nadella As VP Targets Tech Giant Over H-1B VisasMen Trailer​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​ : Jessie Buckley and Rory Kinnear Starrer Men Official Trailer​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​JD Vance Exposes H-1B Scam!: 6,000 Americans Duped; Microsoft, Wipro & TCS On Visa HitlistLatest News'Workers with AI skills in demand, but GenAI is hitting white-collar hiring'Anne Carson wins Nobel Prize in Literature: What we know about her brother, memoir ‘Nox’ and her India connectionQuote of the day by Leonardo da Vinci: \"Men of lofty genius sometimes accomplish the most when they work least, for their minds are occupied with their ideas...to which they afterwards give form.\"Patrick Mahomes and Brittany Mahomes’ Kansas City Current takes a step toward expansion with $235 million funding approvalAquarius Shani Horoscope Today, 9 October 2026: Saturn Says Read the Fine Print on Shared Money; Uttara Phalguni Moon Opens a Hidden FileWho is Jaime Chapman’s boyfriend? All about the NRLW star’s rugby league romance'Hanuman Ansh' box office collection day 63: Vishal Chaturvedi's film earns Rs 75 lakhs; worldwide gross reaches Rs 427.43 crore; India net total stands at Rs 327.98 crore'Sigma' box office collection day 7: Jason Sanjay's film earns Rs 8.27 cr India net; Soori's film reaches Rs 100.58 cr'Drishyam 3: The Conclusion' box office collection day 7: Ajay Devgn-Tabu film earns Rs 13 crore; worldwide gross headed for Rs 400 crore markSteep margins allow room for malpractice: Pharmaceuticals secretaryCapricorn Shani Horoscope Today, 9 October 2026: Saturn Says Send the Reply You Keep Drafting; Uttara Phalguni Moon Points to Good Advice'The Paradise' box office collection day 15 vs 'Don't Trouble The Trouble' day 7: Nani's film earns Rs 89 lakhs; worldwide gross reaches Rs 171.32 cr; Fahadh Faasil starrer collects Rs 4.41 cr India netKPSC scam candidates taken to resorts, provided with Q&A: EDWhat happened in viral video of Dodgers fan refusing ball to child? Incident explainedCorey Pavin reveals wife Lisa’s cancer ‘never went away completely’ months after her final chemotherapy sessionDaily Career Horoscope, October 09, 2026: Success, challenges, and breakthroughs; Know about your careerMalhar Patekar on father Nana Patekar's legacy: 'His achievements have made him immortal'Sagittarius Shani Horoscope Today, 9 October 2026: Saturn Says Home First, Career Second; Uttara Phalguni Moon Puts Your Work on DisplayCopyright © 2026 Bennett, Coleman & Co. Ltd. All rights reserved. For reprint rights: Times Syndication ServiceFollow Us On","title":"Bhagyank vs Namank: Which Number Matters More When Your Name and Birth Date Disagree?","url":"https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/astrology/numerology-tarot/bhagyank-vs-namank-which-number-matters-more-when-your-name-and-birth-date-disagree/articleshow/134789443.cms","id":556},{"content_hash":"01f64f2ec72914dbffcb3622393b5b7b96b5313a8cf0515b4002d88e6be867b7","domain":"www.abc.net.au","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:28:05.804087+00:00","final_url":"https://www.abc.net.au/news/lily-kristanto/105094090","language":"","text":"Lily Kristanto - ABC NewsSkip to main contentSkip to news navigation, settings and searchExplore the ABC More from ABCClose menuABC ABC News ABC iview ABC listen Kids & Students Indigenous Information & ServicesEditorial PoliciesRead our editorial guiding principlesFollow the ABCnewsiviewlistenLoadingABC NewsJust InFor YouPoliticsWorldBusinessAnalysisSportLifestyleEntertainmentQuizzesMoreSearchNews HomeJust InFor YouAnalysisRuralWatch LiveHealthIndigenousPoliticsScienceDeep TimeElectionsWorldEnvironmentInvestigationsBusinessLocal newsQuizzesSportAFLNRLFootballTennisCricketNetballLifestyleWellbeingRelationships & FamilyFood & RecipesPersonal FinanceHome & GardenEntertainmentTV & MoviesBooksMusicPop CultureArtsFacebookYouTubeInstagramTwitterEmergencyBackstoryNewsletters中文新闻BERITA BAHASA INDONESIATOK PISIN Appearance (BETA) Follow system settings Select an optionAlways lightAlways darkFollow system settingsABC iViewABC ListenLily KristantoLily is an award-winning journalist based in ABC's Gippsland newsroom in Victoria. She joined the ABC as a news cadet in 2025 and has previously worked in the Perth newsroom and the Asia-Pacific newsroom in Melbourne.In 2025, she won a Quill Award for her investigation into exploitation within Australia's working holiday visa program.Contact Lily KristantoLatest by Lily KristantoGippsland registers nine earthquakes in 9 daysA series of earthquakes have hit Victoria's east in the past week. Experts say it is an example of normal aftershock behaviour.Topic:EarthquakesFri 9 Oct 2026 at 3:51pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 3:51pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 3:51pmHighway potholes puncture tyres after Victoria's latest bout of rainLarge sharp-edged potholes have opened up along Victorian roads and highways after heavy rain across the state since Friday.Topic:RoadsSat 3 Oct 2026 at 3:43pmSat 3 Oct 2026 at 3:43pmSat 3 Oct 2026 at 3:43pmTeen killed in western Vic crash remembered as 'bubbly' and 'bright'A 14-year-old who died in a horror collision in western Victoria on Sunday night while returning from a volleyball tournament has been remembered as an \"amazing human being\".Topic:Road Accidents and IncidentsTue 29 Sep 2026 at 5:11pmTue 29 Sep 2026 at 5:11pmTue 29 Sep 2026 at 5:11pmHunt continues for man who allegedly attacked parents and brother with axePolice are urging people to remain vigilant and report any sightings of a man who allegedly attacked his parents and brother with an axe in Victoria's east. Topic:CrimeMon 7 Sep 2026 at 10:57amMon 7 Sep 2026 at 10:57amMon 7 Sep 2026 at 10:57amGlobal penguin experts gather at Phillip Island under shadow of climate change, bird fluMore than 200 experts meet on Phillip Island to share penguin research from across the globe.Topic:BirdsSat 5 Sep 2026 at 8:40amSat 5 Sep 2026 at 8:40amSat 5 Sep 2026 at 8:40amLicence loss, fines for companies hosting migrants in shoddy housingVictorian labour hire companies that house migrant workers in substandard accommodation will risk losing their licence under changes aimed at protecting vulnerable workers.Topic:Agricultural WorkersMon 17 Aug 2026 at 6:31amMon 17 Aug 2026 at 6:31amMon 17 Aug 2026 at 6:31amFears bird flu could have 'devastating' effect on Phillip Island penguinsConservationists say they fear the arrival of H5 bird flu in Australia could have a devastating impact on Phillip Island's penguin population.Topic:Avian InfluenzaWed 5 Aug 2026 at 5:25pmWed 5 Aug 2026 at 5:25pmWed 5 Aug 2026 at 5:25pmFire brigade pushes for compensation after 22 members diagnosed with cancerIn Nar Nar Goon's fire brigade, 22 volunteers have been diagnosed with cancer. But as members work to obtain their work insurance cover, almost half of the members are not covered by the state's presumptive legislation.Topic:Emergency ServicesFri 24 Jul 2026 at 4:56amFri 24 Jul 2026 at 4:56amFri 24 Jul 2026 at 4:56amRescue crews searching for kayaker, missing in Goulburn RiverAn SES spokesperson said the missing man is a \"strong swimmer\", but the current was \"flowing quite rapidly\".Topic:Canoeing and KayakingSat 18 Jul 2026 at 3:50pmSat 18 Jul 2026 at 3:50pmSat 18 Jul 2026 at 3:50pmCommunity fights back against caravan park development proposalA community group in Victoria's south-east will appeal a council planning decision to approve the development of a regional caravan park, which it says would be an \"absolute disaster\" for the region.Topic:Regional Development and PlanningTue 19 May 2026 at 7:28amTue 19 May 2026 at 7:28amTue 19 May 2026 at 7:28amVictorians wake to snow a month out from ski seasonSnow has fallen on Victoria's higher peaks overnight, as below-zero temperatures blast the state.Topic:SnowThu 7 May 2026 at 12:34pmThu 7 May 2026 at 12:34pmThu 7 May 2026 at 12:34pmCouple says loophole allowing theft from cars shipped interstateElihu and Amanda Del Valle say thousands of dollars worth of their belongings were stolen from the boot of their car when it was shipped from Melbourne to Perth, but police aren't able to investigate.Topic:Marine Transport IndustrySun 19 Apr 2026 at 3:06pmSun 19 Apr 2026 at 3:06pmSun 19 Apr 2026 at 3:06pmRegional drivers shift gears to electric vehicles as fuel prices climbEV uptake in regional Victoria is on the rise, but is everyone willing to make a switch?Topic:Electric VehiclesFri 3 Apr 2026 at 6:06amFri 3 Apr 2026 at 6:06amFri 3 Apr 2026 at 6:06amFears Easter travellers will hit the brakes as fuel prices climbMany Australian families are adjusting their Easter travel plans as eye-watering fuel prices continue to rise.Topic:Petrol PricesThu 12 Mar 2026 at 2:39pmThu 12 Mar 2026 at 2:39pmThu 12 Mar 2026 at 2:39pmBlack mould, sewage and overcrowding in migrant worker accommodationMigrant workers in Victoria's east were made to pay $190 a week to their employer for overcrowded, mouldy accommodation.Topic:Agricultural WorkersTue 24 Feb 2026 at 7:03amTue 24 Feb 2026 at 7:03amTue 24 Feb 2026 at 7:03amArson squad investigates two downgraded bushfires in Perth's eastPolice are investigating bushfires reported in the nearby suburbs of Boya and Koongamia, which firefighters bring under control on Saturday.Topic:BushfiresSat 3 Jan 2026 at 6:53pmSat 3 Jan 2026 at 6:53pmSat 3 Jan 2026 at 6:53pmCouncillor resigns for personal reasons after 'accidental' strip club visitA City of Joondalup councillor, who lodged an expense claim for a drink he bought at a strip club, resigns from the council citing \"personal reasons\".Topic:Local GovernmentWed 26 Nov 2025 at 10:38pmWed 26 Nov 2025 at 10:38pmWed 26 Nov 2025 at 10:38pmCall for men to step up and help end family and domestic violenceMen and boys are being urged to play a part in changing the culture of violence against women and children, as the annual 16 Days in WA campaign began with a rally in the Perth CBD.Topic:Domestic ViolenceWed 26 Nov 2025 at 9:49amWed 26 Nov 2025 at 9:49amWed 26 Nov 2025 at 9:49am'There was none better': Renowned WA musician Guy Ghouse dies, aged 56Western Australian musician Guy Ghouse dies at the age of 56 after a two year battle with cancer.Topic:MusicFri 21 Nov 2025 at 5:23pmFri 21 Nov 2025 at 5:23pmFri 21 Nov 2025 at 5:23pmPolice gain access to Westfield Carousel cameras in crime crackdownCameras that record the number plates of all the vehicles that enter one of Perth's biggest shopping centres are being used to track criminals, WA police have revealed.Topic:CrimeFri 21 Nov 2025 at 5:00pmFri 21 Nov 2025 at 5:00pmFri 21 Nov 2025 at 5:00pmWoman being questioned by police after baby found dead in Perth's southPolice are investigating after an eight-month-old baby was found dead at a home in Perth's southern suburbs.Topic:PoliceThu 30 Oct 2025 at 7:24pmThu 30 Oct 2025 at 7:24pmThu 30 Oct 2025 at 7:24pmThe candidates putting a fresh face on WA's local government electionsIn the last local government elections in WA, the average age of candidates running for councils was 53 years old — but these young candidates are keen to lower that figure. Topic:Local GovernmentFri 17 Oct 2025 at 8:20amFri 17 Oct 2025 at 8:20amFri 17 Oct 2025 at 8:20amCommunity rocked, man in custody after suspected stabbing murder in Perth's northA man is in custody and homicide detectives are investigating following the death of a man in Perth's northern suburbs.Topic:HomicideTue 14 Oct 2025 at 7:45pmTue 14 Oct 2025 at 7:45pmTue 14 Oct 2025 at 7:45pm'Enough is enough': Family wants domestic violence action after killer pleads guiltyPeter Damjanovic changes his plea at the last minute and pleads guilty to murdering his former partner Tiffany Woodley at her home in Bedford two years ago. WARNING: Indigenous readers are advised this story contains photos of someone who has died.Topic:HomicideThu 5 Mar 2026 at 5:23pmThu 5 Mar 2026 at 5:23pmThu 5 Mar 2026 at 5:23pmFinal 'game changing' piece of Metronet rail project opening in Perth's south-east More than half a billion dollars over budget, the long-awaited Byford rail extension in Perth's south-east is opening to commuters.Topic:Public TransportSun 12 Oct 2025 at 2:49pmSun 12 Oct 2025 at 2:49pmSun 12 Oct 2025 at 2:49pmLoad more stories aboveGot a news tip?If you have inside knowledge of a topic in the news, contact the ABC.Confidential Tip‑offIf you are a whistleblower, believe you have sensitive information that should be made public, or wish to protect your identity, find our more secure options.Confidential Tip‑offNot confidential? Contact ABC News and investigations.Top StoriesVictorian language charity with $16m kitty has links to white nationalistsFamilies of men killed on Mexico surf trip call for maximum sentencesFormer Bachelor Sam Wood to fight for bail application on domestic violence chargesATO delays credit card ban as government backs down after business backlashHow the card surcharge ban could change our relationship with cashWoman, 71, treated on 'cold floor' of Adelaide hospitalData centre operator Firmus pulls blockbuster ASX float after lacklustre demandMass evacuations, cars washed away in Chilean flooding disasterSydney councillor accuses Indigenous elder Mick Mundine of sexual assault'Beau L-C' rental car card among items found near bodies, jury hearsliveButters unveiled by Bulldogs after 'megadeal', Blakey makes his decisionFederal government backtracks on disaster funding splitUS army's first firing squad execution since WW2 to be publicThese are the frontrunners for this year's Nobel Peace Prize Powderfinger confirm reunion, 16 years after breaking upBack to topABC NewsContact ABC NewsYour home of Australian stories, conversations and events that shape our nation.This service may include material from Agence France-Presse (AFP), APTN, Reuters, AAP, CNN and the BBC World Service which is copyright and cannot be reproduced.Follow ABC NewsSectionsABC News HomeJust InFor YouWatch Live NewsLive ABC NewsRadioPoliticsElectionsAustraliaWorldSportLive SportRuralBusinessAnalysisScienceHealthLifestyleEntertainmentQuizzesMore TopicsNews in LanguageChinese 中文Tok PisinBerita Bahasa IndonesiaRelatedABC News appLocal NewsABC EmergencyABC IndigenousABC Religion & EthicsABC AsiaABC PacificMusic & AudioABC Listen Hometriple jLive RadioMovies & TVABC iview HomeList of ABC ShowsLive TVTV GuideKids & StudentsBTNEducationHeywireTakeoverABC KidsGet the ABC News AM newsletter Get the latest ABC News delivered to your email inboxEmail addressSubscribeYour information is being handled in accordance with the ABC Privacy Collection Statement. All ABC newslettersStay informed and connected with the ABC. Covering a wide range of topics and brands including News, iview, listen, and more.Browse all ABC newslettersABC homeInformation & ServicesEditorial PoliciesAccessibilityHelpContact UsCommercialCareersAbout the ABCPrivacy PolicyTerms of Use© 2026 ABCFollow the ABCWe acknowledge Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples as the First Australians and Traditional Custodians of the lands where we live, learn and work.","title":"Lily Kristanto","url":"https://www.abc.net.au/news/lily-kristanto/105094090","id":557},{"content_hash":"23a30b178b218d77761e1b0cf3ffcf2dc229ef2b85fe4cb413e7f4014d9549b1","domain":"www.theglobeandmail.com","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:28:05.600079+00:00","final_url":"https://www.theglobeandmail.com/topics/elon-musk/","language":"","text":"Elon Musk - The Globe and Mail HomeCanadaBusinessInvestingLifeOpinionWorldPoliticsPersonal FinanceCultureSportsMoreMoreLatest in MoreReal EstateDriveWatchlistFor YouEventsFind clarity in the chaos. Subscribe now and save 70%SUBSCRIBE FROM $0.99/WEEKDigital accessDigital + home deliveryElon MuskLatest articlesOctober 7, 2026Elon Musk calls on Quebec, Alberta and Saskatchewan to separate from Canada4 min readOctober 6, 2026opinionWhy do tech CEOs sound like doomsday cult leaders?Leah Eichler5 min readSeptember 24, 2026Trump administration to join Elon Musk in challenging EU’s fine on X2 min readSeptember 18, 2026opinionDon’t believe the calls for slower AI development will work. The juggernaut will keep rollingEric Reguly4 min readSeptember 16, 2026EU’s von der Leyen backs AI slowdown, to invite industry leaders for talks2 min readSeptember 15, 2026AI is too big to slow in a geopolitical raceMike Dolan4 min readSeptember 14, 2026Trump plays down AI concerns, calls it a conspiracy against the technology5 min readSeptember 14, 2026Global AI stocks fall as industry chiefs call for slowing development4 min readSeptember 12, 2026opinionBig Tech and Big Oil have fused into an entity we might think of as Fossil TechNaomi Klein and Astra Taylor9 min readSeptember 4, 2026opinionSovereign individuals are a threat to democracy in the United States – and Canada, too Maxwell Cameron9 min readAugust 24, 2026Trump bought shares in Elon Musk’s SpaceX after June IPO, financial disclosure shows2 min readAugust 14, 2026Alphabet’s SpaceX stake hit $94-billion, a more than 100-fold jump since 20153 min readAugust 5, 2026Scientists now certain that a piece of a SpaceX rocket crashed into the moon3 min readAugust 5, 2026AMD falls as investors seek bigger AI payoff2 min readAugust 4, 2026SpaceX’s bumpy ride on the stock market may get bumpier4 min readJuly 23, 2026opinionThe culture wars come for The Odyssey – and missMarsha Lederman4 min readJuly 23, 2026Tesla shares plunge nearly 15% as once-bullish tone on robotaxis shifts3 min readJuly 22, 2026Elon Musk’s Tesla reports negative free cash flow for first time in more than two years3 min readJuly 17, 2026opinionThe privacy watchdog hasn’t forgotten Grok’s sexualized deepfakes. Neither should youJ.B. Branch4 min readJuly 16, 2026SpaceX keeps on tumbling and the sell-off could worsen as lockup restrictions lift on $123-billion of shares3 min readJuly 15, 2026opinionHow to determine the winners and losers of AIGeorge Athanassakos and Christian Dippel5 min readJuly 9, 2026Eight men indicted in planned drone, sniper attack on White House UFC event2 min readJuly 6, 2026Elon Musk’s bid to set aside Twitter fraud verdict rejected by US judge 3 min readJuly 3, 2026opinionGold, bitcoin, SpaceX and the dangers of market chameleonsTom Bradley3 min readJuly 2, 2026Why Succession mastermind Jesse Armstrong is still king of the media mountain6 min readPrev123NextTerms & ConditionsCommunity GuidelinesPrivacy PolicyDisclaimerSkip footer navigationSubscribeDigital + Home DeliveryDigital AccessGlobe2GoThe New York Times