þÖ¸~ûÖ]u?&½¬\u0005C\u0004t­Sÿ�gÿÙ","title":"","url":"https://i0.wp.com/prnigeria.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/onsa.jpeg?fit=552%2C555&ssl=1","id":627},{"content_hash":"a22a797d72ececd19a5c02cc53aba272a88e58c1697e088a5edf6dac8bad73df","domain":"ml.com","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:50.032026+00:00","final_url":"https://www.ml.com/articles/financial-checklist.html","language":"","text":"How’s your financial plan doing? Use this checklist to review progress with your advisor and identify steps you can take to help your plan work harder for you. Think of it as an annual financial tune-up. MORE THAN HALF OF AMERICANS don’t engage in financial planning regularly.1 If you’ve already developed a plan with your advisor, you probably know what they’re missing out on — everything from a clear road map to suggested course corrections and the confidence to keep moving toward your goals. Don’t have a plan yet? Take the pop quiz below to learn more about the potential benefits. Already have one? Skip to “Your Financial Plan Checklist” and see if your plan’s keeping up with your life. Consider tackling the 12 suggestions below over time. Hint: There’s one action step for every month of the year. POP QUIZ Show text version Hide text version True or false: A financial plan can help you answer all of the questions below: How likely am I to reach my financial goals?How much should I be saving, spending and investing?What could my annual tax bill be in retirement?Should I consider adjusting my portfolio? Tap + to select correct answer and learn more True That’s right — all of that and much more. A good financial plan turns your vision into numbers, specific investment approaches and projections of potential future wealth. It quantifies the likely impact of tax obligations and inflation years from now and factors future costs and potential risks into your current strategies. To learn more, check out “6 surprising benefits of having a financial plan.” False Believe it or not, a good financial plan does all of that and much more. Check out “6 surprising benefits of having a financial plan.” YOUR FINANCIAL PLAN CHECKLIST 1. Ask yourself at least once a year: Does my financial plan still support my financial goals? Your priorities and situation may have changed. See how many of these scenarios apply to you: I haven’t reviewed my plan in the past six months.In the last year, I’ve had big changes in expenses or income.I’m not sure my budget and plan capture my values and priorities. One or more hit home? Consider these steps and questions to ask your advisor: 3 steps to consider: Listing your financial goals. Identify which are high and low priority.Talking with your partner to ensure you’re on the same page about goals.Checking your progress on short- and long-term goals. 3 questions to ask your advisor: How can I juggle competing financial goals and stay on track?How likely am I to reach my goals?What adjustments do I need to make to my financial plan? Source: Motley Fool Money, “These Are the Top Financial New Year’s Resolutions for 2026,” Nov. 19, 2025. Show text version Hide text version 25% Percentage of U.S. adults planning to pay off debt in 2026, the top financial goal 2. Anticipate big life changes Transitions are a part of life. Will you be ready financially? See how many of these scenarios apply to you: Life changes are coming that could change my financial picture (such as switching jobs, getting married, moving or retiring).My family members’ lives are changing (children going to college, parents needing more care, the birth of a child or grandchild).I’m thinking about going back to school, starting a side hustle or picking up an expensive hobby. One or more hit home? Consider these steps and questions to ask your advisor: 3 steps to consider: Adjusting your budget to reflect new expenses or changes to your income.Planning for what you’ll do with your workplace retirement account in the event of a job change.Updating who your financial account beneficiaries are. 3 questions to ask your advisor: Can I afford to assist my parents with their long-term care?How (and how much) can I help my adult children financially without endangering my own financial security? Do I have enough life and disability insurance given this change? Source: U.S. Census Bureau, “Calculating Migration Expectancy Using ACS Data,” August 2024 Show text version Hide text version 9.1 Number of times a person in the U.S. can expect to move after age 18 3. Stay on track for retirement To judge whether you’re on track for retirement, see how many of these scenarios apply to you: I have not raised my contributions for my 401(k), IRA or health savings account (HSA) in the past year.I am contributing to my workplace retirement plan but not collecting the full savings match that my employer provides.I am in my 50s and eligible to make catch-up contributions to my retirement plans, but I have not done so. One or more hit home? Consider these steps and questions to ask your advisor: 3 steps to consider: Increasing your savings rate to take full advantage of current contribution limits for IRAs, 401(k)s and HSAs.Making sure you’re taking advantage of the latest increased catch-up contribution limits if you’re age 50 or older.Creating a sufficient emergency fund so you can avoid dipping into your retirement accounts early to cover short-term needs. 3 questions to ask your advisor: Am I on track to meet my retirement goals?How can I balance saving for retirement with short-term goals like homebuying and debt repayments?Are my retirement savings invested properly to align with my goals and tolerance for risk? Source: Transamerica Center for Retirement Studies, “An Uncertain Future: Retirement Prospects of 4 Generations,” June 2025. Show text version Hide text version 36% Percentage of millennials who expect to retire before age 65 4. Calculate your retirement paycheck: How much income will you have in retirement? To ensure you have enough money to meet your needs throughout retirement, it’s important to craft a well-thought-out income and spending plan. To assess your retirement paycheck, see how many of these scenarios apply to you: I’m hitting one of the key dates for government benefits this year — ages 59½, 62, 65, 70 and 73.I don’t know how much I will collect from income sources such as Social Security, a pension, an annuity and required minimum distributions from tax-deferred accounts.I’m unsure whether my retirement plan can weather key retirement risks. One or more hit home? Consider these steps and questions to ask your advisor: 3 steps to consider: Going to the Social Security website to see estimates of your benefits if you claim early at age 62, at your full retirement age (66 or 67), or at age 70, when you’ll collect the maximum benefit.Estimating your retirement expenses and sources of income.Reviewing the age for required minimum distributions for your workplace retirement plans and IRAs. 3 questions to ask your advisor: Is my retirement spending plan able to withstand the risks of inflation, longevity and market volatility?Should I consider working past retirement age?How can my spouse and I ensure that we’re both leveraging our retirement income potential? Source: Social Security Administration, “Delayed Retirement Credits,” accessed December 2025. Show text version Hide text version 8% Increase in Social Security benefits for every year you delay claiming after full retirement age until age 70 5. Check up on your emergency fund Surprise expenses can put a dent in the best financial plans. See how many of these scenarios apply to you: My emergency fund would cover only a month or two of expenses.My emergency fund is tied up in stocks or other illiquid investments.I keep emergency savings in a non-interest-bearing bank account. One or more hit home? Consider these steps and questions to ask your advisor: 3 steps to consider: Steering more of your savings to your emergency fund until it reaches six months of expenses.Setting up automatic transfers from your checking to your savings account.Comparing rates on short-term savings vehicles to find the best return on your cash. 3 questions to ask your advisor: Do I have enough easily accessible cash available to handle a job loss?Are there other ways for me to quickly raise cash in an emergency?What are the best places for my emergency savings? Source: Bankrate’s 2024 Annual Emergency Savings Report Show text version Hide text version Did you know? Half of Americans with annual incomes of $100,000-plus have an emergency fund that would cover six months of expenses. 6. Review your insurance coverage: Do you have enough? The right insurance can help you pick up the pieces after unexpected life events, such as a natural disaster or death in the family. To test your preparedness, see how many of these scenarios apply to you: It’s been over a year since I checked my homeowners or renter’s insurance policy for disaster coverage.I don’t know if my life insurance policy is sufficient to support my dependents and wealth transfer goals.If I’m suddenly unable to work, I or my family won’t have income to live on. One or more hit home? Consider these steps and questions to ask your advisor: 3 steps to consider: Conducting an inventory of your possessions to make sure you have adequate homeowners or renters insurance.Evaluating life and disability coverage you have or can access through your job.Estimating how many years of income your family would need to replace if you were to die unexpectedly. 3 questions to ask your advisor: Will my family be fully protected if I were to become incapacitated or die unexpectedly?Do I need an individual disability insurance policy to supplement an employer’s group plan?What are the benefits of combining life insurance with an irrevocable trust? Source: Insurify, “Home Insurance Rates to Rise 8% in 2025, After a 20% Increase in the Last Two Years,” 2025. Show text version Hide text version 30.6% Projected increase in the average annual home insurance rate between 2022 and 2025 7. Plan for the uncertainties of future healthcare costs Healthcare costs are generally rising faster than inflation.2 To assess your healthcare coverage, see how many of these scenarios apply to you: I don’t have a health savings account (HSA).I haven’t built paying for long-term healthcare expenses later in life into my financial plan.I’m nearing retirement but haven’t yet considered future healthcare needs and coverage options. One or more hit home? Consider these steps and questions to ask your advisor: 3 steps to consider: Funding an HSA to save for future healthcare expenses.Shopping for long-term care insurance, including hybrid policies that provide an inheritance benefit if you don’t tap them.Extending your health insurance through COBRA or purchasing a private plan if you retire before you are eligible for Medicare at age 65. 3 questions to ask your advisor: How much should I be setting aside for future healthcare expenses?I don’t qualify for long-term care insurance because of a health condition. What other options do I have?I’m nearing retirement but haven’t yet considered future healthcare needs and coverage options. Source: KFF, “Health Care Costs and Affordability,” Oct. 8, 2025. Show text version Hide text version 87% Growth in average out-of-pocket healthcare costs per person, 2003–2023 8. Speed up paying down your debts Creating a targeted plan to pay off high-interest debt can help you reach other goals. To review your situation, see how many of these scenarios apply to you: My current loans or credit cards carry high interest rates.I haven’t looked into refinancing or consolidating these loans.I don’t have a plan for paying back what I owe in a timely manner. One or more hit home? Consider these steps and questions to ask your advisor: 3 steps to consider: Making a list of all debts and prioritizing paying off those with the highest interest rate.Cutting back on one monthly discretionary expense to put more money toward debt repayment.Refinancing or consolidating your debt to qualify for a lower rate. 3 questions to ask your advisor: Should I consider selling assets to pay off a debt?Is it worth it to pay off my mortgage early?How could borrowing against my investments help me manage my debts? Source: Bankrate, “Study: The states where being a homeowner has paid off the most (and the least),” Aug. 13, 2025. Show text version Hide text version 142% Increase in the amount of equity that homeowners have in their homes, on average nationwide, 2020–2025 9. Create a strategy for sharing your wealth Donating to a philanthropic cause you support or helping family members in your lifetime can be rewarding. To review your giving strategy, see how many of these scenarios apply to you: I am weighing making gifts to my heirs in my lifetime to reduce the size of my estate.I’m interested in funding a 529 plan for a grandchild to reduce my estate and retain control of the assets.I want to make a bigger impact with my charitable giving. One or more hit home? Consider these steps and questions to ask your advisor: 3 steps to consider: Identifying philanthropic causes you want to support.Weighing the benefits of 529 plans and custodial accounts to fund education costs.Reviewing the current gift tax exclusion limits to be sure you’re maximizing tax-free giving. 3 questions to ask your attorney, advisor, and accountant: Should I consider opening a donor-advised fund or a charitable trust?How can I support the charities I care about when I die?How can I make sure I’m leveraging gift tax exclusion limits in my plan? Source: Internal Revenue Service Show text version Hide text version Did you know? You can contribute up to $95,000 to a grandchild’s 529 plan in 2026 ($190,000 if you’re married and file jointly) without triggering the federal gift tax. 10. Shore up your estate plan Having an estate plan that reflects your wishes is an important part of financial planning. To pressure-test your plan, see how many of these scenarios apply to you: I haven’t reviewed my estate plan recently and am not sure it accurately reflects my intentions.I am missing a key document, such as a living will, healthcare directive, healthcare proxy or durable power of attorney.I have experienced changes in my life that might require updates to these documents. One or more hit home? Consider these steps and questions to ask your attorney and advisor: 3 steps to consider: Making sure you have an up-to-date will, living will, healthcare directive, healthcare proxy and durable power of attorney.Scheduling a family conversation to ensure that everyone understands your wishes.Reviewing your estate plan to make sure it reflects your current circumstances. 3 questions to ask your attorney, advisor, and accountant: What are the benefits of including a trust in my estate plan?What types of life events could warrant changes to my estate plan?What changes to the tax laws regarding estate planning do I need to know about? Source: Caring.com, 2025 Wills and Estate Planning Study Show text version Hide text version 24% Percentage of Americans who have a will 11. Look for ways to minimize taxes No matter your goals, tax laws can have an impact on how far your money goes. To see where you stand on tax planning, see how many of these scenarios apply to you: I don’t keep up on new tax laws or IRS rule changes that could impact my financial planning, including changes in tax rates, tax brackets and deductions.I’m considering converting a traditional IRA to a Roth IRA.I have losses in my investment portfolio that could be valuable for tax planning. One or more hit home? Consider these steps and questions to ask your advisor: 3 steps to consider: Meeting with a tax professional to discuss how to integrate tax planning into your overall financial plan.Reviewing your taxable portfolio for market losses that could minimize your tax bill through tax loss harvesting.Exploring the benefits of a Roth conversion. 3 questions to ask your accountant and advisor: How can I minimize taxes on my capital gains when I sell high-performing stocks?Am I taking full advantage of opportunities to save for long-term goals in tax-advantaged accounts?Should I consider converting a traditional IRA to a Roth IRA now? Source: Tax Foundation, “National Tax Literacy Poll: Assessing Taxpayer Knowledge and Perceptions of the US Tax System,” Dec. 18, 2024. Show text version Hide text version 66% Percentage of U.S. taxpayers who say the tax code is overly complex 12. Pressure-test your investment portfolio Reviewing — and possibly adjusting — your strategy regularly can help your investments stay on track as you pursue your financial goals. See how many of these scenarios apply to you: I am uneasy about how to manage risk as the financial markets and my circumstances change.I am not confident that my mix of stocks, bonds and other assets in my portfolio is still suitable for my risk tolerance and retirement timeline.I have never considered whether my investment strategy aligns with my values. One or more hit home? Consider these steps and questions to ask your advisor: 3 steps to consider: Reviewing your current portfolio allocation to see if it still matches your risk tolerance, timelines, cash needs and goals.Rebalancing your portfolio if your allocation no longer lines up with your targets.Adjusting your target stock-bond allocations to match your risk tolerance if you are not comfortable with market volatility. 3 questions to ask your advisor: How can I minimize the effect of risks like inflation and market volatility on my portfolio?Is my portfolio as diversified as it should be?Are there new market trends that I can take advantage of? Source: Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System, “Economic Well-Being of U.S. Households in 2024,” May 28, 2025. Show text version Hide text version 54% Percentage of U.S. adults who are largely uncomfortable choosing and managing investments Want a copy of this checklist to keep? Download one now to use as a starting point when consulting your advisor and reviewing what you need to do next to make the most of your financial strategy. Download checklist New to Merrill? Connect with a Merrill Advisor to discuss your priorities. There are items below that require your attention before submitting. Something went wrong! Your form couldn’t be submitted correctly. Please try again. Would you like us to contact you? Yes No First name* Last name* Email address* Confirm email address* Primary phone* Zip code* Investment minimum $250,000 By providing your contact information above, you agree that a representative of Merrill, the Brokerage affiliate of Bank of America Corporation, may contact you via telephone and/or email to discuss and/or offer investment products and services that may be appropriate for you. You agree that you are providing to us your consent for us to contact you regardless of any Do Not Call or Do Not Email privacy choices you may have previously expressed until you revoke this consent, or up to 90 days. You may revoke your consent at any time by notifying the Merrill representative. Submit Thank you. You’ll receive an automated email confirming receipt of your request shortly. A Merrill financial advisor will be in contact with you in the coming days. 1 Motley Fool Money, “Over Half of Americans Make This Serious Mistake With Their Financial Planning,” January 2024. 2 KFF, “Health Care Costs and Affordability,” May 28, 2024.","title":"How’s your financial plan doing?","url":"https://www.ml.com/articles/financial-checklist.html","id":628},{"content_hash":"558c6f4de9c91822e42c63e6fb4ac7cc5cc9ae22e262b9c75dd4b49d4790c5d5","domain":"www.lemonde.fr","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:49.581597+00:00","final_url":"https://www.lemonde.fr/archives/article/1951/11/08/la-premiere-reunion-de-la-6e-assemblee-generale-a-donne-un-exemple-de-celerite_2073161_1819218.html","language":"","text":"Affluence des grands jours, mais atmosphère des plus froides, en dépit d'une température d'étuve, dans cette salle du théâtre de Chaillot où pour la seconde fois dans l'histoire se réunit l'assemblée générale des Nations unies. L'enterrement de la cinquième session lundi n'avait pas duré une heure. Il n'a guère fallu plus de temps mardi pour entendre les discours d'usage et élire le nouveau président. Bel exemple de célérité, qui n'a d'égal que celui qu'ont fourni ouvriers et architectes en mettant les bouchées doubles pour achever pratiquement à temps les aménagements du palais. On aimerait que ces bonnes habitudes ne se perdissent pas trop vite... Sur la scène une cloison blanche des plus sobres porte en son centre sur fond d'azur l'emblème des Nations unies. A mi-hauteur s'ouvrent les fenêtres des \" aquariums \", où travaillent en permanente ébullition les \" interprètes simultanés \". Derrière une tribune banale, trois fauteuils rouge et or, du style de ceux qu'on utilise pour les grands mariages à la Madeleine et qui dans ce décor de clinique détonnent quelque peu. Sur le devant de la scène un autre fauteuil du même type amené à l'intention de M. Vincent Auriol; M. René Mayer, qui accompagne le président de la République, en l'absence de M. René Pleven retenu au Palais-Bourbon, a droit à un siège plus modeste, mais également plus moderne. Applaudis à leur passage dans le hait, voici les principaux délégués : MM. Eden, plus jeune que jamais en dépit de ses cheveux maintenant bien argentés ; Acheson, aussi britannique d'allure que possible, avec cependant à la boutonnière une énorme rosette rouge ; Robert Schuman, tout de gris vêtu, un bon sourire illuminant son visage. M. Vychinski, que flanque, sanglé dans un costume trop étroit, M. Jacob Malik, fait une entrée plus silencieuse, mais non moins remarquée. On attend un peu, cependant que Mme Vincent Auriol reçoit dans sa loge les compliments de nombreux admirateurs. Voici enfin l'heure solennelle. M. Entezam, délégué de l'Iran et président de l'assemblée sortante, prend place au fauteuil présidentiel. Entre MM. Trygve Lie et Andrew Cordier, qui ont l'un et l'autre des carrures de boxeurs, il a l'air tout fluet. Dans un français parfait il accueille le président de la République, auquel il donne la parole. Il vous reste 59.09% de cet article à lire. La suite est réservée aux abonnés.","title":"La première réunion de la 6e assemblée générale a donné un exemple de célérité","url":"https://www.lemonde.fr/archives/article/1951/11/08/la-premiere-reunion-de-la-6e-assemblee-generale-a-donne-un-exemple-de-celerite_2073161_1819218.html","id":629},{"content_hash":"0ab7bd3c14bae2db5cf11d5e606432a390fa0409b658be5599792b26924b8b3f","domain":"www.theconversation.com","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:49.493913+00:00","final_url":"https://theconversation.com/economy-trumps-climate-change-as-top-concern-12592","language":"","text":"Economy trumps climate change as top concern Published: March 3, 2013 6:36pm EST https://theconversation.com/economy-trumps-climate-change-as-top-concern-12592 https://theconversation.com/economy-trumps-climate-change-as-top-concern-12592 Link copied Share article Share article Copy link Email Bluesky Facebook WhatsApp Messenger LinkedIn X (Twitter) Print article Concerns about the economy rank higher than worries about climate change across the world, shows a recent survey by the International Social Survey Programme. A comparison of recent results with the same survey from 1993 showed little change noted on people’s concern for climate change. Respondents were asked the relative importance of eight issues: health care, education, crime, the environment, immigration, the economy, terrorism, and poverty. The survey found that people were five times more likely to point to the economy over the environment. “One reason for the relatively low ranking of climate change is that people often believed it did not directly affect them. Climate change is seen more as a country-level problem than as a personal problem,” stated Tom W. Smith, director of the General Social Survey and author of the survey’s results. Read more at The University of Chicago Source The University of Chicago","title":"Economy trumps climate change as top concern","url":"https://theconversation.com/economy-trumps-climate-change-as-top-concern-12592","id":630},{"content_hash":"2f5a78c0c095ea848fc7259c74baa4b6a38a5f024ff4bfa4381c2398f0b13d0c","domain":"www.abc.net.au","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:48.988299+00:00","final_url":"https://www.abc.net.au/news/brandon-long/103003534","language":"","text":"Brandon Long - ABC NewsSkip to main contentSkip to news navigation, settings and searchExplore the ABC More from ABCClose menuABC ABC News ABC iview ABC listen Kids & Students Indigenous Information & ServicesEditorial PoliciesRead our editorial guiding principlesFollow the ABCnewsiviewlistenLoadingABC NewsJust InFor YouPoliticsWorldBusinessAnalysisSportLifestyleEntertainmentQuizzesMoreSearchNews HomeJust InFor YouAnalysisRuralWatch LiveHealthIndigenousPoliticsScienceDeep TimeElectionsWorldEnvironmentInvestigationsBusinessLocal newsQuizzesSportAFLNRLFootballTennisCricketNetballLifestyleWellbeingRelationships & FamilyFood & RecipesPersonal FinanceHome & GardenEntertainmentTV & MoviesBooksMusicPop CultureArtsFacebookYouTubeInstagramTwitterEmergencyBackstoryNewsletters中文新闻BERITA BAHASA INDONESIATOK PISIN Appearance (BETA) Follow system settings Select an optionAlways lightAlways darkFollow system settingsABC iViewABC ListenBrandon LongBrandon Long is the Rural Reporter for ABC Southern Queensland, based in Toowoomba. Contact Brandon LongLatest by Brandon Long'Consumers should feel ripped off': How coffee brands have changedIf your coffee tastes different, you may not be imagining things. Brands have quietly changed their recipes and labels after bean prices surged to almost 50-year highs.Topic:SupermarketsFri 9 Oct 2026 at 7:33amFri 9 Oct 2026 at 7:33amFri 9 Oct 2026 at 7:33amProminent pork industry identity charged over alleged multi-million-dollar fraudDarren and Cameron Wilson have been charged over allegations they kept millions in sales off the books of a business for personal use between 2017 and 2026.Topic:CourtsTue 15 Sep 2026 at 7:52amTue 15 Sep 2026 at 7:52amTue 15 Sep 2026 at 7:52amHyper-scale data centre could draw quarter of Queensland's power usageThe proposed $30 billion data centre in Queensland has a peak capacity comparable to the average power requirements of 1.5 million households.Topic:Data CentresMon 14 Sep 2026 at 6:34amMon 14 Sep 2026 at 6:34amMon 14 Sep 2026 at 6:34amFire rips through distinctive Queensland highway hotelFire has engulfed Falvey's Sundowner Saloon on the Warrego Highway west of Brisbane, with emergency crews responding to the blaze.Topic:FiresThu 3 Sep 2026 at 1:28pmThu 3 Sep 2026 at 1:28pmThu 3 Sep 2026 at 1:28pmChina's rejection of Australian mung beans prompts chemical rethink China rejects 10 containers of Australian mung beans after testing found the shipment exceeded allowed chemical levels. Topic:HerbicidesFri 14 Aug 2026 at 11:14amFri 14 Aug 2026 at 11:14amFri 14 Aug 2026 at 11:14amSandstone miner scraps Lockyer Valley project after farmers' pleasA quiet farming community found itself at the centre of a major battle when mining threatened their land. What happened next surprised everyone.Topic:AgricultureSun 2 Aug 2026 at 6:47amSun 2 Aug 2026 at 6:47amSun 2 Aug 2026 at 6:47amBillion-dollar industry 'watching, not panicking' over bird flu spreadQueensland's poultry industry is on high alert after the state's first H5 bird flu detection, but consumers are being told there is no need to panic.Topic:Avian InfluenzaWed 29 Jul 2026 at 8:58amWed 29 Jul 2026 at 8:58amWed 29 Jul 2026 at 8:58amParts of Queensland drought declared for first time in two yearsParts of southern Queensland have been drought-declared for the first time in two years, with farmers facing worsening conditions after at least 12 months of below-average rainfall. Topic:DroughtsTue 28 Jul 2026 at 4:33pmTue 28 Jul 2026 at 4:33pmTue 28 Jul 2026 at 4:33pmThe unanswered question in the rush for Queensland's hidden oil jackpotAn expert is warning that the push to fast-track approvals for the proposed Taroom Trough lacks crucial detail.Topic:Oil and GasFri 17 Jul 2026 at 8:32amFri 17 Jul 2026 at 8:32amFri 17 Jul 2026 at 8:32amCrisp mornings forecast for southern Qld as temperatures dipAs Queenslanders brace for cooler temperatures this week, farmers on the Granite Belt are welcoming single digits to ensure their crops are thriving come harvest time.Topic:WeatherTue 7 Jul 2026 at 8:36amTue 7 Jul 2026 at 8:36amTue 7 Jul 2026 at 8:36amFuture of family farm at stake as young farmer opposes quarry A young Queensland farmer says his family's property is under threat from a proposed sandstone quarry, but the company behind the project insists there is nothing to fear.Topic:Mining Environmental IssuesWed 1 Jul 2026 at 7:48amWed 1 Jul 2026 at 7:48amWed 1 Jul 2026 at 7:48amFarmers claim partial victory after government backflips on gasFarmers are claiming a partial victory after the Queensland government backed down on controversial changes to gas mining approvals above a vital underground water source.Topic:AgricultureFri 26 Jun 2026 at 9:04amFri 26 Jun 2026 at 9:04amFri 26 Jun 2026 at 9:04amAlarm over suspected illegal sales of imported peanutsAustralian biosecurity authorities are probing claims imported raw peanuts are being sold illegally without quarantine checks and exposing the nation's own peanut industry to potential plant diseases.Topic:BiosecurityWed 24 Jun 2026 at 7:19amWed 24 Jun 2026 at 7:19amWed 24 Jun 2026 at 7:19amCattle company's own tip-off revealed biosecurity breachA NSW company tipped off authorities to the illegal movement of its cattle, triggering the investigation that led to the largest-ever biosecurity fine under a Queensland law. Topic:CourtsMon 1 Jun 2026 at 7:41amMon 1 Jun 2026 at 7:41amMon 1 Jun 2026 at 7:41am'The sword is still hanging': Farmers in limbo as Inland Rail land sits idleFor more than a decade, Australians in the path of the proposed Inland Rail corridor have wondered if the nation-building project will force them from their homes. Although the northern section has been scrapped, the legacy of its blueprints is still fuelling anxiety.Topic:Rail Transport IndustrySat 16 May 2026 at 11:57amSat 16 May 2026 at 11:57amSat 16 May 2026 at 11:57amSouthern Queensland graziers call for drought declarationGraziers start destocking to preserve dwindling feed with rainfall well below average across the region.Topic:DroughtsFri 15 May 2026 at 11:59amFri 15 May 2026 at 11:59amFri 15 May 2026 at 11:59amHow a remote farming community became Australia's first oil fieldWith oil exploration back in the headlines, here's how Australia struck it lucky in the 1960s.Topic:Oil and GasMon 27 Apr 2026 at 8:01amMon 27 Apr 2026 at 8:01amMon 27 Apr 2026 at 8:01amAustralia's largest cattle feedlot on the market as grain-fed beef surgesMort & Co, which fattens hundreds of thousands of cattle on grain before being slaughtered for beef, puts the majority of its assets on the market.Topic:Beef Cattle FeedlotsFri 22 May 2026 at 2:09pmFri 22 May 2026 at 2:09pmFri 22 May 2026 at 2:09pmFarmers take action as dry grips Queensland regionQueensland farmers gripped by a dry spell are turning to drastic and inventive measures: offloading most of their livestock and laying kilometres of water pipelines.Topic:DroughtsFri 10 Apr 2026 at 7:30amFri 10 Apr 2026 at 7:30amFri 10 Apr 2026 at 7:30amNational campdraft competition cancelled over soaring cost of fuelOne of Australia's biggest campdrafting events is postponed due to the fuel crisis, with organisers hoping to reschedule the event within a few months.Topic:Petrol PricesMon 30 Mar 2026 at 5:08pmMon 30 Mar 2026 at 5:08pmMon 30 Mar 2026 at 5:08pmFarmers clash with government over new water basin lawsThe Queensland government says new legislation will protect a vital groundwater reserve, but farmers warn the new laws will make things worse.Topic:Oil and GasMon 30 Mar 2026 at 2:56pmMon 30 Mar 2026 at 2:56pmMon 30 Mar 2026 at 2:56pmDiesel cost hikes hurt 'travelling city' of resilient showmenShowmen are determined to keep putting on agricultural shows for regional Australia despite the \"frightening\" cost of fuel. Topic:Petrol PricesSat 28 Mar 2026 at 10:54amSat 28 Mar 2026 at 10:54amSat 28 Mar 2026 at 10:54amPastoral company fined record $45,000 for Queensland biosecurity breachesA pastoral company has been hit with a record $45,000 fine after moving thousands of cattle across state lines without proper tracking. Authorities say the penalty sends a clear warning.Topic:BiosecurityTue 24 Mar 2026 at 6:08pmTue 24 Mar 2026 at 6:08pmTue 24 Mar 2026 at 6:08pmMore than 1,600 new gas wells approved for rural Queensland until 2081A major multinational gas venture has just secured federal approval to ramp up extraction in rural Queensland — locking in operations for the next 55 years.Topic:Oil and GasFri 20 Mar 2026 at 5:27pmFri 20 Mar 2026 at 5:27pmFri 20 Mar 2026 at 5:27pm'We want your ticks': Researchers investigate chemical resistance Queensland researchers are asking farmers to send them live cattle ticks as part of an effort to protect the nation's $17.7 billion cattle industry.Topic:AgricultureThu 19 Mar 2026 at 8:17amThu 19 Mar 2026 at 8:17amThu 19 Mar 2026 at 8:17amLoad more stories aboveGot a news tip?If you have inside knowledge of a topic in the news, contact the ABC.Confidential Tip‑offIf you are a whistleblower, believe you have sensitive information that should be made public, or wish to protect your identity, find our more secure options.Confidential Tip‑offNot confidential? Contact ABC News and investigations.Top StoriesVictorian language charity with $16m kitty has links to white nationalistsFamilies of men killed on Mexico surf trip call for maximum sentencesFormer Bachelor Sam Wood to fight for bail application on domestic violence chargesATO delays credit card ban as government backs down after business backlashHow the card surcharge ban could change our relationship with cashWoman, 71, treated on 'cold floor' of Adelaide hospitalData centre operator Firmus pulls blockbuster ASX float after lacklustre demandMass evacuations, cars washed away in Chilean flooding disasterSydney councillor accuses Indigenous elder Mick Mundine of sexual assault'Beau L-C' rental car card among items found near bodies, jury hearsliveButters unveiled by Bulldogs after 'megadeal', Blakey makes his decisionFederal government backtracks on disaster funding splitUS army's first firing squad execution since WW2 to be publicThese are the frontrunners for this year's Nobel Peace Prize Powderfinger confirm reunion, 16 years after breaking upBack to topABC NewsContact ABC NewsYour home of Australian stories, conversations and events that shape our nation.This service may include material from Agence France-Presse (AFP), APTN, Reuters, AAP, CNN and the BBC World Service which is copyright and cannot be reproduced.Follow ABC NewsSectionsABC News HomeJust InFor YouWatch Live NewsLive ABC NewsRadioPoliticsElectionsAustraliaWorldSportLive SportRuralBusinessAnalysisScienceHealthLifestyleEntertainmentQuizzesMore TopicsNews in LanguageChinese 中文Tok PisinBerita Bahasa IndonesiaRelatedABC News appLocal NewsABC EmergencyABC IndigenousABC Religion & EthicsABC AsiaABC PacificMusic & AudioABC Listen Hometriple jLive RadioMovies & TVABC iview HomeList of ABC ShowsLive TVTV GuideKids & StudentsBTNEducationHeywireTakeoverABC KidsGet the ABC News AM newsletter Get the latest ABC News delivered to your email inboxEmail addressSubscribeYour information is being handled in accordance with the ABC Privacy Collection Statement. All ABC newslettersStay informed and connected with the ABC. Covering a wide range of topics and brands including News, iview, listen, and more.Browse all ABC newslettersABC homeInformation & ServicesEditorial PoliciesAccessibilityHelpContact UsCommercialCareersAbout the ABCPrivacy PolicyTerms of Use© 2026 ABCFollow the ABCWe acknowledge Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples as the First Australians and Traditional Custodians of the lands where we live, learn and work.","title":"Brandon Long","url":"https://www.abc.net.au/news/brandon-long/103003534","id":631},{"content_hash":"27e4489f56b4c26d48ea16382c9385338fcce83c550effaa6d2e3a0a4cf6abf7","domain":"healthline.com","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:48.660375+00:00","final_url":"https://www.healthline.com/health/what-a-bipolar-manic-episode-feels-like","language":"","text":"The first time I became manic, I was awake for 3 days straight.Share on PinterestBipolar disorder runs in my family, but I didnât know that when I had my first manic episode. I was a hardworking, self-employed writer and photographer. A lifelong night owl, I was no stranger to late nights. Sometimes Iâd stay up all night, focused on a writing assignment. Other times Iâd stay out until 3 a.m. photographing concerts, then processing raw photos until sunup so they could be published that afternoon. I was living on my own terms, having the time of my life.So, when that first manic episode suddenly and without warning came on, it took a few days to realize something was wrong.I received a diagnosis of bipolar disorder in 2012 and have been on a strict treatment plan to manage the condition ever since. My day-to-day life is normal and well-managed. I take care of myself and take my meds without fail. If you didnât know, you wouldnât know I live with bipolar.But despite my best efforts, Iâve experienced mania again. If you donât know much about the implications of bipolar disorder, itâs important for you to know that mania is not necessarily what it seems.For me, itâs not a âsuper highâ or being âextremely happy.â Mania is overwhelming, terrifying, and exhausting. Hereâs what a day in the life of a bipolar manic episode feels like.7 a.m. The alarm goes off. I didnât get any sleep last night. I never got tired â my mind was racing. Idea after idea streamed through my mind, one after the next after the next. Articles I should write. Photographs I should take. And song lyrics. So many song lyrics, all taking on new meanings. Iâm so anxious. The Brainwave Tuner Sleep Induction app on my phone usually helps me fall and stay asleep, but it wasnât any help last night. I took two doses of sleeping pills over the course of the night, but my body overrode their effect. Am I manic again? I know I havenât missed any doses. Is my dose too low? 7:15 a.m.I sit up. With my left hand, I reach for the brown bottle of little white pills on my bedside and clutch my red water bottle with my right. I remove one pill and swallow my daily dose of hypothyroid medication, which needs to be taken on an empty stomach. Many people with bipolar disorder also have a thyroid condition or other dual diagnosis.8 a.m. I donât want to eat. Iâm not hungry. But my medication for bipolar disorder needs to be taken with food, and proper nutrition is critical, so I make a veggie omelet, rinse a cup of fresh berries, and sit down at the table with todayâs pillbox.Everything tastes horrible. I might as well be chewing cardboard. After choking down the meal, I take my first of two daily medications for bipolar disorder, along with half my daily dose of fish oil. I wash it all down with water and decaf coffee. I had to give up caffeine years ago because bipolar and caffeine donât do well together.9 a.m. I sit down at my desk. I write and write, hyper-focused on my latest project. The ideas are plenty, but next week Iâll read it back and hate every word, Iâm sure. 12 p.m. Itâs lunchtime. Iâm still not hungry. Iâm craving the carbs of spaghetti, but I donât keep food like this in the house. I force vegetable soup and a salad down my throat because I know I need to eat. Eating is a chore. It tastes like nothing. I swallow half my daily dose of multivitamin, a biotin capsule for my thinning hair, and vitamin E because my last blood test showed a slight deficiency. More pills. 12:30 p.m. OK, itâs back to work. I switch gears and start editing photos from my last photo shoot. Dozens of ideas rush through my mind. I need to make changes to my website. I feel an intense need to do them all right now. 6 p.m. My husband comes home from work. Iâm still working. He comes in to chat, and I get upset at the interruption. He asks if Iâd gotten any sleep. My husband knows I was tossing and turning all night, and it scared him. He makes dinner: chicken and wild rice with vegetables. On a normal day, this would be delicious. Today, it turns to dry, flavorless dust in my mouth. I take the second of two daily doses of medication for bipolar disorder, fish oil, and multivitamin.Over dinner, he notices how fast Iâm talking and how quickly my mind is working.He knows what to do. He packs my bags and takes me into the car so he can drive me to the emergency room. Iâm terrified and donât want to go. Iâm paranoid, convinced weâll get in an accident on the way.The psychiatric ward is across town. A few years ago, their emergency room closed due to budget cuts. So now we have to go through the ER at a city hospital.Iâm singing loudly behind my curtain. The nurse tries to take my vitals, but Iâm too scared to let her. They call the psych ward, secure a bed, and arrange for the ambulance to take me there.10 p.m. Itâs been a long day. Iâm finally at the psych ward. Doctors and nurses in white are milling about all around me. The lights are so bright. Doors open and close, open and close constantly. They give me a snack: peanut butter crackers. More dry, flavorless food. They up my dosage of medication for bipolar disorder and send me to bed. Will I be able to sleep at all?11:30 p.m. I didnât sleep last night, but Iâm still wide awake.I approach the nursesâ station and ask for a sleeping pill.1:30 a.m. The night nurse has stopped by to check on me every 20 minutes since I crawled into bed. If Iâve slept at all, itâs only been for a few minutes. If I donât get another sleeping pill before 2 a.m., they wonât let me have one later, so I make my way to the nursesâ station.6:30 a.m.The nurse comes in to take my vitals and gives me my morning dose of hypothyroid medication.Was I asleep? Had I slept at all? Soon, theyâll be calling us to breakfast. Theyâll serve a lackluster breakfast sandwich cooked at least 2 hours prior. Iâll go to group therapy, where we might make art. Art has been known to help people with their mental health.Other than that, thereâs nothing to do but watch TV. Itâs so boring.Looking forwardBipolar mania can be a scary thing to experience. However, treatment is available to make symptoms more manageable. Since receiving my diagnosis, Iâve found the right medication and the right dosage so that day-to-day life is stable.I havenât had another one of these episodes in five years. I go to bed early and pay close attention to my sleep patterns. I plan healthy meals for the week and never miss a dose of medication. Bipolar disorder is a fairly common condition, so if you or a loved one live with a mental illness, take comfort that youâre not alone. Bipolar disorder can affect people from all walks of life.Itâs true that episodes of mania or depression can recur after years of remission, and medication may need to be adjusted in a doctor or hospital setting. But with proper treatment and a positive outlook, itâs possible to lead a balanced, productive life. Iâm doing it. I know you can, too.Share on PinterestMara Robinson is a freelance marketing communications specialist with more than 15 years of experience. Sheâs created many forms of communications for a wide variety of clients, including feature articles, product descriptions, ad copy, sales materials, packaging, press kits, newsletters, and more. Sheâs also an avid photographer and music lover who can frequently be found photographing rock concerts at MaraRobinson.com.","title":"This Is What It Feels Like to Have a Bipolar Manic Episode","url":"https://www.healthline.com/health/what-a-bipolar-manic-episode-feels-like","id":632},{"content_hash":"7657836f8c2fec3ca982e720d0de21887efde5d2a4ce4e05739fce2af95ce815","domain":"www.lemonde.fr","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:48.377450+00:00","final_url":"https://www.lemonde.fr/archives/article/1951/11/08/terreur-rouge-a-changhai_2072832_1819218.html","language":"","text":"Hong-Kong, ... novembre. - Ceci se passe à Changhaï, dans la nuit du 27 avril dernier (1). A l'heure où la ville s'est endormie, vers minuit, des camions et des voitures de police, en nombre impressionnant et chargés d'hommes armés, se répandent à travers les grandes avenues des anciennes concessions, les rues, les ruelles obscures des quartiers chinois. Ici et là les autos s'arrêtent. Des policiers et des soldats sautent sur le pavé et cognent à cette porte, à cette autre. Appels, cris dans le parler rauque de Changhaï, volets qui s'entr'ouvrent avec bruit, tumulte dans la maison envahie par la police. Cela ne traîne guère: un Chinois ou plusieurs, jetés dehors, se voient hissés à bord du camion, qui démarre aussitôt pour aller chercher un peu plus loin ses prochaines victimes. C'est une rafle monstre de contre-révolutionnaires, la plus importante jusqu'à ce jour. Rafle ? Le mot n'est sans doute pas exact. Les agents de la sécurité publique n'arrêtent pas au hasard : ils savent où ils vont et qui ils cherchent; ils ont des listes et viennent cueillir leurs proies une à une, aux logis dont ils ont les adresses. Combien d'arrestations cette nuit-là ? Le chiffre ne sera pas publié. Les estimations les plus optimistes disent au moins trois mille. Et le chiffre de dix mille, avancé par beaucoup, ne parait pas invraisemblable. Le lendemain, à travers la ville, chaque Chinois rapporte un ou plusieurs cas qu'il connaît personnellement : un voisin de rue, un ami, un parent, se trouve de la \" charrette \". Beaucoup de résidants français citent les noms des disparus qu'ils ont connus. Un prêtre français est au nombre de ceux-ci. Les autorités ne font d'ailleurs aucun effort pour dissimuler l'opération, au contraire. Si elle s'est déroulée la nuit c'était sans doute pour plus de commodité et parce que les gens étaient chez eux. Les jours suivants c'est en plein midi que tout le monde pourra voir passer en ville des camions, souvent peints en rouge, qui emportent on ne sait où leur charretée d'ennemis du peuple. Les malheureux sont ficelés et entourés par un peloton de soldats en uniforme de Coton vert. Les fusils de ces gardes sont tournés vers les passants. Comme si l'on manquait de véhicules à cause du nombre de condamnés a transporter, des voitures-ambulances servent à la sinistre besogne. Une escorte armée en jeep ouvre la route en faisant retentir une sirène au cri aigu. Il vous reste 78.42% de cet article à lire. La suite est réservée aux abonnés.","title":"TERREUR ROUGE A CHANGHAI","url":"https://www.lemonde.fr/archives/article/1951/11/08/terreur-rouge-a-changhai_2072832_1819218.html","id":633},{"content_hash":"1ffd5b692d9000c5a8f713dfcd174ddd1a92304491cf6a343f0726f514b2bab4","domain":"www.theconversation.com","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:48.305402+00:00","final_url":"https://theconversation.com/education-before-marriage-the-latest-on-generational-differences-13407","language":"","text":"Education before marriage: the latest on generational differences Published: April 10, 2013 2:58am EDT https://theconversation.com/education-before-marriage-the-latest-on-generational-differences-13407 https://theconversation.com/education-before-marriage-the-latest-on-generational-differences-13407 Link copied Share article Share article Copy link Email Bluesky Facebook WhatsApp Messenger LinkedIn X (Twitter) Print article How much can a society change in one generation? The latest Australian Social Trends report, released today by the Australian Bureau of Statistics, compares data from the 2011 Census and the 1976 Census - proving just how different today’s young adults (aged 18-34) are from the previous generation. The researchers found a particularly large decrease in the number of young adults getting married. In 1976, 67% of 24-year-olds had been married, compared with just 14% of 24-year-olds in 2011. Similarly striking was the increase in educated young adults: in 2011, nearly twice the number of young adults were attending an educational institution compared with 1976. This change also saw a shift from more young men than young women in higher education in 1976, to the opposite in 2011, when more young women were attending an educational institution than young men. The analysis also found that part-time work was much more common in 2011 than in 1976. Contrastingly, young adults are also tending to leave the family nest later in life. In 2011, 29% of young adults lived with their parents, compared to only 21% in 1976. Read more at Australian Bureau of Statistics Source Australian Bureau of Statistics Tags Education, Marriage, Family, Demographics","title":"Education before marriage: the latest on generational differences","url":"https://theconversation.com/education-before-marriage-the-latest-on-generational-differences-13407","id":634},{"content_hash":"4634ba019c27bca1f6aa0948d26f1408b400d8a64124bd735bc6fadf9d360d24","domain":"youverify.co","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:48.192875+00:00","final_url":"https://youverify.co/en/blogs/how-to-get-a-proof-of-address","language":"","text":"How To Get A Proof of AddressByLola, Edited by Emmanuel AgwuMarch 17, 2023•5mins ReadWhat is Proof Of Address?Why A Proof Of Address Is Necessary For Businesses?Achieving Know Your Customer (KYC) Address Verification with YouverifyShare this postProof of address might sound somewhat familiar already, especially in association with financial institutions such as banks, when opening a new market. The proof of address is a requisite part of the KYC (Know your customer) process. KYC is a regulatory requirement that financial institutions and other businesses must comply with to prevent money laundering, fraud, and other illicit activities. What is Proof Of Address? The term “proof of address” is somewhat explanatory. It is evident that the stated address of an individual is real. It verifies the address of an individual. Proof of address documents are usually required in KYC processes. These include utility bills, bank statements, government-issued documents, and letters from recognized entities. Proof of address is a document or set of documents that demonstrates an individual's current residential address. It is used to confirm the individual's identity and verify that they live at their provided address. It is important to know that the documents must be recent and have a current address on them. Some businesses may require specific types of proof of address documents, depending on their internal policies and regulatory requirements. For example, a bank may require a recent utility bill or bank statement as proof of address when opening a new account. Proof of residency is used in conjunction with other forms of identification that connote the KYC process, like a passport or a driver's license. The documents, together, confirm the identity of their customers and comply with regulatory requirements. Why A Proof Of Address Is Necessary For Businesses? Proof of address or proof of residency is an important component of KYC, just like every other component. KYC, of course, refers to knowing your customer, which is a verification process required of banks and other regulated entities. The proof of address documents is used to verify the identity and addresses of customers and assess the potential risks associated with them. This is done as a precaution for illicit activities like money laundering. Financial institutions and other regulated entities are required to perform ongoing monitoring of their customers to ensure that they remain in compliance with laws and regulations. KYC involves collecting and verifying personal information about a customer, such as their name, address, date of birth, and identification documents like passport or driver's license. However, there are automated ways to do that now. In South America, KYC regulations and practices can vary from country to country. However, many countries in the region have implemented similar KYC standards to those in the USA, particularly in the banking and financial sectors. For example, in Brazil, financial institutions are required to verify the identity of their customers through a variety of methods, such as electronic verification, physical documents, or in-person interviews. Similarly, in Argentina, financial institutions are required to verify the identity of their customers using a variety of methods, such as electronic verification, physical documents, or in-person interviews. Proof of address is required by businesses to verify the identity and address of their customers, clients, or suppliers. This is an important security measure that helps prevent fraud and ensures that the business is dealing with legitimate individuals or entities. This is one of the reasons why proof of residency will always be necessary for businesses. Let's explore a number of reasons why proof of address is necessary for a business : a. Compliance with regulations: Many businesses are required by law to verify the identity and address of their customers or clients to comply with anti-money laundering (AML) and know-your-customer (KYC) regulations. b. Prevention of fraud: Requiring a proof of address helps prevent fraud by ensuring that the business is dealing with a real person or entity and not a fictitious one. c. Contact information: Businesses need to have accurate contact information for their customers, clients, or suppliers to ensure that they can communicate with them when necessary. d. Credit checks: Some businesses may need to perform credit checks or other background checks on their customers, clients, or suppliers to assess their financial risk. ProofProof of address can help confirm their identity and assess their creditworthiness. e. Delivery and shipment: Some businesses may require proof of address to ensure that their products or services are delivered to the correct address. This is especially important for online businesses that ship products to customers. f. Tax purposes: For businesses that deal with vendors or clients overseas, proof of address may be necessary for tax purposes. This helps the business to ensure that they are complying with international tax laws and regulations. g. Insurance requirements: Some insurance policies may require proof of address to determine coverage eligibility or to process claims. This is particularly true for home insurance policies, where the address of the insured property is a crucial piece of information. h. Rental agreements: Landlords and leases may require proof of address from prospective tenants to verify their identity and assess their ability to pay rent. This helps to protect the landlord from potential rental scams or non-payment of rent. How To Get A Proof of Address Many individuals wonder how to get proof of address or how to get proof of residency when preparing for compliance processes. There are several alternatives that businesses can use to obtain proof of address documents from customers for KYC purposes. Here is what counts as proof of residency to meet regulatory obligations. 1. Utility Bills A common option when asked how to get proof of address, as it directly shows residency. Request the customer to provide a recent utility bill in their name, such as a water, electricity, or gas bill. This should have the customer's name and address mentioned on it. 2. Bank Statements Widely accepted; many ask, “is a bank statement proof of address?” Yes, it often is, provided it is recent. Request the customer to provide a recent bank statement that shows their current address. The statement should not be more than three months old. 3. A Government-Issued ID Some IDs also double as proof of residency when they contain the holder’s address. Government-issued IDs like passports, driving licenses, etc., also contain the address of the holder. 4. Rental Agreement Request the customer to provide a copy of their rental agreement or lease. This should have the customer's name and address mentioned on it. 5. Postal Mail Request the customer to provide a recent letter or package they received at their address. 6. Digital Verification With the advent of technology, digital verification services are also available in the market, which helps to validate the customers' addresses by cross-verifying their provided data with their digital footprint. 7. Credit Report If the customer has a good credit history, they may have a credit report that includes their current address. 8. Tax Documents Request the customer to provide a recent tax document, such as a tax return or assessment notice. This should have the customer's name and address mentioned on it. 9. Employer Verification If the customer is employed, their employer may be able to provide a letter verifying their address. 10. Online Verification Some companies may use online address verification services that check the customer's address against a database of addresses or use geolocation to verify their location. 11. Face-to-Face Verification Businesses may also choose to verify the customer's address in person by conducting a face-to-face meeting or inspection.Each of these provides businesses with options on how to get proof of address securely while ensuring compliance. Achieving Know Your Customer (KYC) Address Verification with Youverify Youverify has a range of software services that provide identity verification services, including address verification. The flagship product of Youverify, YV OS, is made to assist companies that handle sensitive data or must adhere to rules. Included in them are KYC and AML, two crucial compliances that could result in severe penalties from regulatory authorities. The YV OS, most notably, reduces the time and labour costs associated with performing physical identification verification yourself, saving your firm money. Accuracy is also guaranteed due to our elaborate agent network that manually verifies the provided address. See how 100+ leading companies use Youverify for KYC and AML screening of customers for compliance and real-time risk detection. book a demo today. Related ArticlesView All PostsAddress VerificationLola, Edited by Emmanuel Agwu•May 3, 2023What is Address Verification Service (AVS)?Read MoreAddress VerificationEmmanuel Agwu•June 15, 2023Digital Address VerificationRead MoreAddress VerificationEmmanuel Agwu•August 1, 2022REVEALED: Financial Institutions Need To Conduct Physical Address Verification Or Face Up To N20 Million Fine - Here's WhyRead More","title":"How To Get A Proof of Address","url":"https://youverify.co/en/blogs/how-to-get-a-proof-of-address","id":635},{"content_hash":"0b7e51829bce40478cfedce1a1587ade6ddd706441ecb6b9bbb1ac2110f47832","domain":"docs.djangoproject.com","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:47.912227+00:00","final_url":"https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/dev/ref/contrib/postgres/forms/","language":"","text":"PostgreSQL specific form fields and widgets¶ All of these fields and widgets are available from the django.contrib.postgres.forms module. Fields¶ SimpleArrayField¶ class SimpleArrayField(base_field, delimiter=',', max_length=None, min_length=None)¶ A field which maps to an array. It is represented by an HTML <input>. base_field¶ This is a required argument. It specifies the underlying form field for the array. This is not used to render any HTML, but it is used to process the submitted data and validate it. For example: >>> from django import forms >>> from django.contrib.postgres.forms import SimpleArrayField >>> class NumberListForm(forms.Form): ... numbers = SimpleArrayField(forms.IntegerField()) ... >>> form = NumberListForm({\"numbers\": \"1,2,3\"}) >>> form.is_valid() True >>> form.cleaned_data {'numbers': [1, 2, 3]} >>> form = NumberListForm({\"numbers\": \"1,2,a\"}) >>> form.is_valid() False delimiter¶ This is an optional argument which defaults to a comma: ,. This value is used to split the submitted data. It allows you to chain SimpleArrayField for multidimensional data: >>> from django import forms >>> from django.contrib.postgres.forms import SimpleArrayField >>> class GridForm(forms.Form): ... places = SimpleArrayField(SimpleArrayField(IntegerField()), delimiter=\"|\") ... >>> form = GridForm({\"places\": \"1,2|2,1|4,3\"}) >>> form.is_valid() True >>> form.cleaned_data {'places': [[1, 2], [2, 1], [4, 3]]} Note The field does not support escaping of the delimiter, so be careful in cases where the delimiter is a valid character in the underlying field. The delimiter does not need to be only one character. max_length¶ This is an optional argument which validates that the array does not exceed the stated length. min_length¶ This is an optional argument which validates that the array reaches at least the stated length. User friendly forms SimpleArrayField is not particularly user friendly in most cases, however it is a useful way to format data from a client-side widget for submission to the server. SplitArrayField¶ class SplitArrayField(base_field, size, remove_trailing_nulls=False)¶ This field handles arrays by reproducing the underlying field a fixed number of times. base_field¶ This is a required argument. It specifies the form field to be repeated. size¶ This is the fixed number of times the underlying field will be used. remove_trailing_nulls¶ By default, this is set to False. When False, each value from the repeated fields is stored. When set to True, any trailing values which are blank will be stripped from the result. If the underlying field has required=True, but remove_trailing_nulls is True, then null values are only allowed at the end, and will be stripped. Some examples: SplitArrayField(IntegerField(required=True), size=3, remove_trailing_nulls=False) [\"1\", \"2\", \"3\"] # -> [1, 2, 3] [\"1\", \"2\", \"\"] # -> ValidationError - third entry required. [\"1\", \"\", \"3\"] # -> ValidationError - second entry required. [\"\", \"2\", \"\"] # -> ValidationError - first and third entries required. SplitArrayField(IntegerField(required=False), size=3, remove_trailing_nulls=False) [\"1\", \"2\", \"3\"] # -> [1, 2, 3] [\"1\", \"2\", \"\"] # -> [1, 2, None] [\"1\", \"\", \"3\"] # -> [1, None, 3] [\"\", \"2\", \"\"] # -> [None, 2, None] SplitArrayField(IntegerField(required=True), size=3, remove_trailing_nulls=True) [\"1\", \"2\", \"3\"] # -> [1, 2, 3] [\"1\", \"2\", \"\"] # -> [1, 2] [\"1\", \"\", \"3\"] # -> ValidationError - second entry required. [\"\", \"2\", \"\"] # -> ValidationError - first entry required. SplitArrayField(IntegerField(required=False), size=3, remove_trailing_nulls=True) [\"1\", \"2\", \"3\"] # -> [1, 2, 3] [\"1\", \"2\", \"\"] # -> [1, 2] [\"1\", \"\", \"3\"] # -> [1, None, 3] [\"\", \"2\", \"\"] # -> [None, 2] HStoreField¶ class HStoreField¶ A field which accepts JSON encoded data for an HStoreField. It casts all values (except nulls) to strings. It is represented by an HTML <textarea>. User friendly forms HStoreField is not particularly user friendly in most cases, however it is a useful way to format data from a client-side widget for submission to the server. Note On occasions it may be useful to require or restrict the keys which are valid for a given field. This can be done using the KeysValidator. Range Fields¶ This group of fields all share similar functionality for accepting range data. They are based on MultiValueField. They treat one omitted value as an unbounded range. They also validate that the lower bound is not greater than the upper bound. All of these fields use RangeWidget. IntegerRangeField¶ class IntegerRangeField¶ Based on IntegerField and translates its input into django.db.backends.postgresql.psycopg_any.NumericRange. Default for IntegerRangeField and BigIntegerRangeField. DecimalRangeField¶ class DecimalRangeField¶ Based on DecimalField and translates its input into django.db.backends.postgresql.psycopg_any.NumericRange. Default for DecimalRangeField. DateTimeRangeField¶ class DateTimeRangeField¶ Based on DateTimeField and translates its input into django.db.backends.postgresql.psycopg_any.DateTimeTZRange. Default for DateTimeRangeField. DateRangeField¶ class DateRangeField¶ Based on DateField and translates its input into django.db.backends.postgresql.psycopg_any.DateRange. Default for DateRangeField. Widgets¶ RangeWidget¶ class RangeWidget(base_widget, attrs=None)¶ Widget used by all of the range fields. Based on MultiWidget. RangeWidget has one required argument: base_widget¶ A RangeWidget comprises a 2-tuple of base_widget. decompress(value)¶ Takes a single “compressed” value of a field, for example a DateRangeField, and returns a tuple representing a lower and upper bound.","title":"PostgreSQL specific form fields and widgets¶","url":"https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/dev/ref/contrib/postgres/forms/","id":636},{"content_hash":"6be5f941397172001f90591bd218e12213703f8272218904063569d35de24c33","domain":"www.theguardian.com","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:47.677843+00:00","final_url":"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/11/republican-senator-aide-nazi-ss-picture","language":"","text":"Republican senator fires aide who used Nazi soldiers as Facebook profile pictureWashington Post report also reveals Jon Husted staffer Stephen Woytek created pro-Rhodesia playlist on Spotify Robert Tait in WashingtonFri 11 Sep 2026 19.21 EDTLast modified on Fri 11 Sep 2026 19.52 EDTSharePrefer the Guardian on GoogleThe Republican senator for Ohio, Jon Husted, has fired an aide who was discovered to have used a photo of Nazi SS soldiers as his Facebook profile photo.Stephen Woytek was appointed as Husted’s political director last month in the senator’s knife-edge re-election contest against former Democrat senator Sherrod Brown. According to the Washington Post, Husted had decided to “part ways” with Woytek, 25, after learning that his Facebook profile showed he followed a military re-enactment group called LAH Living History Unit, which portrays the 1st SS Panzer division.The group’s website says its members dress up as the Leibstandarte, a Waffen-SS armored division that began as Adolf Hitler’s bodyguards. LAH says the Leibstandarte “came to symbolize the highest dedication to duty and individual as well as collective loyalty”. The group claims to be “non-political” and insists is disavows “political and religious persecution” that happened the second world war.A Spotify playlist recently created by an account bearing Woytek’s name hailed the former racist white-minority regime of Rhodesia, now Zimbabwe, seen as a symbol of white supremacy by some racist groups.In a statement, a spokesperson for Husted said the campaign had ended its relationship with Woytek.“While he denies negative intent, his social media activity displays a complete lack of judgement and disregard for its impact on others,” the spokesperson said. “Senator Husted demands better of those who represent him. Upon learning about the social media posts today, Senator Husted made the immediate decision to part ways.”The campaign did not respond to the Post’s questions about whether and how Woytek’s social media activity had been vetted before his appointment, the newspaper reported.Woytek’s departure follows a series of damaging episodes in which young Republicans groups have been discovered expressing pro-Nazi sympathies in group chats and internet forums. And in Georgia, Republican congressman Mike Collins’s campaign for Senate has been shaken by controversies involving his staff’s online activity. This summer, Collins replaced top aide, Kip Talley, after Slate revealed he had been part of a group chat with white supremacists.Woytek, who serves in the national guard and was a graduate of the Citadel, a military academy based in Charleston, South Carolina, issued a statement of regret, saying he wished he had “exercised better judgment when posting about my activities online”.“I want to be unequivocal: I reject the racist and antisemitic ideology the SS and Nazi Germany represented. I believe it is important to educate our younger generations, which is why I participate in historical reenactments,” he said.LAH shared a photo on a Flickr account that showed Woytek in 2018 – when he was 16 – wearing an SS uniform and marching in an area adorned with Nazi flags. Woytek follows several suppliers of SS uniforms on his Facebook page.On a Quora account bearing his name, Woytek also answered a question on whether anything good had occurred under Hitler, writing in 2017 “that Hitler started an anti-smoking campaign”.More recently, he created a public playlist of pro-Rhodesia songs on Spotify called “Tales from Rhodesia”, which is captioned: “Homesick for a place that no longer exists.” One of the songs uses a slur to refer to African troops.The former British colony’s white minority government fought a long war against guerrilla groups after issuing a unilateral declaration of independence in 1965. The country was officially recognized as Zimbabwe under black majority rule in 1980, a year after the minority government accepted its rule was unsustainable and entered peace negotiations.Rhodesia has been used by white supremacists as a symbol of the supposed superiority of white rule.Explore more on these topicsRepublicansUS politicsOhionewsShareReuse this content","title":"Republican senator fires aide who used Nazi soldiers as Facebook profile picture","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/11/republican-senator-aide-nazi-ss-picture","id":637},{"content_hash":"1d4fa59650e2eb2c33e921df65bd488b58646b9b362be52cc6b1cb4c4a9cbc48","domain":"timesofindia.indiatimes.com","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:47.629399+00:00","final_url":"https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/etimes/trending/its-a-mahindra-one-its-ours-anand-mahindra-spots-rickshaw-in-london-social-media-reacts-to-unusual-sight/articleshow/134791138.cms","language":"","text":"‘It’s a Mahindra one, it’s ours’: Anand Mahindra spots rickshaw in London, social media reacts to unusual sight | - The Times of IndiaSign InTOITOIhomelifestylerelationshiptrendingHealth+styleparentingsoul searchbeautybooksrecipesfood newstravelhome & gardeneventsspotlightNewsetimeslifestyletrending‘It’s a Mahindra one, it’s ours’: Anand Mahindra spots rickshaw in London, social media reacts to unusual sightTrendingBaby NamesVibhor JainChildren PsychologyIndiGo Flight Lightning StrikeLeo Tolstoy QuoteYellow Pillow StainsBen AffleckKarl DeisserothRam VilasSharad Navratri 2026Baby NamesVibhor JainChildren PsychologyIndiGo Flight Lightning StrikeLeo Tolstoy QuoteYellow Pillow StainsBen AffleckKarl DeisserothRam VilasSharad Navratri 2026Baby NamesVibhor JainChildren PsychologyIndiGo Flight Lightning StrikeLeo Tolstoy QuoteYellow Pillow StainsBen AffleckKarl DeisserothRam VilasSharad Navratri 2026‘It’s a Mahindra one, it’s ours’: Anand Mahindra spots rickshaw in London, social media reacts to unusual sightTOI Trending Desk / etimes.in / Oct 08, 2026, 20:30 ISTSaveCommentsShareAa+Text SizeSmallMediumLargePrint Anand Mahindra spots rickshaw in London, social media reacts to unusual sight A rickshaw on a London road is the kind of sight that can make people look twice. A recent social media post featuring one has caught attention for bringing together two very different road scenes, with users also joining the conversation with their own reactions and observations.The post was shared by Anand Mahindra, who appeared to take particular interest in the vehicle after spotting it in London. The discussion that followed ranged from Indian pride to jokes about how unusual the sight was on British roads.What the video showsThe nearly 24-second clip shows a black Mahindra auto-rickshaw travelling through central London. The driver is wearing sunglasses. The footage was recorded from the roadside as the three-wheeler moved through traffic.Pedestrians and black cabs are visible in the surrounding scene, along with London’s familiar city architecture.Anand Mahindra’s captionMahindra shared the video on October 5 along with a Gujarati caption.He wrote, “A rickshaw has come to the UK It’s a Mahindra one, it’s ours.”Users bring up other Mahindra sightingsThe post prompted users to share their own observations about seeing Mahindra vehicles outside India.One user recalled spotting a Mahindra vehicle at Urquhart Castle in Scotland the previous week. They described it as exciting to see Indian brands making their presence felt globally.Social media adds a humorous touchThe unusual setting also led to some playful comments.One user joked that a rickshaw on British roads was “one of the most confident imports since tea”.Another encouraged Mahindra to take a proper spin around London in his own rickshaw.The combination of the London setting, the familiar three-wheeler and the reactions in the comments turned a short video into an interesting social media moment.Disclaimer: The information in this article is based on the social media post and reactions mentioned above. The Times of India has not independently verified the claims made by social media users.Thumb image: XGet the latest movie news, reviews, and celebrity updates. Download the TOI App.End of ArticleFollow Us On Social MediaTop TrendingDonna KelcePatrick Mahomes MotherSam BealAsim MunirUS Iran WarINDIA Bloc ProtestBengaluru CJP ProtestSimone BilesCJP Chappal Protes