il MoviesUpcoming Telugu MoviesUpcoming Malayalam MoviesUpcoming Kannada MoviesFashion TipsTravel NewsEntertainment NewsBollywood NewsTollywood NewsKollywood NewsMollywood NewsFood NewsLatest Hindi MoviesLatest Tamil MoviesParenting TipsHome RemediesWeight LossBeauty TipsParenting TipsHindi VideosHindi Video SongsBhojpuri Music VideosLatest Telugu MoviesBhojpuri Music VideoHindi TV NewsLatest NewsWho is Jaime Chapman’s boyfriend? All about the NRLW star’s rugby league romance'Hanuman Ansh' box office collection day 63: Vishal Chaturvedi's film earns Rs 75 lakhs; worldwide gross reaches Rs 427.43 cr; India net total stands at Rs 327.98 crore'Sigma' box office collection day 7: Jason Sanjay's film earns Rs 8.27 cr India net; Soori's film reaches Rs 100.58 cr'Drishyam 3: The Conclusion' box office collection day 7: Ajay Devgn-Tabu film earns Rs 13 crore; worldwide gross headed for Rs 400 crore markSteep margins allow room for malpractice: Pharmaceuticals secretaryCapricorn Shani Horoscope Today, 9 October 2026: Saturn Says Send the Reply You Keep Drafting; Uttara Phalguni Moon Points to Good Advice'The Paradise' box office collection day 15 vs 'Don't Trouble The Trouble' day 7: Nani's film earns Rs 89 lakhs; worldwide gross reaches Rs 171.32 cr; Fahadh Faasil starrer collects Rs 4.41 cr India netKPSC scam candidates taken to resorts, provided with Q&A: EDWhat happened in viral video of Dodgers fan refusing ball to child? Incident explainedCorey Pavin reveals wife Lisa’s cancer ‘never went away completely’ months after her final chemotherapy sessionDaily Career Horoscope, October 09, 2026: Success, challenges, and breakthroughs; Know about your careerMalhar Patekar on father Nana Patekar's legacy: 'His achievements have made him immortal'Sagittarius Shani Horoscope Today, 9 October 2026: Saturn Says Home First, Career Second; Uttara Phalguni Moon Puts Your Work on DisplayFrance turned 127 hectares of abandoned gravel pits into Europe’s largest floating solar farm; 135,000 panels now generate power for 37,000 peopleFlydubai cockpit attack: Israel to honour Indian pilot Smit Machchhar with top civilian bravery awardScorpio Shani Horoscope Today, 9 October 2026: Saturn Says Earn the Introduction Before You Use It; Uttara Phalguni Moon Brings Helpful ContactsJharkhand should 'revisit' DGP appointment rules, says Supreme CourtIPS quota in CAPF posts comes into forceCopyright © 2026 Bennett, Coleman & Co. Ltd. All rights reserved. For reprint rights: Times Syndication ServiceFollow us on","title":"‘It’s a Mahindra one, it’s ours’: Anand Mahindra spots rickshaw in London, social media reacts to unusual sight","url":"https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/etimes/trending/its-a-mahindra-one-its-ours-anand-mahindra-spots-rickshaw-in-london-social-media-reacts-to-unusual-sight/articleshow/134791138.cms","id":638},{"content_hash":"7580c2a9053d4529c013c8a64acda5fc552d6fb4c1152cd30e64f312dba1dc7b","domain":"www.abc.net.au","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:47.580530+00:00","final_url":"https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-10-07/nasa-rover-takes-striking-image-of-dawn-s-early-light-on-mars/107240852","language":"","text":"NASA rover takes striking image of dawn's early light on MarsTopic:SpacePosted Wed 7 Oct 2026 at 10:05pmWed 7 Oct 2026 at 10:05pmWed 7 Oct 2026 at 10:05pm, updated Wed 7 Oct 2026 at 10:49pmWed 7 Oct 2026 at 10:49pmWed 7 Oct 2026 at 10:49pmA view of the Martian surface showing wind-carved crags called yardangs on Mount Sharp. (NASA: JPL-Caltech/MSSS)In short:A new image from Mars has been released, showing a dawn over wind-carved cliffs.The scene was snapped by NASA's Curiosity rover at 8:30 am local Mars time.What's next?Scientists hope Curiosity will reach the base of the crags, known as yardangs, sometime in 2027.abc.net.au/news/nasa-rover-takes-striking-image-of-dawn-s-early-light-on-mars/107240852Link copiedShareShare articleNASA has released a striking image of dawn on the Martian surface taken by its Curiosity rover, showing sunlight bathing jagged crags formed billions of years ago.Curiosity, which is about the size of a Mini Cooper, landed in 2012 in Gale Crater near the Martian equator, and since 2014 has been climbing Mount Sharp, a 5-kilometre-tall mountain rising from the crater floor.Panoramic Martian viewsThe Mars Perseverance rover provides a panoramic look at the Jezero Crater site on the Red Planet.The image was taken by the six-wheeled rover's Mastcam camera about an hour after the sun rose above a landscape featuring wind-carved cliffs in the distance, in August.\"The bright craggy peaks in the distance are a rock layer that is quite different in appearance from all the layers the rover has driven through so far,\" said planetary scientist Ashwin Vasavada of NASA's Jet Propulsion Laboratory in California.\"We think it once was wind-blown sediment, maybe sand or maybe even ash that blew into the crater from nearby volcanic activity.\"After the sediment hardened into rock, eons of wind carved up the rock layer into ridges called yardangs,\" the Curiosity project scientist said.The yardang layer most likely formed about 3 billion years ago, around the same time as the rest of the mountain, according to Dr Vasavada.This layer spans about 16 kilometres across the north-western reaches of Mount Sharp.\"However, the yardang layer doesn't appear to be part of the continuous stack of layers that make up the layer-cake of Mount Sharp. It was added on a little later. It's above what geologists call an unconformity: a gap in time where previous layers eroded down before new layers were deposited on top,\" Dr Vasavada said.'You can almost feel the silence'The rover on its gradual ascent up the mountain has gained upwards of 1km in elevation, the most ever climbed on Mars, according to NASA.Curiosity's five yearsNASA's Curiosity rover has already taught us a lot in the past five years, but NASA scientists think there is still much more to come.Mount Sharp is built of layers, each recording a period of the planet's geological past. In studying these layers, scientists have learned more about bodies of water — lakes and streams — that long ago covered this region, at a time when Mars was wetter and warmer than the cold and desolate place it is today.Dr Vasavada said NASA hoped Curiosity would reach the yardang layer in 2027 or 2028, at which time it would use its instruments to scrutinise the geology there.Curiosity has been studying the geology and climate of Mars and examining whether it once bore conditions conducive to harbouring microbial life.It is one of two NASA rovers operating on Mars.The Perseverance rover is currently traversing the margins of Jezero Crater in the northern hemisphere.Curiosity's new image of Martian dawn is certainly otherworldly.\"This scene has a wildness that reminds me of a road trip through Monument Valley, Arizona,\" Dr Vasavada said.\"You can almost feel the silence and the endless open space under the sky. But as familiar as that sounds, the sky is orange and the sunrise has shades of blue. It's like Earth, but it's definitely Mars.\"ReutersShare optionsCopy linkFacebookX (formerly Twitter)See more ABC coverage in your search resultsMake ABC a preferred source in GooglePromotionTop StoriesVictorian language charity with $16m kitty has links to white nationalistsTopic:ExtremismFamilies of men killed on Mexico surf trip call for maximum sentencesTopic:CrimeFormer Bachelor Sam Wood to fight for bail application on domestic violence chargesTopic:Law, Crime and JusticeATO delays credit card ban as government backs down after business backlashTopic:Federal GovernmentHow the card surcharge ban could change our relationship with cashTopic:ExplainerRelated storiesWhere our Curiosity took us — five years on MarsTopic:Space ExplorationStill life on Mars: Curiosity rover snaps a selfie on the dusty Red PlanetTopic:Space ExplorationRelated topicsSpaceUnited StatesTop StoriesVictorian language charity with $16m kitty has links to white nationalistsTopic:ExtremismFamilies of men killed on Mexico surf trip call for maximum sentencesTopic:CrimeFormer Bachelor Sam Wood to fight for bail application on domestic violence chargesTopic:Law, Crime and JusticeATO delays credit card ban as government backs down after business backlashTopic:Federal GovernmentHow the card surcharge ban could change our relationship with cashTopic:ExplainerJust InFamilies of men killed on Mexico surf trip call for maximum sentencesTopic:CrimeFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:05pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:05pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:05pmAmbulance ramping data casts doubt over LNP promise to reduce wait timesTopic:Ambulance ServiceFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:05pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:05pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:05pmHow the card surcharge ban could change our relationship with cashTopic:ExplainerFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:01pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:01pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:01pmThe fruit and vegetables to look out for this monthTopic:Food and DrinkFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:04pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:04pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:04pmMore Just InBack to top","title":"NASA rover takes striking image of dawn's early light on Mars","url":"https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-10-07/nasa-rover-takes-striking-image-of-dawn-s-early-light-on-mars/107240852","id":639},{"content_hash":"ba5c698c30da3c46cf92cb4e9516ac330a7db70342970ad33e043f2e317f3e0a","domain":"healthline.com","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:47.362046+00:00","final_url":"https://www.healthline.com/health/bipolar-disorder/hospitalization","language":"","text":"How does hospitalization fit into your treatment?In most circumstances, a combination of medication, psychotherapy, and lifestyle management can keep bipolar disorder under control. But sometimes, more help is needed and hospitalization may be necessary.Hospitalization is considered an emergency option in bipolar disorder care. It becomes necessary in extreme cases where the disorder is causing someone to be an immediate threat to themselves or others. It may also be used when medications need monitoring or adjustment. How does hospitalization work?Warning signs that hospitalization may be necessary include:exhibitions of extreme or dangerous behaviorextended periods of behavior associated with mood swings which place the individual or others at riskHospitalization can last a few days to a few weeks, or longer, depending on the individualâs circumstances.In his book âThe Bipolar Handbook: Real-Life Questions with Up-to-Date Answers,â Dr. Wes Burgess says that if youâre wondering if hospitalization is necessary, it likely means itâs time to go. He also recommends discussing hospitalization with your healthcare providers and loved ones.If you or a loved one has bipolar disorder, itâs a good idea to research nearby hospitals. Try to gather the following information:the applicable services available at the hospitalsthe contact information for the hospitals and how to get therethe names of the primary care providers for bipolar disorderthe list of treatments you or your loved one is receiving Who can be hospitalized?Hospitalization can be an option for anyone who has bipolar disorder. It depends on the circumstances, but itâs often used for those considering suicide or harming other people, or for those behaviors that can result in serious bodily injury or death of the person or others around them. These thoughts or acts are likely to occur during the depression or mania stages.If you think someone is at immediate risk of self-harm or hurting another person:Call 911 or your local emergency number.Stay with the person until help arrives.Remove any guns, knives, medications, or other things that may cause harm.Listen, but donât judge, argue, threaten, or yell.If you or someone you know is considering suicide, get help from a crisis or suicide prevention hotline. Call or text the 988 Suicide and Crisis Lifeline at 988 or use the chat feature at 988Lifeline.org. What are the side effects?There are no direct side effects to a hospital stay, but there may still be complications. Except for extreme cases, hospitalization must be a voluntary decision. In cases where the person is a clear and immediate danger to themselves or others, involuntary hospitalization can occur.It may be challenging to get someone admitted to a hospital, even if they wish to go. The hospital may keep them for a shorter period than you think is necessary. In either case, if the hospital isnât giving the care thatâs needed, it may be time to try another hospital.A severe bipolar episode can cause extreme or even dangerous behavior. This can include suicide attempts or threats against others. You should take this behavior seriously and take action immediately. If the situation seems out of control or about to get out of control, you may need to call the police for assistance.Many hospitals can handle a wide range of mental health issues. To find out more, check with your primary care provider or the hospitals themselves. Some of these resources may help. TakeawayHospitalization is considered an option for emergency situations in treatment for bipolar disorder. Be sure to create a plan ahead of time in case hospitalization becomes necessary. If a situation becomes unmanageable or dangerous, you may need to contact the police.","title":"Hospitalization for Bipolar Disorder","url":"https://www.healthline.com/health/bipolar-disorder/hospitalization","id":640},{"content_hash":"94cf49203337c28833f02f71cc359c2b0c9397e2014fe9236ceee134cd45d937","domain":"www.lemonde.fr","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:47.204827+00:00","final_url":"https://www.lemonde.fr/archives/article/1951/11/08/la-commission-de-la-production-industrielle-demande-l-abrogation-du-decret-de-hausse_2072864_1819218.html","language":"","text":"Cet article vous est offert Pour lire gratuitement cet article réservé aux abonnés, connectez-vous Se connecter Vous n'êtes pas inscrit sur Le Monde ? Inscrivez-vous gratuitement Archives Archives Archives La commission de la producti