r govt’s motto is Sabka Saath, Sabka Vikas & Sabka Hisaab: CMMisplaced passport & three failed attempts: Agarwal’s fiancée & her partner waited for perfect timing to execute murder at Lohagad FortOn Syama Prasad death anniv, CM trains guns on TMC & Left for erasing his legacyThe Geno Smith assault case takes another twist as detectives are back on it19-year-old students dies as SUV hits himMP cabinet clears Rs 5,960 cr welfare, edu & farm relief packageMIT-WPU develops technology to cut industrial noise by up to 20dBFree temples from govt control, ensure audited trusts: ShankaracharyaTourism secretary, MPSTDC MD depose before judicial panel probing Bargi cruise tragedyBJP forms 106-member MP executive, clears way for first state working committee meetReal estate firm director’s accidental fall at Lohagad Fort turns out to be pre-planned murder, his fiancée & her partner arrested for pushing him off cliffTeacher brandishes rifle on govt school campus; FIR registeredFour men break into temple, loot donation boxesCity’s worst air comes after dark, peaks around midnightInfluencer booked, car seized over stuntsISKCON to Take Over PM POSHAN Midday Meals in Kolkata, Likely to Drop Eggs from Menu in State-Run SchoolsCopyright © 2026 Bennett, Coleman & Co. Ltd. All rights reserved. For reprint rights: Times Syndication ServiceFollow Us On","title":"“I am here”: Cristiano Ronaldo fires back at retirement calls after Portugal vs Uzbekistan as FIFA World Cup 2026 dream continues","url":"https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/sports/football/fifa-world-cup/i-am-here-cristiano-ronaldo-fires-back-at-retirement-calls-after-portugal-vs-uzbekistan-as-fifa-world-cup-2026-dream-continues/articleshow/131949669.cms","id":706},{"content_hash":"717213e8154602e2a920b5a84f19fd5d1d148efdff4753e5b87a9cded8a55029","domain":"reallygoodemails.com","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:35.097031+00:00","final_url":"https://reallygoodemails.com/features","language":"","text":"The features behindreally good emailsBuild better campaigns without duct-taping your workflow together. RGE Studio gives your team one place to design emails, manage brand assets, collaborate on feedback, run QA, and ship campaigns that look polished before they hit the inbox. Here you can explore these email builder features, one by one.Talk to our teamOr start free See RGE Studio in action! START DEMO RGE Studio is an HTML email and landing page builder. All work is organized within workspaces, which serve as central hubs for creating, organizing, and managing designs. Each account includes at least one workspace. Multiple workspaces can be assigned to specific brands, business units, or clients, with separate designs, styles, templates, users, and integrations. Multiple workspaces are available on Business and Enterprise plans. The Projects tab provides access to email and landing page designs with search and management capabilities. Users can create new emails, landing pages, folders, or import designs from other RGE Studio accounts. The platform includes a template catalog with over 1700 email and landing page templates for various occasions, industries, and seasons. The HTML email builder uses drag and drop functionality for adding elements, editing text, and uploading media. Users can modify subject lines, preheaders, and UTMs in the Edit Details page. Additional functions include sending test emails, creating templates, exporting to email service providers, and initiating team review processes. Designs can be organized using folders and located using the search function. The Library tab stores reusable content including templates, saved rows, and uploaded media. Saved rows are reusable content blocks that can be added to multiple designs. Synced rows are saved rows that automatically update across all designs when edited, such as headers or footers used in multiple newsletters. The Settings tab manages workspace-specific configurations. Each workspace has independent settings, styles, templates, user permissions, and connectors. The Styles feature establishes centralized brand guidelines controlling colors, typography, and overall brand appearance. Connectors enable export of designs to email sending platforms, marketing automation systems, and email applications. Designs can be exported to any platform by copying HTML or creating custom connectors. User management includes role assignment and access control. Available roles include admin, manager, editor, and contributor. User roles and permissions control editing access and visibility of sensitive information. This feature is available on Professional, Business, and Enterprise plans. Users can be assigned to individual workspaces or multiple workspaces as needed. Advanced permissions control access to specific editing options, allowing restriction of junior team members while granting full access to senior staff. When creating a new workspace, users can copy settings from existing workspaces including styles, templates, and saved rows, or start from scratch. The builder interface consists of the Stage (canvas for dragging and dropping content blocks and rows) and the Sidebar (controls for adjusting properties like colors, fonts, and padding). Content blocks include text elements (title, paragraph, list) and media elements (images, videos, gifs). Rows define horizontal layout structure and column arrangement. The Settings tab establishes global design elements that rows and content blocks inherit. If Styles are configured in the workspace, settings apply automatically to new designs. Brand Styles and Advanced Style Kit lock fonts, colors, buttons, and spacing so projects start on-brand. Advanced User Permissions control who can edit brand settings, templates, and designs. The approval workflow system includes commenting directly on designs. The Activity Dashboard displays project activity including comments and design review updates. Smart Check identifies issues before export including missing links, missing subject lines, large images, and large HTML files. The AI Assistant adds ALT text to images, identifies typos and grammatical errors, and checks language translations. Once a design is approved through the Approval Flow, it is locked to prevent alterations. Accessibility features include clean, structured HTML generation with semantic heading levels (H1, H2, H3). Smart Check identifies accessibility issues including missing headings, missing alt text, language attribute problems, small text, and color contrast issues. Mobile design mode adjusts text size, element visibility, stacking, and padding for smaller screens. Bulk alt text addition scans all images and allows adding alt text across multiple images simultaneously. Dark mode preview enables design refinement for dark backgrounds. The editor aligns with WCAG 2.2 accessibility principles. Plays nice with your stackEasy to integrate, easy to scaleYou already have a tech stack. RGE Studio fits into it instead of barging in and rearranging the furniture. ‍Connect to the ESPs, CRMs, and platforms your email marketing already runs on, so the emails you build here can go out through the tools your team already trusts.As your team grows, the email builder platform grows with you. Add teammates, manage multiple brands, or connect a new platform without turning your workflow into a group project from hell.Explore integrationsNot a dev? Not a probNo-code email designIf creating an email from start to finish without a developer feels like an impossible dream, think again.RGE Studio is a no-code, drag-and-drop email builder for polished, responsive emails. Start with a template, save reusable rows, quickly comment and approve, and ship a stunning, mobile-ready, fully accessible, fully ESP-optimized email in minutes, not days.And when you need finer control, RGE Studio can also work as an HTML email builder. Browse ready-to-use templatesResponsive email builderMobile-friendly layoutsPeople read email on phones, in bad lighting, while doing twelve other things. So your desktop-only masterpiece? Cute, but risky.RGE Studio builds responsive emails by default, so designs adapt for mobile, tablet, and desktop. Add dynamic content, video, GIFs, animation, and dark mode previews before your subscribers find the weird stuff for you.No more rogue logosConsistent, effective brandingMore people building emails means more chances for the logo to look weird, the blue to drift teal, and the button copy to go rogue.RGE Studio helps prevent that. Import your brand styles, set colors, fonts, logos, and approved components, then sync brand assets across workspaces.Update once. Use everywhere. Collaboration tools for email teamsApprovals without the chaosEmail gets messy fast: Slack threads, mystery spreadsheets, late approvals, and “quick notes” that are never quick.RGE Studio puts collaboration tools inside the work itself. Co-edit in real time, leave comments on specific elements, and route emails through approvals before anything ships.For large teams managing multiple brands, campaigns, and stakeholders, it keeps everyone moving in the same direction. A rare and beautiful thing.AI-assisted asset creationMove faster with first drafts, alt text, copy support, and small in-flow tasks, thanks to RGE Studio’s AI tools. AI Co-PilotTurn ideas into email drafts before the inspiration fades, with AI Co-Pilot.AI assistantDrafts and tightens copy, writes alt text, and handles the small jobs as you build.MCP serverConnect the AI tools and agents you already use straight to RGE Studio, via our MCP.See what it takesWant to see what this looks like when tailored to your team, stack and processes? We are here to help.Chat with SalesOr start freeThe complete RGE Studio packageThe full picture, grouped so you can scan for the features that matter most to you. No treasure map required.FeaturesView allAI FeaturesDesign & contentPersonalization & dynamic contentBrand managementWorkflow & collaborationIntegrations & analyticsAI featuresAI Co-PilotTurn a brief or prompt into a structured first draft you can edit, with every decision staying in your hands.More details AI assistantGenerate and refine copy, write alt text, and handle the small in-the-flow jobs as you build.More details MCP serverConnect your existing AI tools and agents to RGE Studio.More details Design & contentNo-code drag-and-drop builderBuild complete emails by moving blocks around, no code required.More details Responsive editorCreate designs that adapt automatically to mobile, tablet, and desktop.More details TemplatesStart from hundreds of ready-made layouts instead of a blank page.More details Saved & Synced rowsReuse your favorite sections, and update them everywhere at once.More details Version historyRoll back when “let’s try something” goes sideways.Mode details Video, GIFs & animationAdd motion to make inboxes feel less beige.Mode details Dark mode previewSee how your email looks in dark mode before you send.Mode details Smart CheckCatch broken links, missing alt text, and other tiny gremlins before they go out.Mode details HTML import & custom HTMLBring in existing code, or drop into HTML when you want finer control.More details Media library & image hostingStore, organize, and serve your images from one place.More details Personalization & dynamic contentMerge tagsPersonalize with names, locations, and any field from your data.More details Dynamic contentShow different content to different readers in one send.More details Multilingual designsManage multiple language versions without building a folder monster.More details Custom attributesPersonalize around the data that matters to your business.More details Brand managementBrand style kitSet colors and fonts so every email starts on-brand.More details Centralized brand controlKeep approved assets in sync across workspaces.Color palette permissionsEnsure only approved brand colors can be used in your workspace designs.Import style guidelinesBring your existing brand styles straight into RGE Studio.More details Multi-brand managementRun several brands from one account without overlap.Custom domainCustomize domain and subdomain to match your brand.More details Workflow & collaborationWorkspacesKeep teams, clients, and brands organized.More details Real-time co-editingWork on the same email together, live.More details Approval workflowsRoute work through single or multi-step sign-off.More details Roles & permissionsGive people exactly the access they need. More details Design commentingLeave feedback on the exact element in question.More details Comment & review dashboardsDon’t leave coworkers hanging: see all your open threads in one place.More details Integrations & analyticsOne-click export to sending platformsPush finished emails straight to your ESP.More details Custom connectorBuild a connection to whatever you send from.More details ZIP / HTML exportTake your code with you anytime.More details Landing page analyticsTrack performance using your data analytics platform.More detail Two-factor authentication & Okta SSOSingle sign-on and security for bigger teams.More details Get in touchIf RGE Studio looks like the missing piece, let’s talk. Tell us what your team is trying to ship and we will show you the fastest way there.Chat with SalesOr try it freeTake the next step and start building your really good emailsFind inspirationIgnite your creativity with thousands of handpicked real emails.Go Pick a templateProfessionally designed, ready-to-use templates to use today.Browse Explore plansBased on your size and needs, discover the perfect plan for you.This way Talk to usAsk your questions and get all the answers. We're here for you.Book a call","title":"The features behindreally good emails","url":"https://reallygoodemails.com/features","id":707},{"content_hash":"f852af0ff88c68ffdddc70a2883763a9d790c6a304414e7e2708f133b768adca","domain":"www.theconversation.com","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:35.090605+00:00","final_url":"https://theconversation.com/chinas-dust-and-sand-deposits-controlled-by-yellow-river-19194","language":"","text":"China’s dust and sand deposits controlled by Yellow River Published: October 14, 2013 10:48pm EDT https://theconversation.com/chinas-dust-and-sand-deposits-controlled-by-yellow-river-19194 https://theconversation.com/chinas-dust-and-sand-deposits-controlled-by-yellow-river-19194 Link copied Share article Share article Copy link Email Bluesky Facebook WhatsApp Messenger LinkedIn X (Twitter) Print article The movement of desert sands and dust in Northern China is controlled by one of the world’s largest rivers, new research has discovered. Analysis of individual grains of wind-blown dust deposited in the Chinese Loess Plateau showed that the Yellow River, which flows through China, transports large quantities of sediment from Northern Tibet to the Mu Us desert in Mongolia. The findings will assist in climate change modelling, now that it is known that changes in the region’s major river systems will influence the amount of dust that is released into the atmosphere. Northern China holds some of the world’s largest dust deposits, known as loess. The origins of this dust had long been the subject of debate. Read more at Royal Holloway University Source Royal Holloway University Tags Climate change, China, Rivers, Mongolia, dust cloud","title":"China’s dust and sand deposits controlled by Yellow River","url":"https://theconversation.com/chinas-dust-and-sand-deposits-controlled-by-yellow-river-19194","id":708},{"content_hash":"48162be0707ed3c438ea606c379e5a4a8f8d0ed567f18d2c102bedd23e0397f5","domain":"prnigeria.com","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:34.994667+00:00","final_url":"https://prnigeria.com/2026/10/01/navy-rescues-two-kidnap/","language":"","text":"Navy Rescues Two Kidnap Victims, Recovers Stolen Engines in Akwa Ibom By Prnigeria - October 1, 2026 Navy Rescues Two Kidnap Victims, Recovers Stolen Engines in Akwa Ibom The Nigerian Navy has rescued two kidnapped victims and recovered several stolen outboard engines during an operation against sea robbers and kidnappers in Ibeno, Akwa Ibom State. The operation, conducted on September 30, followed intelligence reports that suspected criminals were targeting fishermen, seizing their boats and stealing outboard engines. The Navy said the Nigerian Navy Ship JUBILEE Maritime Quick Response Team, Ibeno, swiftly mobilised to the area after receiving credible information about the criminal activities. During the operation, the naval team encountered two boats suspected to be operated by the criminals. The occupants reportedly fled into adjoining creeks when they sighted the naval personnel, triggering a pursuit. The suspects abandoned one of the boats, which contained several stolen outboard engines and the two kidnapped victims. The naval team rescued the victims and escorted them to safety, while the recovered engines were secured for verification and further action. Read Also: FULL TEXT: President Tinubu’s 66th Independence Day Anniversary Speech Emir of Zazzau Backs NAHCON’s Reform Drive, Calls for Sustained Excellence in Hajj Administration Gombe PDP Suspends Mailantarki, Garry over Alleged Anti-Party Activities after Governorship Primary The Navy said efforts were ongoing to track down and apprehend the fleeing suspects. The Director of Naval Information, Navy Captain Abiodun Folorunsho, said the operation demonstrated the Navy’s commitment to protecting lives and securing legitimate maritime activities across the country’s waterways. He said the service would sustain proactive patrols, search-and-rescue operations and intelligence-driven interventions to prevent criminal activities and respond promptly to distress situations. Folorunsho also stressed the importance of credible intelligence and community support in tackling maritime crimes, urging coastal communities, fishermen and other maritime stakeholders to provide timely information to security agencies. He said the Navy would continue to deploy its ships, bases, surveillance systems and maritime quick response teams to safeguard Nigeria’s maritime domain and deny criminal elements freedom of action. The operation comes amid ongoing efforts by the Navy to protect coastal communities and legitimate maritime activities from sea robbery, kidnapping and the theft of fishing equipment. By PRNigeria VISIT OUR OTHER WEBSITES PRNigeria.com EconomicConfidential.com PRNigeria.com/Hausa/ EmergencyDigest.com PoliticsDigest.ng TechDigest.ng HealthDigest.ng SpokesPersonsdigest.com TeensDigest.ng ArewaAgenda.com Hausa.ArewaAgenda.com YAShuaib.com TAGSNigerian NavyNigerian Navy Ship JUBILEE Maritime Quick Previous articleFULL TEXT: President Tinubu’s 66th Independence Day Anniversary Speech Prnigeria Xing","title":"Navy Rescues Two Kidnap Victims, Recovers Stolen Engines in Akwa Ibom","url":"https://prnigeria.com/2026/10/01/navy-rescues-two-kidnap/","id":709},{"content_hash":"d089aed936378e3e6b286d1a4427b42a898c47244420ff9bff9c5d1ca887fd3b","domain":"ml.com","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:34.754740+00:00","final_url":"https://www.ml.com/articles/art-services.html","language":"","text":"Art Services At Bank of America, we understand the significant role that art plays in both our clients’ lives and within our communities. We offer a range of solutions to address the needs of art collectors, families, artists, foundations, museums, and art businesses throughout the collecting life cycle. Our Approach Our clients collect art because it’s a reflection of life experiences, values and interests, but art can also be a significant asset that should be considered in the context of a broader wealth plan. We help individuals and families borrow against their art collection, design wealth and legacy plans fully integrating their art, and prepare for a sale of art or collectibles at auction or via private sale. For institutions, we provide nonprofit advisory services, Consignment Services, and offer institutional investment management by a fully outsourced Chief Investment Office. Liquidity Unlock the value of your collection by using your art as collateral for a loan to finance business objectives, acquire additional artwork, or to raise funds for a philanthropic endeavor all while keeping your art on your walls. Leverage your art's value Consulting and Consignment Whether you are looking to acquire your first piece of fine art or seeking to refine your existing collection, Art Consulting offers a tailored experience for clients at every stage of their collecting journey built around a multistep process of consultation, strategy guidance, execution support and long term advice. Through Consignment Services, we can help optimize the sale of art and collectibles so our clients receive end to end guidance on the selling process and preferred pricing on seller's commissions and fees with major global auction partners. Planning Our dedicated team of wealth strategists carefully balance considerations around taxes, wealth transfer, and philanthropic goals while planning for the disposition of your art and collectibles. Plan your art legacy with us Philanthropy We offer private philanthropy services for individuals, as well as tailored consulting and investment management solutions for museums and foundations. In addition, collecting institutions can leverage our consignment services for thoughtful deaccession strategies Strategize your philanthropic giving Insights We deliver comprehensive insights and thought-leadership on the art market, collecting trends, industry shifts, tax considerations for collectors, philanthropy and more in reports like our bi-annual Art Market Update. Explore art market insights Access Bank of America Corporation is one of the largest corporate sponsors of arts and culture giving our clients access to major events throughout the art world calendar, including TEFAF New York, where we have been the leading corporate partner since 2017. Discover exclusive art access Support for every stage of the collecting journey Drew Watson is the Art Services Executive at Bank of America. He leads a team of specialists with extensive industry experience from careers in major auction houses, appraisal firms, museums, and galleries. Contact Drew Our commitment to the arts At Bank of America Corporation, we believe that investing in the arts has a positive impact on our lives. We support a wide range of nonprofit organizations with funding and programming to help make the arts more accessible to communities around the world and to preserve works of art and heritage sites for generations to come. Art in our communities® Bank of America shares our art collection with our communities through curated exhibitions that museums and nonprofit galleries may borrow at no cost. William Gottlieb (American, 1917-2006) Dizzy Gillespie, 52nd St., New York, N.Y., c. 1948 Gelatin silver print Bank of America Collection Featured in Jazz Greats: Classic Photographs from the Bank of America Collection Museums on Us® Bank of America offers our cardholders free general admission to cultural institutions across the U.S.– during the first full weekend of every month. Visitors in “The Salon” gallery at the Museum of Fine Arts, Boston. Penny and Jeff Vinik Gallery Photograph © Museum of Fine Arts, Boston Art Conservation Project Art and objects of cultural heritage are vulnerable to the impacts of time and the conservation of these works calls attention to the rich diversity of the human experience. National Gallery of Ireland, Dublin Daniel Maclise (Irish, 1806 –1870) The Marriage of Strongbow and Aoife, 1854 Oil on canvas 124 7/8” x 202 7/8” (317 x 515 cm) Sponsorships & Partnerships We partner with museums and nonprofit cultural institutions that are vital to the economic health of vibrant, successful communities. Alvin Ailey American Dance Theater's Corrin Rachelle Mitchell and Michael Jackson Jr. in Alvin Ailey's Revelations. Photo by Paul Kolnik. 1 of 4 Frequently asked questions Q: What are consignment services? Art consignment services are those offered by a consultant or financial services firm, that can help a collector arrange for the sale of art and collectibles through partnerships with various auction houses. Often these services can offer pre-negotiated terms available and streamline the sales process. They can also help collectors: Optimize the sale of their property at auction via a preferred selling channelSave time and money with preferred pricing on seller’s commissions and feesReceive sales strategy and independent advice throughout the auction processGenerate liquidity to acquire more art or to raise capital for other opportunities Q: Can I donate my art collection? Yes. When part of a well-structured philanthropic or estate plan, art can be donated to a museum or set of museums. Doing so can help the donor potentially reap tax benefits while supporting an arts institution. But museums are not always able or willing to accept artworks offered to them and if they do, they may not be obligated to keep or display them as you would like. Collectors can also form their own museum, which can offer greater control over how the collection is presented to the public. This approach requires strict adherence to the Private Operating Foundation rules and may also require significant costs of building, maintaining and staffing a museum. Q: What is an art loan agreement? An art loan agreement is a type of structured lending (also known as custom lending) agreement that allows a collector to use their art as collateral for a line of credit, while keeping the collection on display. These kinds of structured loans are often used by collectors to finance business goals; acquire additional artwork; take advantage of other financial opportunities; and/or raise funds for donating and gifting. Q: Can I borrow against my art collection? Fine art is a powerful capital financial asset that may be appropriate as collateral for a structured line of credit. By borrowing against artwork, collectors may create liquidity to take advantage of a broad range of financial opportunities, unlock capital, and/or purchase additional art or cash flowing assets. Banks and other lenders often have strict guidelines for art lending that include the types of art collateral accepted, minimum collection and loan values and loan terms and covenants. Stay ahead of art market trends with our outstanding insights Art Market Update – Spring 2026 Meeting your life goals with customized lending Art and your estate plan Nonfinancial assets, such as closely-held businesses, real estate, fine art, oil, gas and mineral properties, and timber, farm and ranch land, are complex in nature and involve risks including total loss of value. Special risk considerations include natural events (for example, earthquakes or fires), complex tax considerations, and lack of liquidity. Nonfinancial assets are not suitable for all investors. Always consult with your independent attorney, tax advisor, investment manager, and insurance agent for final recommendations and before changing or implementing any financial, tax, or estate planning strategy. The Chief Investment Office (CIO) provides thought leadership on wealth management, investment strategy and global markets; portfolio management solutions; due diligence; and solutions oversight and data analytics. CIO viewpoints are developed for Bank of America Private Bank, a division of Bank of America, N.A., (“Bank of America”) and Merrill Lynch, Pierce, Fenner & Smith Incorporated (“MLPF&S” or “Merrill”), a registered broker-dealer, registered investment adviser and a wholly owned subsidiary of Bank of America Corporation (“BofA Corp.”).","title":"Art Services","url":"https://www.ml.com/articles/art-services.html","id":710},{"content_hash":"2e14029b5aca186ecef9ef437eda7fa4aefee3896c72ea9977b07bc4ce5a2ff6","domain":"www.chinadaily.com.cn","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:34.620716+00:00","final_url":"https://www.chinadaily.com.cn/a/202510/20/WS68f5976ba310f735438b5e19.html","language":"","text":"Open China: Advancing South-South cooperation for global growth - Chinadaily.com.cn Search HOME CHINA WORLD BUSINESS LIFESTYLE CULTURE TRAVEL WATCHTHIS SPORTS OPINION REGIONAL FORUM NEWSPAPER MOBILE Home Opinion Broad Horizon: Open Paths Home / Opinion / Broad Horizon: Open Paths Open China: Advancing South-South cooperation for global growth chinadaily.com.cn | Updated: 2025-10-20 09:58 Share Share - WeChat CLOSE \"Open China\", a 10-part video series produced by China Daily, delves into the profound transformations that have reshaped China over the past four more decades. Through interviews with more than 100 global opinion leaders — including diplomats, economists and business leaders — the series will highlight a unique aspect of China's dramatic journey into a new era. This episode emphasizes China's significant contribution to deepening South-South cooperation. Through key initiatives such as the Belt and Road Initiative (BRI) and the Global Development Initiative (GDI), China has played a pivotal role in fostering economic growth, sustainability, and mutual benefit across the developing world. Uruguay's former ambassador to China Fernando Lugris highlighted the breadth of this collaboration. \"We visualized the cooperation between China and Latin American and Caribbean countries as a comprehensive strategic partnership with many different areas that we have been working on,\" Lugris said. Click the video for more. Photo In Xi's footsteps: Achieving harmony with nature (6) Dandong: More than a gateway 'Surrounded by Labubus at work? Sign me up!' Xi: Cherish oceans as we treat our lives Xi arrives in Pyongyang for state visit to DPRK How Xiamen protects Chinese white dolphins Top BACK TO THE TOP English 中文 HOME CHINA WORLD BUSINESS CULTURE TRAVEL VIDEO SPORTS OPINION REGIONAL NEWSPAPER China Daily PDF China Daily E-paper MOBILE Copyright 1994 - . All rights reserved. The content (including but not limited to text, photo, multimedia information, etc) published in this site belongs to China Daily Information Co (CDIC). Without written authorization from CDIC, such content shall not be republished or used in any form. Note: Browsers with 1024*768 or higher resolution are suggested for this site. License for publishing multimedia online 0108263 Registration Number: 130349 About China Daily Advertise on Site Contact Us Job Offer Expat Employment FOLLOW US Copyright 1994 - . All rights reserved. The content (including but not limited to text, photo, multimedia information, etc) published in this site belongs to China Daily Information Co (CDIC). Without written authorization from CDIC, such content shall not be republished or used in any form.","title":"Open China: Advancing South-South cooperation for global growth","url":"https://www.chinadaily.com.cn/a/202510/20/WS68f5976ba310f735438b5e19.html","id":711},{"content_hash":"bbf6a580bee2f428dcbcb12c89f0346d4ed9020cb3a857ee8303f5fae222ef06","domain":"news.un.org","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:34.342934+00:00","final_url":"https://news.un.org/en/story/2026/10/1168555","language":"","text":"‘Overshoot is not a reason to surrender’: UN calls for accelerated climate action ahead of COP31 summit | UN News Skip to main content / navigation Welcome to the United Nations Language العربية 中文 English Français Русский Español Português Kiswahili Other Hindi हिंदी Urdu اردو Global UN News Global perspective Human stories English Search Search Advanced Search Language العربية 中文 English Français Русский Español Português Kiswahili Other Hindi हिंदी Urdu اردو Global UN News Global perspective Human stories Menu Home Global Africa Americas Asia Pacific Middle East Europe UN Art and Gifts History Corner Topics Peace and Security Economic Development Humanitarian Aid Climate and Environment Human Rights UN Affairs Women Law and Crime Prevention Health Culture and Education SDGs Migrants and Refugees In depth In Focus Interviews Features Photo Stories UN News Today The Lid is On UN Gender Focus UN and Africa UN Podcasts Secretary-General Spokesperson All Statements Selected Speeches Press Encounters Official Travels Media UN Video UN Photo Meeting Coverage Media Accreditation UN Web TV Language العربية 中文 English Français Русский Español Português Kiswahili Other Hindi हिंदी Urdu اردو Global Search Search Advanced Search Audio and Subscription Audio Hub Subscribe ‘Overshoot is not a reason to surrender’: UN calls for accelerated climate action ahead of COP31 summit © Fiji MECC/Kiara Worth Deputy Secretary-General Amina J. Mohammed (right) addresses the opening of the Pre-COP meeting in Tuvalu, ahead of COP31. Facebook Twitter Print Email ‘Overshoot is not a reason to surrender’: UN calls for accelerated climate action ahead of COP31 summit 8 October 2026 Climate and Environment As world leaders prepare for November’s major COP31 climate summit in Türkiye, record-breaking heat, devastating floods and an unprecedented El Niño climate pattern are making global climate action ever more urgent. Ahead of the summit, leaders gathered for a pre-conference in the South Pacific this week to prepare for the intense negotiations to come and set the agenda. UN Deputy Secretary-General Amina Mohammed joined senior government figures and top policy makers in Tuvalu and Fiji – two Pacific island nations facing the brunt of rising seas and intensifying floods – to lay out the UN’s climate priorities. “We must take urgent action to ensure every child born today across the Pacific Islands can grow up, prosper and live on the islands they call home,” she told the pre-COP in Fiji.‘Keeping 1.5 alive’ A key priority raised by the UN Deputy Secretary-General was “keeping 1.5 alive” – referencing the 2015 Paris Agreement target to limit global warming to 1.5 degrees Celsius above pre-industrial levels. As the world is heading to exceed the 1.5°C target, Ms Mohammed urged states not to give up. “Overshoot is not a reason to surrender,” she said in Tuvalu. “It is a call to accelerate – to make overshoot as short and small as possible and bring temperatures back down below 1.5 as quickly as possible.”Reduce emissions, boost security She called on leaders to deliver on promises made at previous climate conferences, most notably the 2023 Climate Change Conference in Dubai (COP28) where leaders agreed to transition away from fossil fuels, triple renewable capacity and double energy efficiency by 2030. She highlighted the benefits of this transition to renewables by linking it directly to energy security. “For the 655 million people still living without electricity, clean power means a mother surviving birth with the lights on, and a child doing her homework after dark,” she said in Fiji. “It frees economies from the price swings from impacts of global conflicts on fossil fuels.”Protect and adapt At the same time, with the impacts of global warming already being felt, the UN Deputy Secretary-General also called for stronger adaptation and protection measures. © UNICEF/Lasse Bak Mejlvang Waves crash against a road by Tuvalu's shoreline. She urged countries to expand early warning systems, which help predict extreme weather events and alert communities before disaster strikes.“An early warning that reaches a family hours before a cyclone gives them time to get to safety,” she explained in Fiji.These systems must be complemented by resilient infrastructure, secure water supplies and healthy ecosystems, she stressed, highlighting ongoing efforts in Pacific communities to strengthen coastal resilience and restore marine ecosystems.Fair funding To enable this transition, a quick, fair and clear funding scheme is critical. She reiterated that developed countries should take the lead – pointing to the Baku to Belém Roadmap which aims to mobilise at least $1.3 trillion annually in climate finance for developing countries by 2035.Crucially, she emphasised that funding must be easy to access. “Every dollar has to arrive where it is meant to go. A small island ministry with a handful of staff should be able to reach concessional finance quickly and simply,” she said in Fiji.“The UN's message remains emphatic: Keep the promise of Paris, fight harder, and make the tragic overshoot as small and short as possible,” she emphasised. ♦ Receive daily updates directly in your inbox - Subscribe here to a topic. ♦ Download the UN News app for your iOS or Android devices. Climate ActionCOP31 Related Stories COP30 kicks off with urgent call to deliver on climate promises and scale up finance Belém COP30 delivers climate finance boost and a pledge to plan fossil fuel transition Countries urged to ‘go further, faster’ and deliver on climate commitments News Tracker: Past Stories on This Issue Security, sacrifice or opportunity: Visions differ over effective climate action 5 October 2026 UN Affairs Should the world move away sharply from fossil fuels, or manage a slower, more careful retreat? Extreme heat making pregnancy a ‘new fault line’ in climate crisis 5 October 2026 Climate and Environment Pregnancy and childbirth have become a “new fault line in the global climate crisis” as extreme heat worsens, the head of the UN climate action body (UNFCCC) warned on Monday, calling for maternal and newborn health to be built into countries’ climate plans. Resources Button collapse Navigate the News Information for Broadcasters UN System Links Media Alert UN Journal Meetings Coverage Audiovisual Library Secretary-General Button collapse All Statements Official Travels Press Encounters SG Twitter Spokesperson's Office Button collapse Latest Statements Briefing Highlights Briefing Transcripts Notes to Correspondents Find Us Button collapse UN News App Facebook Twitter YouTube Footer menu A-Z Site Index Copyright FAQ Fraud Alert Privacy Notice Terms of Use Social Media Links Footer buttons Donate Facebook Twitter Print Email","title":"‘Overshoot is not a reason to surrender’: UN calls for accelerated climate action ahead of COP31 summit","url":"https://news.un.org/en/story/2026/10/1168555","id":712},{"content_hash":"34cbfc463c61c92dbbf7878fb370007535a642e5d2d1de4859a2d8b994c20138","domain":"healthline.com","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:34.279925+00:00","final_url":"https://www.healthline.com/health/mania","language":"","text":"Mania is the hallmark symptom of bipolar disorder. It can lead to dangerous behavior, but treatment is available to manage these episodes. What Is Mania?Mania is a psychological condition that causes a person to experience unreasonable euphoria, very intense moods, hyperactivity, and delusions. Mania (or manic episodes) is a common symptom of bipolar disorder.Mania can be a dangerous condition for several reasons. People may not sleep or eat while in a manic episode. They may engage in risky behaviors and harm themselves. People with mania have a greater risk of experiencing hallucinations and other perceptual disturbances.What Causes Mania?Family history may play a factor in mania. People whose parents or siblings have the condition are more likely to experience a manic episode (National Alliance on Mental Illness). However, having a family member with manic episodes does not mean a person will definitely experience them.Some people are prone to mania or manic episodes because of an underlying medical condition or psychiatric illness, such as bipolar disorder. A trigger or a combination of triggers can cause mania in these people.Brain scans to show that some patients with mania have slightly different brain structures or activity. Physicians do not use brain scans to diagnose mania or bipolar disorder.Environmental changes can trigger mania. Stressful life events, such as the death of a loved one, can contribute to mania. Financial stress, relationships, and illness can also cause manic episodes. Conditions like hypothyroidism can also contribute to manic episodes.What Are the Symptoms of Mania?Patients with mania exhibit extreme excitement and euphoria, as well as other intense moods. They are hyperactive and may experience hallucinations or delusions. Some patients feel jumpy and extremely anxious. A manic personâs mood can quickly change from manic to depressive, with extremely low energy levels (Mayo Clinic, 2012). Manic episodes make a person feel as if he or she has a tremendous amount of energy. They can cause body systems to speed up, as if everything in the world is moving faster.People with mania may have racing thoughts and rapid speech. Mania can prevent sleep or cause poor work performance. People with mania may become delusional. They may be easily irritated or distracted, exhibit risky behavior, and go on spending sprees.People with mania can have aggressive behavior. Drug or alcohol abuse is another symptom of mania.A milder form of mania is called hypomania. Hypomania is associated with the preceding symptoms, but to a lesser degree. Episodes of hypomania also last a shorter amount of time than manic episodes.How Is Mania Diagnosed?A physician or psychiatrist can evaluate a patient for mania by asking questions and discussing symptoms. Direct observations can indicate that a patient is having a manic episode.The Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders (DSM), from the American Psychiatric Association, outlines criteria for a manic episode. The episode must occur for a week, or less than a week if the patient is hospitalized. In addition to a disturbed mood, patients must experience at least three of the following symptoms: He or she is easily distracted.He or she engages in risky or impulsive behavior. This includes spending sprees, business investments, or risky sexual practices.He or she has racing thoughts.He or she has a reduced need for sleep.He or she has obsessive thoughts. A manic episode disrupts a personâs life and negatively affects relationships, as well as work or school. Many manic episodes require hospitalization to stabilize the patientâs mood and prevent self-harm.In some instances, hallucinations or delusions are part of manic episodes. For example, a person may believe that he or she is famous or has superpowers.For the personâs state to be considered a manic episode, symptoms must not be the result of outside influences, such as abuse of drugs or alcohol.How Is Mania Treated?Hospitalization can be necessary if a patientâs mania is severe or is accompanied by psychosis. Hospitalization can help a patient from injuring himself or herself. MedicationsMedications are typically the first line of mania treatment. These medications are prescribed to balance a patientâs mood and reduce the risk of self-injury. Medications include:Lithium (Cibalith-S, Eskalith, Lithane) Antipsychotics such as aripiprazole (Abilify), olanzapine (Zyprexa), quetiapine (Seroquel), and risperidine (Risperdal). Anticonvulsants such as valproic acid (Depakene, Stavzor), divalproex (Depakote), or lamotrigine (Lamictal). Benzodiazepines such as alprazolam (Niravam, Xanax), chlordiazepoxide (Librium), clonazepam (Klonopin), diazepam (Valium), or lorazepam (Ativan). Medications should be used only as prescribed by a medical professional.PsychotherapyPsychotherapy sessions can help a patient identify mania triggers. They can also help patients manage stress. Family or group therapy may also help. Online therapy optionsRead our review of the best online therapy options to find the right fit for you.What Is the Outlook for Mania?An estimated 90 percent of patients who experience one manic episode will experience another (Kaplan, et al., 2008). If mania is the result of bipolar disorder or other psychological conditions, patients must practice lifelong management to prevent mania episodes.Preventing ManiaPrescription medications can help prevent manic episodes. Patients may also benefit from psychotherapy or group therapy. Therapy can help patients recognize the onset of a manic episode so they can seek help.","title":"Mania","url":"https://www.healthline.com/health/mania","id":713},{"content_hash":"8936bdbed4a3c809f4f37c0251676814121a9e0d494ce331aa108a7dea41d1f0","domain":"mongodb.com","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:34.194709+00:00","final_url":"https://www.mongodb.com/company/blog/news/hello-community-meet-2026-mongodb-champions","language":"","text":"We are thrilled to announce this year’s new cohort of MongoDB Champions!Champions are the connective tissue between MongoDB and our builder community, keeping them informed about MongoDB’s latest developments and offerings. Whether they are sharing their knowledge by writing tutorials, speaking at events, or serving as the go-to expert within their company, they are constantly finding ways to support other builders.“Being a MongoDB Champion for the 9th consecutive year is a true honor, “ says Arek Borucki, Machine Learning Platform & Database Engineer at Hugging Face. “This journey has opened doors to writing MongoDB 8.0 in Action, speaking at conferences across the globe, and working with the latest AI and database technologies alongside talented people building innovative solutions. Above all, it's the community that makes this program so special. I'm grateful for the opportunity to keep sharing knowledge, learning from others, and helping developers build the next generation of AI-powered applications with MongoDB.”This year’s 69-member group includes 33 new champions. They come to us from countries all over the world, including Canada, the United States, Malaysia, Colombia, China, India, Brazil, Spain, Ireland, Mexico, France, Thailand, the Republic of Korea, Argentina, and New Zealand. Our Champions wear many different hats in their day jobs. You’ll find them working as engineering leads, chief architects, founders, and everything in between.“I'm excited to be part of the MongoDB Champions program and to collaborate with a global network of innovators pushing the boundaries of data architecture,” says Zoheb Chirammal, Director, Application Development Engineering at Centene Corporation and first-year Champion. “My focus is on driving complex cloud migrations, cloud optimization, and leveraging Atlas Stream Processing for real-time data solutions. I look forward to both learning from this exceptional community and sharing my own enterprise experiences to help shape the future of the ecosystem.”What unites them is a shared passion for helping other builders succeed and a genuine excitement for what’s possible with MongoDB.“Community has always been one of the most rewarding parts of my tech journey,” says Loveleen Kaur, Senior Software Engineer at Twin Health and first-year Champion. “I'm grateful to be recognized as a MongoDB Champion and excited to connect, learn, and give back alongside this amazing group.”As members of this program, Champions gain a variety of experiences—including exclusive access to product roadmaps, preview programs, an annual Champions Summit with product leaders—and relationships that grow their professional stature as MongoDB practitioners, helping them be seen as leaders in the technology community. “Joining the MongoDB Champions program is both an honor and an exciting opportunity,” says Bálder Carraté, Principal Software Engineer at Klikin and first-year Champion. “I’m looking forward to connecting with other passionate MongoDB practitioners, sharing real-world lessons from production systems, and continuing to learn from a community that is constantly pushing what’s possible with data.”And now, without further ado, let’s meet the 2026 cohort of MongoDB Champions!New Champions:Aasawari Sahasrabuddhe, Andres Rangel, Azim Uddin, Bálder Carraté, Barry Ruffner, Bikram Das, ChanLing Li, Darshan Jayarama, Ena Vu, Fatma Selcen Sahin, Genaro Neto, Jesus Ernesto Carrasco, Kanin Kearpimy, Kunal Kannav, Loveleen Kaur, Max Hoarau, Minjong Kim, Mohamed Amr, Mohammed Hamzeh, Ninad Hulle, Pedro Henriques, Pranav Kumar Verma, Prashant Shandilya, Priyanka Taneja, Rama Pabolu, Rashmi Bhagwat, Rossana Suarez, Swetank Poddar, Valeri Karpov, Vincent Thinselin, Yadvinder Brar, Zoheb Chirammal, Zuzana Matevossian. Returning Champions:Abirami Sukumaran, Arek Borucki, Azri Azmi, Carla Barata, Christopher Dellaway, Claudia Cardeno Cano, Elie Hannouch, Flavia da Silva Bomfim Policante, Igor Alekseev, Joey Marburger, Justin Jenkins, Karen Zhang, Kevin Smith, Lai Kai Yong, Leandro Domingues, Luke Thompson, Malak Abu Hammad, Margaret Menzin, Marko Aleksendrić, PhD, Markus Wildgruber, Mateus Leonardi, Michael Höller, Mustafa Kadioglu, Nancy Agarwal, Nenad Milosavljevic, Nuri Halperin, Rajesh Nair, Roman Right, Ruthvik Reddy Anumasu, Sachin Gupta, Samuel Molling, Shaun Roberts, Shrey Batra, Steve Jones, Tamara Manzi de Azevedo, XiaoLei Dai.megaphoneNext StepsFor more, visit our MongoDB Champions page. If you'd like to connect with your local MongoDB community, check out our MongoDB User Groups on Meetup.","title":"“Hello, Community!”: Meet the 2026 MongoDB Champions!","url":"https://www.mongodb.com/company/blog/news/hello-community-meet-2026-mongodb-champions","id":714},{"content_hash":"07c6805c0f30ccb931df66a3bdb07b207bad566da045620bd52a50463085ee44","domain":"www.abc.net.au","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:33.985402+00:00","final_url":"https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-10-05/andrew-mountbatten-windsor-legal-action-after-epstein-arrest/107228702","language":"","text":"Andrew Mountbatten-Windsor launches legal action against police over Epstein files arrestTopic:RoyaltyPosted Mon 5 Oct 2026 at 6:39pmMon 5 Oct 2026 at 6:39pmMon 5 Oct 2026 at 6:39pm, updated Tue 6 Oct 2026 at 8:28amTue 6 Oct 2026 at 8:28amTue 6 Oct 2026 at 8:28amAndrew Mountbatten-Windsor was arrested in February on his 66th birthday. (Reuters: Phil Noble)In short: Andrew Mountbatten-Windsor is taking legal action against the police over his arrest earlier this year.A court hearing will take place ​after the former prince requested a judge examine ‌the lawfulness ⁠of search warrants preceding his arrest.Mr Mountbatten-Windsor was arrested on suspicion of leaking government documents to the late ​sex ‌offender Jeffrey Epstein.abc.net.au/news/andrew-mountbatten-windsor-legal-action-after-epstein-arrest/107228702Link copiedShareShare articleAndrew Mountbatten-Windsor is taking legal action against the police over his arrest in relation to the Epstein files earlier this year.Britain's judicial office said a court hearing would take place on Thursday ​after the former prince and brother of King Charles requested that a judge examine ‌the lawfulness ⁠of search warrants that preceded his arrest ​in ‌February.Britain's Thames ‌Valley Police issued a statement confirming they were ⁠engaged in legal proceedings.\"Whilst our investigation into misconduct in public office continues, we are engaged in legal proceedings in relation to warrants previously obtained from the Central Criminal Court,\" the brief statement said.Andrew Mountbatten-Windsor was stripped of his royal titles in October 2025. (Reuters: Toby Melville)A Palace source said Mr Mountbatten-Windsor had been told that money provided from private funds by his brother, King Charles III, should not be used to fund his legal challenge.Mr Mountbatten-Windsor was arrested on suspicion of leaking government documents to the late ​sex ‌offender Jeffrey Epstein when he was ⁠a special ‌representative for trade ‌between 2001 and 2011.It is the first time a member of the royal family has challenged the lawfulness of criminal proceedings against them since King Charles I's trial in 1649.The arrest of the senior royal, eighth in line to the throne, was also unprecedented in modern times.Ex-prince's emails in Epstein filesMr Mountbatten-Windsor was arrested at his Norfolk home in February this year on suspicion of misconduct in public office.King Charles's younger brother was interviewed for almost 12 hours before he was released under investigation.The focus of the inquiry is the former prince's trade and investment role.It followed the release of millions of documents by the US Department of Justice (DOJ) relating to Epstein.In the glut of files were several emails that appeared to show Mr Mountbatten-Windsor forwarded on sensitive materials to Epstein in 2010.Investigation into King Charles's brother, Andrew, will be lengthy, UK police sayThe British police investigation into Andrew Mountbatten-Windsor will be long and complex, senior officers say, after his arrest earlier this year on suspicion of misconduct in public office.Loading...Being named in the Epstein files is not an indication of misconduct, but trade envoys are required to maintain confidentiality over sensitive, commercial or political information related to their work.The second son of the late Queen Elizabeth has always denied any wrongdoing in relation to Epstein and said he regretted their friendship.He has made no public statement since his arrest.In 2011, Mr Mountbatten-Windsor resigned as trade envoy.Misconduct in public office, which carries a maximum sentence of life imprisonment, can relate to any serious wrongdoing, from sharing confidential information to corruption and sexual misconduct.In May, Thames Valley Police assistant chief constable Oliver Wright said the force was also assessing reports that a woman was taken to an address in Windsor in 2010 for sexual purposes after a lawyer for the alleged victim told the BBC she had been sent to Britain by Epstein for a sexual encounter with the former prince.King Charles, who stripped his sibling of his titles and honours last October, said at the time of his brother's arrest that he was deeply concerned about the news.He said authorities had the royal family's \"full and wholehearted support and cooperation\".ABC/ReutersShare optionsCopy linkFacebookX (formerly Twitter)See more ABC coverage in your search resultsMake ABC a preferred source in GoogleTop StoriesVictorian language charity with $16m kitty has links to white nationalistsTopic:ExtremismFamilies of men killed on Mexico surf trip call for maximum sentencesTopic:CrimeFormer Bachelor Sam Wood to fight for bail application on domestic violence chargesTopic:Law, Crime and JusticeATO delays credit card ban as government backs down after business backlashTopic:Federal GovernmentHow the card surcharge ban could change our relationship with cashTopic:ExplainerPopular nowHow the card surcharge ban could change our relationship with cashTopic:ExplainerUS army's first firing squad execution since WW2 to be publicTopic:HomicideMcLaren driver clocked allegedly doing 259km/h on WA highway Topic:Traffic OffencesRelated topicsPoliceRoyaltyUnited KingdomTop StoriesVictorian language charity with $16m kitty has links to white nationalistsTopic:ExtremismFamilies of men killed on Mexico surf trip call for maximum sentencesTopic:CrimeFormer Bachelor Sam Wood to fight for bail application on domestic violence chargesTopic:Law, Crime and JusticeATO delays credit card ban as government backs down after business backlashTopic:Federal GovernmentHow the card surcharge ban could change our relationship with cashTopic:ExplainerJust InFamilies of men killed on Mexico surf trip call for maximum sentencesTopic:CrimeFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:05pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:05pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:05pmAmbulance ramping data casts doubt over LNP promise to reduce wait timesTopic:Ambulance ServiceFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:05pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:05pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:05pmHow the card surcharge ban could change our relationship with cashTopic:ExplainerFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:01pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:01pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:01pmThe fruit and vegetables to look out for this monthTopic:Food and DrinkFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:04pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:04pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:04pmMore Just InBack to top","title":"Andrew Mountbatten-Windsor launches legal action against police over Epstein files arrest","url":"https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-10-05/andrew-mountbatten-windsor-legal-action-after-epstein-arrest/107228702","id":715},{"content_hash":"4bd247d5103837b62c4108d6d672c2af7b2989e180a850bbd84e47fe31ad8eea","domain":"www.lemonde.fr","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:33.936073+00:00","final_url":"https://www.lemonde.fr/archives/article/1951/11/08/la-metallurgie-lyonnaise-veut-accroitre-sa-productivite_2073059_1819218.html","language":"","text":"Cet article vous est offert Pour lire gratuitement cet article réservé aux abonnés, connectez-vous Se connecter Vous n'êtes pas inscrit sur Le Monde ? Inscrivez-vous gratuitement Archives Archives Archives LA MÉTALLURGIE LYONNAISE VEUT ACCROITRE SA PRODUCTIVITÉ Le Monde Publié le 08 novembre 1951 à 00h00, modifié le 08 novembre 1951 à 00h00 Temps de Lecture 1 min. Article réservé aux abonnés Lire plus tard Mettre Le Monde en favori sur Google Partager Partager sur Messenger Partager sur Facebook Envoyer par e-mail Partager sur Linkedin Copier le lien","title":"LA MÉTALLURGIE LYONNAISE VEUT ACCROITRE SA PRODUCTIVITÉ","url":"https://www.lemonde.fr/archives/article/1951/11/08/la-metallurgie-lyonnaise-veut-accroitre-sa-productivite_2073059_1819218.html","id":716},{"content_hash":"b02d3f739d716bdef9eab43b306e1bbb5cc5a4d28e12fcc68785a06516228811","domain":"www.theconversation.com","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:33.891212+00:00","final_url":"https://theconversation.com/global-warming-dries-up-soil-nutrient-balance-19774","language":"","text":"Global warming dries up soil nutrient balance Published: November 1, 2013 1:27am EDT https://theconversation.com/global-warming-dries-up-soil-nutrient-balance-19774 https://theconversation.com/global-warming-dries-up-soil-nutrient-balance-19774 Link copied Share article Share article Copy link Email Bluesky Facebook WhatsApp Messenger LinkedIn X (Twitter) Print article Global warming will act as a catalyst for increased aridity and result in an imbalance of soil nutrients and decreased productivity in the world’s drylands, according to new research. The study was conducted by a global team of scientists and found increased aridity can be associated with an increase in phosphorus and a decrease in carbon and nitrogen in the soil. More than 200 dryland sites over 16 countries were studied by the team, covering every continent except Antarctica. 41% of the earth’s surface is covered by drylands, supporting 38% of the world’s population. But due to the increase in aridity and growing population, marginal lands will become less reliable yet more depended upon. Read more at UNSW Source UNSW Tags Global warming, Plant nutrients, Soil carbon","title":"Global warming dries up soil nutrient balance","url":"https://theconversation.com/global-warming-dries-up-soil-nutrient-balance-19774","id":717},{"content_hash":"a532e3f13761dc9a729fb4ffc55227287adc9943d9122a11047b7036814248b9","domain":"grafana.com","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:33.871839+00:00","final_url":"https://grafana.com/grafana/dashboards/20394-freebox-monitoring/","language":"","text":"freebox-monitoring | Grafana Labs Searching... Site search Ask Grot AITry using Grot AI for this query -> All Docs View all resultsNo results.There was an error with your request.Grafana Labs is a Leader in the 2026 Gartner® Magic Quadrant™ for Observability Platforms.Learn moreDownloadsContact UsGrafana CloudSolutionsPricingOpen SourceLearnDocs CompanyAI/SearchSign inSign upSite SearchAsk AIAll dashboardsfreebox-monitoringMonitoring dashboard for the freebox delta. Monitoring dashboard for the freebox delta. Tool available here: https://github.com/mazama923/freebox-monitoringData source configCollector type: Collector plugins:Collector config:RevisionsUpload revisionUpload an updated version of an exported dashboard.json file from Grafana Upload new revisionRevisionDescriptionCreatedDownloadGet this dashboard1Sign up for Grafana CloudCreate free account2Import the dashboard templateCopy ID to clipboardorDownload JSONIDDatasourceDependencies Published byLast updateEditResourcesDocs: Importing dashboards Webinar: Getting started with Grafana dashboard design Webinar: Building advanced Grafana dashboardsStill have questions?Ask your questions. Let AI do the heavy lifting.Get every updateSubscribe to our newsletterSubscribeBy submitting, you agree to our Privacy policyGrafana CloudOverviewPricingWhat's in the free tier?AI AssistantAgent ObservabilityApplication ObservabilityKubernetes MonitoringDashboards & VisualizationDatabase ObservabilityFrontend ObservabilitySynthetic MonitoringPerformance & Load TestingIncident Response & ManagementAI InvestigationsWhat’s NewGrafana Cloud StatusSolutionsAI ObservabilityFull-Stack ObservabilityInfrastructure & Cloud ObservabilityCloud Provider ObservabilityDigital Experience MonitoringScaled PrometheusCost Management & OptimizationSite ReliabilityLog ManagementMigrate to OpenTelemetryIntegrationsAll IntegrationsAll PluginsAWSGoogle CloudMicrosoft AzureKubernetesDatadogNew RelicOpen SourceOur ProjectsGitHubDownloadsDashboard TemplatesLearnDocumentationBlogCommunityEventsObservability Survey & ReportsCompanyAbout Grafana LabsCareersPartnershipsNewsroomSuccess StoriesContact UsGetting HelpProfessional ServicesHey AICompareDatadog vs. Grafana CloudDynatrace vs. Grafana CloudElasticsearch vs. Grafana CloudNew Relic vs. Grafana CloudPagerDuty vs. Grafana CloudSplunk vs. Grafana CloudDonut take our word for it. Try Grafana Cloud today.Grafana Cloud StatusLegal & SecurityTerms of ServicePrivacy PolicyTrademark PolicyCopyright 2026 © Grafana LabsGrafana Labs uses cookies for the normal operation of this website. Learn more.Got it!","title":"freebox-monitoring","url":"https://grafana.com/grafana/dashboards/20394-freebox-monitoring/","id":718},{"content_hash":"1265b8740e10f932208951317f08529e485fd8aa926346cab87a8a0226939926","domain":"www.chinadaily.com.cn","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:33.313638+00:00","final_url":"https://www.chinadaily.com.cn/a/202511/10/WS6911e295a310fc20369a4453.html","language":"","text":"Open China: China's openness enhances mutual understanding - Opinion - Chinadaily.com.cn Search HOME CHINA WORLD BUSINESS CULTURE TRAVEL VIDEO SPORTS OPINION REGIONAL NEWSPAPER MOBILE Global EditionASIA 中文双语Français HOME CHINA WORLD BUSINESS CULTURE TRAVEL VIDEO SPORTS OPINION REGIONAL NEWSPAPER China Daily PDF China Daily E-paper MOBILE Opinion Cartoons Editorials Global Lens We Comment Columnists Global Views Chinese Perspectives Opinion Line Home Opinion / Broad Horizon: Open Paths Home / Opinion / Broad Horizon: Open Paths Open China: China's openness enhances mutual understanding chinadaily.com.cn | Updated: 2025-11-10 21:03 Share Share - WeChat CLOSE When the global landscape is facing \"decoupling\" and \"derisking\", which path should the world take — globalization or deglobalization? Openness or isolation? And what is the future of trade cooperation? In this episode, titled \"China's openness enhances mutual understanding\", global experts and diplomats share their insights on China's choice. Follow this video to listen to their answers. Cartoons Xi inspires sci-tech workers Emerald Lake, Mangya, Qinghai Shenzhou XXI astronauts return after 7 months in space Shenzhou XXI crew returns after record-long space mission Shenzhou XXI crew to return to Earth Porcelain carries much more than beauty Most Viewed in 24 Hours Global Lens Renewable Energy Law country's green transition spur Mobilizing private capital to scale digital infrastructure Columnists + China-Serbia ties a good example for the world Huge potential of tiny tokens powering AI revolution Chinese Perspectives Opening up the northern gate of China Growth that doesn't show in economic metrics China and the World Roundtable + Building a shared future through South-South cooperation Navigating a new global security situation Top BACK TO THE TOP English 中文 HOME CHINA WORLD BUSINESS CULTURE TRAVEL VIDEO SPORTS OPINION REGIONAL NEWSPAPER China Daily PDF China Daily E-paper MOBILE Copyright 1994 - . All rights reserved. The content (including but not limited to text, photo, multimedia information, etc) published in this site belongs to China Daily Information Co (CDIC). Without written authorization from CDIC, such content shall not be republished or used in any form. Note: Browsers with 1024*768 or higher resolution are suggested for this site. License for publishing multimedia online 0108263 Registration Number: 130349 About China Daily Advertise on Site Contact Us Job Offer Expat Employment FOLLOW US Copyright 1994 - . All rights reserved. The content (including but not limited to text, photo, multimedia information, etc) published in this site belongs to China Daily Information Co (CDIC). Without written authorization from CDIC, such content shall not be republished or used in any form.","title":"Open China: China's openness enhances mutual understanding","url":"https://www.chinadaily.com.cn/a/202511/10/WS6911e295a310fc20369a4453.html","id":719},{"content_hash":"808e6562382c8e2abb7a04d0b8163ef8e0361bebb4fbc6ad89a9fefdec6fd2fc","domain":"docs.djangoproject.com","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:33.098509+00:00","final_url":"https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/dev/ref/contrib/postgres/aggregates/","language":"","text":"PostgreSQL specific aggregation functions¶ These functions are available from the django.contrib.postgres.aggregates module. They are described in more detail in the PostgreSQL docs. Note All functions come without default aliases, so you must explicitly provide one. For example: >>> SomeModel.objects.aggregate(arr=ArrayAgg(\"somefield\")) {'arr': [0, 1, 2]} Common aggregate options All aggregates have the filter keyword argument and most also have the default keyword argument. General-purpose aggregation functions¶ ArrayAgg¶ class ArrayAgg(expression, distinct=False, filter=None, default=None, order_by=(), **extra)¶ Returns a list of values, including nulls, concatenated into an array, or default if there are no values. distinct¶ An optional boolean argument that determines if array values will be distinct. Defaults to False. order_by¶ An optional string of a field name (with an optional \"-\" prefix which indicates descending order) or an expression (or a tuple or list of strings and/or expressions) that specifies the ordering of the elements in the result list. Examples: from django.db.models import F ArrayAgg(\"a_field\", order_by=\"-some_field\") ArrayAgg(\"a_field\", order_by=F(\"some_field\").desc()) BitAnd¶ class BitAnd(expression, filter=None, default=None, **extra)¶ Returns an int of the bitwise AND of all non-null input values, or default if all values are null. Deprecated since version 6.1: This class is deprecated in favor of the generally available BitAnd class. BitOr¶ class BitOr(expression, filter=None, default=None, **extra)¶ Returns an int of the bitwise OR of all non-null input values, or default if all values are null. Deprecated since version 6.1: This class is deprecated in favor of the generally available BitOr class. BitXor¶ class BitXor(expression, filter=None, default=None, **extra)¶ Returns an int of the bitwise XOR of all non-null input values, or default if all values are null. Deprecated since version 6.1: This class is deprecated in favor of the generally available BitXor class. BoolAnd¶ class BoolAnd(expression, filter=None, default=None, **extra)¶ Returns True, if all input values are true, default if all values are null or if there are no values, otherwise False. Usage example: class Comment(models.Model): body = models.TextField() published = models.BooleanField() rank = models.IntegerField() >>> from django.db.models import Q >>> from django.contrib.postgres.aggregates import BoolAnd >>> Comment.objects.aggregate(booland=BoolAnd(\"published\")) {'booland': False} >>> Comment.objects.aggregate(booland=BoolAnd(Q(rank__lt=100))) {'booland': True} BoolOr¶ class BoolOr(expression, filter=None, default=None, **extra)¶ Returns True if at least one input value is true, default if all values are null or if there are no values, otherwise False. Usage example: class Comment(models.Model): body = models.TextField() published = models.BooleanField() rank = models.IntegerField() >>> from django.db.models import Q >>> from django.contrib.postgres.aggregates import BoolOr >>> Comment.objects.aggregate(boolor=BoolOr(\"published\")) {'boolor': True} >>> Comment.objects.aggregate(boolor=BoolOr(Q(rank__gt=2))) {'boolor': False} JSONBAgg¶ class JSONBAgg(expressions, distinct=False, filter=None, default=None, order_by=(), **extra)¶ Returns the input values as a JSON array, or default if there are no values. You can query the result using key and index lookups. distinct¶ An optional boolean argument that determines if array values will be distinct. Defaults to False. order_by¶ An optional string of a field name (with an optional \"-\" prefix which indicates descending order) or an expression (or a tuple or list of strings and/or expressions) that specifies the ordering of the elements in the result list. Examples are the same as for ArrayAgg.order_by. Usage example: class Room(models.Model): number = models.IntegerField(unique=True) class HotelReservation(models.Model): room = models.ForeignKey(\"Room\", on_delete=models.CASCADE) start = models.DateTimeField() end = models.DateTimeField() requirements = models.JSONField(blank=True, null=True) >>> from django.contrib.postgres.aggregates import JSONBAgg >>> Room.objects.annotate( ... requirements=JSONBAgg( ... \"hotelreservation__requirements\", ... order_by=\"-hotelreservation__start\", ... ) ... ).filter(requirements__0__sea_view=True).values(\"number\", \"requirements\") <QuerySet [{'number': 102, 'requirements': [ {'parking': False, 'sea_view': True, 'double_bed': False}, {'parking': True, 'double_bed': True} ]}]> StringAgg¶ class StringAgg(expression, delimiter, distinct=False, filter=None, default=None, order_by=())¶ Deprecated since version 6.0: The PostgreSQL StringAgg class is deprecated in favor of the generally available StringAgg class. Returns the input values concatenated into a string, separated by the delimiter string, or default if there are no values. delimiter¶ Required argument. A string, Value, or expression representing the string for separating values. For example, Value(\",\"). Deprecated since version 6.0: Support for providing a string is deprecated. distinct¶ An optional boolean argument that determines if concatenated values will be distinct. Defaults to False. order_by¶ An optional string of a field name (with an optional \"-\" prefix which indicates descending order) or an expression (or a tuple or list of strings and/or expressions) that specifies the ordering of the elements in the result string. Examples are the same as for ArrayAgg.order_by. Usage example: class Publication(models.Model): title = models.CharField(max_length=30) class Article(models.Model): headline = models.CharField(max_length=100) publications = models.ManyToManyField(Publication) >>> article = Article.objects.create(headline=\"NASA uses Python\") >>> article.publications.create(title=\"The Python Journal\") <Publication: Publication object (1)> >>> article.publications.create(title=\"Science News\") <Publication: Publication object (2)> >>> from django.contrib.postgres.aggregates import StringAgg >>> Article.objects.annotate( ... publication_names=StringAgg( ... \"publications__title\", ... delimiter=\", \", ... order_by=\"publications__title\", ... ) ... ).values(\"headline\", \"publication_names\") <QuerySet [{ 'headline': 'NASA uses Python', 'publication_names': 'Science News, The Python Journal' }]> Aggregate functions for statistics¶ y and x¶ The arguments y and x for all these functions can be the name of a field or an expression returning a numeric data. Both are required. Corr¶ class Corr(y, x, filter=None, default=None)¶ Returns the correlation coefficient as a float, or default if there aren’t any matching rows. CovarPop¶ class CovarPop(y, x, sample=False, filter=None, default=None)¶ Returns the population covariance as a float, or default if there aren’t any matching rows. sample¶ Optional. By default CovarPop returns the general population covariance. However, if sample=True, the return value will be the sample population covariance. RegrAvgX¶ class RegrAvgX(y, x, filter=None, default=None)¶ Returns the average of the independent variable (sum(x)/N) as a float, or default if there aren’t any matching rows. RegrAvgY¶ class RegrAvgY(y, x, filter=None, default=None)¶ Returns the average of the dependent variable (sum(y)/N) as a float, or default if there aren’t any matching rows. RegrCount¶ class RegrCount(y, x, filter=None)¶ Returns an int of the number of input rows in which both expressions are not null. Note The default argument is not supported. RegrIntercept¶ class RegrIntercept(y, x, filter=None, default=None)¶ Returns the y-intercept of the least-squares-fit linear equation determined by the (x, y) pairs as a float, or default if there aren’t any matching rows. RegrR2¶ class RegrR2(y, x, filter=None, default=None)¶ Returns the square of the correlation coefficient as a float, or default if there aren’t any matching rows. RegrSlope¶ class RegrSlope(y, x, filter=None, default=None)¶ Returns the slope of the least-squares-fit linear equation determined by the (x, y) pairs as a float, or default if there aren’t any matching rows. RegrSXX¶ class RegrSXX(y, x, filter=None, default=None)¶ Returns sum(x^2) - sum(x)^2/N (“sum of squares” of the independent variable) as a float, or default if there aren’t any matching rows. RegrSXY¶ class RegrSXY(y, x, filter=None, default=None)¶ Returns sum(x*y) - sum(x) * sum(y)/N (“sum of products” of independent times dependent variable) as a float, or default if there aren’t any matching rows. RegrSYY¶ class RegrSYY(y, x, filter=None, default=None)¶ Returns sum(y^2) - sum(y)^2/N (“sum of squares” of the dependent variable) as a float, or default if there aren’t any matching rows. Usage examples¶ We will use this example table: | FIELD1 | FIELD2 | FIELD3 | |--------|--------|--------| | foo | 1 | 13 | | bar | 2 | (null) | | test | 3 | 13 | Here’s some examples of some of the general-purpose aggregation functions: >>> TestModel.objects.aggregate(result=StringAgg(\"field1\", delimiter=\";\")) {'result': 'foo;bar;test'} >>> TestModel.objects.aggregate(result=ArrayAgg(\"field2\")) {'result': [1, 2, 3]} >>> TestModel.objects.aggregate(result=ArrayAgg(\"field1\")) {'result': ['foo', 'bar', 'test']} The next example shows the usage of statistical aggregate functions. The underlying math will be not described (you can read about this, for example, at wikipedia): >>> TestModel.objects.aggregate(count=RegrCount(y=\"field3\", x=\"field2\")) {'count': 2} >>> TestModel.objects.aggregate( ... avgx=RegrAvgX(y=\"field3\", x=\"field2\"), avgy=RegrAvgY(y=\"field3\", x=\"field2\") ... ) {'avgx': 2, 'avgy': 13}","title":"PostgreSQL specific aggregation functions¶","url":"https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/dev/ref/contrib/postgres/aggregates/","id":720},{"content_hash":"e7c9da7b4421ade17a31f02a4246c8bffb5f0783ef66bebd49a9587dd794d95b","domain":"healthline.com","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:32.955567+00:00","final_url":"https://www.healthline.com/health/could-it-be-bipolar-signs-to-look-for","language":"","text":"Key takeaways Bipolar disorder includes several types, each characterized by varying degrees of mania and depression, which can sometimes be difficult to distinguish from other conditions. Key signs of bipolar disorder include distinct periods of elevated mood (mania or hypomania) and periods of depression, which can impact energy, sleep, behavior, and overall well-being. An accurate diagnosis is essential for effective treatment, as bipolar disorder can be mistaken for depression or other conditions, and specific treatments like antidepressants may not be effective or could trigger manic episodes. Bipolar disorder is a mental health condition that involves significantly high and low moods. Highs are periods of mania or hypomania, while lows are periods of depression. The changes in mood may also become mixed, so you might feel elated and depressed at the same time.The National Institute of Mental Health estimates that around 4.4% of adults in the United States experience bipolar disorder during their lifetime. The symptoms usually appear between the ages of 18 to 29 years, but they can occur at any age, including childhood and the teenage years.Bipolar disorder can be hard to diagnose, as signs and symptoms vary. The Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders, 5th edition, text revision (DSM-5-TR) lays out the criteria for diagnosing bipolar disorder.Types of bipolar disorderThere are four common types of bipolar disorder. Bipolar I and II are the most common types.Bipolar ITo have bipolar I, a person must experience manic episodes. In order for an event to be considered a manic episode, it must:include shifts in mood or behaviors that are unlike the personâs usual behaviorbe present most of the day, nearly every day during the episodelast at least 1 week, or be so extreme that the person needs immediate hospital carePeople with bipolar I typically have depressive episodes as well, but a depressive episode isnât required to make the bipolar I diagnosis. For a diagnosis of bipolar I, the person should not have another condition that could explain the symptoms.Bipolar IIBipolar II also involves high and low moods, but depressive symptoms are more likely to dominate, and manic symptoms are less severe. This less severe type of mania is known as hypomania.For a diagnosis of bipolar II disorder, a person must:have experienced at least one episode of major depressionhave had at least one episode of hypomanianot have another condition that could explain the symptomsCyclothymic disorderCyclothymic disorder involves changes in mood and shifts similar to bipolar I and II, but the shifts may be less dramatic. A person with cyclothymic disorder will have had symptoms of hypomania and episodes of depression for at least 2 years, or 1 year for children and teens.Bipolar disorder not otherwise specifiedBipolar disorder not otherwise specified is a general category for a person who only has symptoms of bipolar disorder that donât match the three other categories.The symptoms are not enough to make a diagnosis of one of the other three types.Signs of maniaMania can cause other symptoms as well, but 10 of the key signs of this phase of bipolar disorder are:feeling overly happy or âhighâ for long periods of timefeeling jumpy or âwiredâhaving a reduced need for sleeptalking very fast, often with racing thoughts and rapid changes in topicfeeling extremely restless or impulsivebecoming easily distractedfeelings of grandiosity, which is when you feel youâre very important or have important connectionsfeeling as if you can do anythingengaging in harmful behaviors, like having impulsive sex or gambling with life savingsSigns of depressionLike mania, depression can cause other symptoms as well. Here are 10 of the key signs of depression from bipolar disorder:feeling sad or hopeless for long periods of timewithdrawing from friends and familylosing interest in activities that you once enjoyedhaving a significant change in appetitefeeling severe fatigue or lack of energyfeeling slowed down and unable to carry out simple taskstalking slowlysleeping too much or too littlehaving problems with memory, concentration, and decision makingthinking about death or suicide or attempting suicideAn extremely high or low mood can sometimes involve hallucinations or delusions, known as psychosis. During a manic period, the person may have delusions of grandeur. For example, they may believe theyâre very important or have special powers.A person with depressive psychosis might believe theyâve committed a crime or are financially ruined. The person may also see, hear, or smell things that are not there.Substance useSubstance use disorder involves the use of substances like drugs or alcohol in a way thatâs harmful to the personâs mental and physical health. Studies suggest that substance use disorder may be three to six times higher among people with bipolar disorder than in the general population.Having bipolar disorder alongside a substance use disorder can make it harder to treat either condition. It can also affect the outcome of each disorder.People with both disorders are more likely to have a lower quality of life, a less stable progression through treatment, and are more likely to consider suicide.Having a substance use disorder can also make it harder to get an accurate diagnosis. A doctor may have difficulty identifying which symptoms are due to bipolar disorder and which stem from substance use.Â»MORE: Learn about the link between bipolar disorder and alcohol use disorder.Bipolar disorder or depression?Doctors sometimes find it hard to distinguish between bipolar disorder and depression. This can lead to misdiagnosis. People with bipolar disorder are more likely to seek help during a low mood because depression is more likely to have a negative impact on their health and well-being. During a high mood, they may feel exceptionally well.Factors that increase the chance of misdiagnosis include the following:Depression is the dominant mood.Depression is the first episode you have.You have experienced mania or hypomania but have not realized it could be significant.Itâs essential to get an accurate diagnosis in order to work out a treatment plan. Antidepressants may not be effective in treating bipolar disorder.In addition, some antidepressant medications can trigger a first manic or hypomanic episode if youâre susceptible to them. This could complicate both treatment and outcomes.If you go to see your doctor with depression, be sure to tell them about any of the following, as these can help get an accurate diagnosis:a family history of bipolar disorder or other mental health conditionsany other conditions that affect your mental or physical well-beingany medications, drugs, or other substances youâre taking or have used in the past if youâve already tried antidepressants and they didnât helpÂ»MORE: Learn how bipolar disorder is diagnosed.Symptoms in children and teensSymptoms of bipolar disorder usually emerge in early adulthood, though they can occur at any age. Sometimes, they can appear in children.Signs that a child may have bipolar disorder include:getting much more excited or irritable than other childrenhaving high and low moods that seem extreme compared with other childrenhaving mood changes that affect their behavior at school or homeChildren or teens who are experiencing a high mood may:appear excessively happy or silly for long periodshave a short tempertalk rapidly about many different thingshave difficulty sleeping but not be sleepyhave difficulty focusing on an activityhave racing thoughtsseem excessively interested in potentially harmful activities or take unusual risks Those with a low mood may:often feel sad for no apparent reasonhave a short temper or show hostility or angercomplain about aches and painssleep more than usualeat more or less than usualhave difficulty focusingfeel hopeless or worthlesshave difficulty maintaining relationshipshave little energylose interest in things they used to enjoythink about death or suicideThere are many reasons why children and teens can experience mood changes or moods that seem extreme. The hormonal changes in puberty can lead to fluctuations in mood. The symptoms of attention deficit hyperactivity disorder (ADHD) and other conditions can resemble those of bipolar disorder. If youâre concerned about yourself or a young person, seek medical help early. Whatever the reason for mood changes in a young person, getting a correct diagnosis can help manage the symptoms and prevent long-term complications.Suicide preventionIf you or someone you know is considering suicide or self-harm, please seek support:Dial 988 to reach the Suicide & Crisis Lifeline.Text âHOMEâ to the Crisis Textline at 741-741.Not in the United States? Find a helpline in your country with Befrienders Worldwide.Call 911 or your local emergency number if you feel itâs an emergency.While you wait for help to arrive, stay with someone if you can. Remove any weapons or substances that can cause harm. Remember, you are not alone.What bipolar disorder feels likeHealthline connected with people living with bipolar disorder to hear a little bit about their experiences and feelings. Hereâs what they shared: âI have found my bipolar disorder to be exhilarating, dark, and painful. I found that one of the benefits of this disorder was the creativity, energy, and euphoria that came with the mania. For the longest time, I didnât realize that this was mania.ââ MelissaBipolar disorder can affect many different aspects of day-to-day life, including energy levels and sleep. âIt can be difficult to physically move. I tend to sleep 10, or even 12 hours a day.ââ ErinIntense feelings â from feeling like you can do anything to feeling hopeless â are among the most common experiences shared by many people living with bipolar disorder.âEveryoneâs self-esteem fluctuates somewhat. But [with bipolar disorder] you are feeling on top of the world, like you can do no wrong and are the âbestâ at everything one minute, and completely hopeless and self-flagellating the next.ââ SueTalk with your doctorIf you think that you or a loved one has signs or symptoms of bipolar disorder, your first step should be to talk with your doctor. Only a trained medical professional can diagnose this disorder, and diagnosis is key to getting proper treatment. Medication, therapy, or other treatment options can help you or your loved one manage symptoms and maximize quality of life.Â»MORE: Learn more about treatments for bipolar disorder.SummaryBipolar disorder is a mental health condition that involves high and low moods. There are different types of bipolar disorder. Depending on the type, signs and symptoms can range from mania to depression. Symptoms of bipolar disorder can be similar to those of other conditions, including depression, substance use disorder, or ADHD. Getting a correct diagnosis can be challenging but is essential for getting the right treatment.","title":"Is It Bipolar Disorder? Signs and Symptoms to Look For","url":"https://www.healthline.com/health/could-it-be-bipolar-signs-to-look-for","id":721},{"content_hash":"177ab0902ae95600454aea51397b6a72371be4bbfa1ce77ea3dc49db1390d7fb","domain":"youverify.co","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:32.930008+00:00","final_url":"https://youverify.co/en/blogs/merchant-onboarding-process-in-south-africa","language":"","text":"Merchant Onboarding Process in South AfricaByTemitope LawalMarch 14, 2023•5mins ReadWhat is Merchant Onboarding Process?Who is a Merchant Service Provider?What are Merchant Onboarding Solutions?What is Merchant Onboarding Risk?What is the Best Payment Gateway in South Africa- Top Payment Gateways in South AfricaWhich Payment Method is commonly used in South Africa?What is Merchant Onboarding Process Flow?What is Digital Merchant Onboarding- How to Automate your Merchant Onboarding ProcessFrequently Asked Questions on Merchant Onboarding Process in South AfricaDigitize your Merchant Onboarding ProcessShare this post Merchant onboarding process in South Africa is one of the key components of the modern payment gateway. A merchant is required to submit information about its business for review, a process known as underwriting before this merchant can accept electronic payments. As the world continues to move towards a digital future, modern payment gateway and merchant onboarding services are becoming an increasingly important part of the South African economy. In fact, according to Statistica.com, 41% of e-commerce transactions in South Africa were completed using a credit card as of January 2022. This underscores the growing trend of modern payment gateways preferred by South Africans. However, the process can be complex and time-consuming, involving a range of merchant onboarding risk assessments and compliance procedures. In this blog post, we'll provide a comprehensive overview of the merchant onboarding process in South Africa, highlighting the merchant onboarding process flow and offering insights into how businesses can optimize their approach to minimize risk and maximize success. What is Merchant Onboarding Process? The merchant onboarding process is the process whereby payment service providers or payment processors in South Africa bring new merchants onto their payment platforms or marketplace, enabling them to accept payments. These payment processors allow for transactions to happen between merchants and consumer banks. Who is a Merchant Service Provider? A Merchant Service Provider (MSP) is a financial services company that facilitates electronic payment transactions for merchants. They are also known as payment processors or payment service providers. MSPs in South Africa provide merchants with the necessary infrastructure and services to accept various forms of electronic payments, including credit cards, debit cards, and other electronic payment methods during the merchant onboarding process. What are Merchant Onboarding Solutions? Merchant onboarding solutions refer to the processes and tools that enable payment processors to onboard or sign up new merchants onto their payment processing platforms or systems. These solutions help payment service providers streamline the merchant onboarding process, which can otherwise be time-consuming and complicated. Merchant onboarding solutions typically involve a combination of technologies, including application programming interfaces (APIs), software applications, and other digital tools. These solutions enable merchants to submit their information and documentation electronically, which is then verified and processed by the payment processor. As a payment processor, one of the best practices for a seamless merchant onboarding process is using professional merchant onboarding services to onboard new merchants. These merchant onboarding services help to automate your merchant onboarding process and ensure compliance with regulatory requirements. What is Merchant Onboarding Risk? Merchant onboarding risk refers to the potential financial, legal, and reputational risks that a financial institution or payment processor may face when onboarding a new merchant or business onto their platform. When a financial institution or payment processor agrees to provide payment processing services to a new merchant, they assume certain risks. These risks can include fraud, money laundering, regulatory violations, or reputational harm if the merchant engages in activities that are illegal or unethical. To mitigate merchant onboarding risk, payment processors typically implement thorough due diligence procedures, such as background checks, credit checks, and risk assessments, to evaluate the potential risks associated with a merchant. They may also require merchants to provide additional documentation or security deposits to reduce the risk of financial losses. What is the Best Payment Gateway in South Africa- Top Payment Gateways in South Africa The common payment processors otherwise called payment gateways in South Africa include:Payfast Yoco – Best for card paymentsOzow – Best for Instant EFTsZapper – Best for QR codes paymentsSnapScanMobicredPayflexPeach PaymentsPaygatePayGeniusNetcashPayUPaypal2checkoutStripe South Africa In South Africa, the Payments Association of South Africa (PASA) manages a National Payment System (NPS) comprising of over 18 different payment systems which customers and businesses can choose from. These range from low-value card transactions to high-value bond exchange payments. The South African Reserve Bank (SARB) oversees the NPS and is responsible for guaranteeing the safety, efficiency, and settlement of all transactions made by South Africans in the SAMOS system. To protect the stability of the country’s financial sector, the SARB further implements measures to reduce systemic risk within the NPS. Which Payment Method is commonly used in South Africa? There are several payment methods payment processors provide for merchants during the merchant onboarding process in South Africa. They include: CashChecks.Debit cards.Credit cards.Mobile payments.Electronic bank transfersDigital Wallets Among these payment options provided by payment processors, the most common payment option used in South Africa is credit cards. What is Merchant Onboarding Process Flow? The merchant onboarding process flow typically involves several steps that enable businesses or payment processors to effectively onboard new merchants onto their payment processing platforms. The specific steps involved may vary depending on the business and the payment processing platform they use, but generally, the process includes the following: Step 1: Application: A new merchant will apply to accept card payment using a Merchant Account on the payment service provider’s platform he has chosen. The application typically includes providing personal and business information, such as legal name, business name, tax ID, contact information, and banking details. Step 2: Card ReaderThe merchant pays the payment service provider the fees for the chosen Card Reader. Step 3: Due Diligence:The merchant due diligence process is an important step in the merchant onboarding process. It includes: i. Merchant Identity Verification: To comply with AML and KYC requirements for FICA verification, the payment service provider will perform due diligence to verify the merchant's identity, business operations, and financial stability. This may involve conducting a credit check, checking for any criminal history, and verifying the merchant's bank account. Upon completion of these identity verifications, the payment service provider will notify the merchant as to whether or not the application has been approved or declined. If the merchant’s application is approved, the payment service provider will arrange for the Card Reader or any other payment method to be delivered to the merchant’s trading location. ii. Merchant’s Document Verification: There are some FICA requirements for the merchant onboarding process in South Africa. Merchants must provide all FICA documentation! The payment service provider will undergo a verification process on all submitted FICA documents. Merchants must provide the service provider with Fica documents from time to time, as required. Step 4: Integration: Merchants will be required to download the payment service provider app and connect the Card Reader to their Compatible Device.The payment service provider provides the merchant with technical integration information and tools to connect to their payment gateway. This includes APIs, SDKs, and other technical documentation to help the merchant integrate their website or application with the payment service provider's platform. Step 5: Activation: Once the merchant has completed the application, due diligence, integration, and compliance requirements, the payment service provider activates the account and the merchant can start accepting payments. The payment service provider may also provide additional services, such as fraud detection and chargeback management, to help the merchant manage their payment transactions. By agreeing to the terms and conditions of payment processors, merchants automatically authorize payment processors to perform credit and regulatory checks on them and their businesses and/or any other principal, partner, proprietor, or owner of your business. All merchant onboarding process in South Africa may not follow the same exact process, however, there are key steps that must be taken like the FICA document verification. The above are the common merchant onboarding processes payment processors follow in South Africa. What is Digital Merchant Onboarding- How to Automate your Merchant Onboarding Process The digital merchant onboarding process typically involves the use of digital tools and platforms that allow merchants to submit their information and documents online, and for the payment processor or acquiring bank to review and approve the application in a timely manner. This can help reduce the time and cost associated with traditional paper-based onboarding processes. Effective digital merchant onboarding is important for ensuring that merchants are legitimate and comply with regulatory requirements, and for reducing the risk of fraud and chargebacks. It can also help improve the customer experience by enabling merchants to quickly start accepting electronic payments. Today, there are several digital merchant onboarding process in South Africa for payment processors. Frequently Asked Questions on Merchant Onboarding Process in South Africa 1. Can my Card Reader work on another merchant’s account? The Card Reader that is delivered to you is linked to the Merchant Account that you created and will not work with any other Merchant Accounts. 2. When can I start processing transactions on my card reader as a merchant? You can commence processing Transactions from the date on which you have activated the Card Reader but the payout for these transactions will not be completed by the payment service provider until and unless your FICA Documentation has been received, reviewed, approved and electronically stored by the payment processor. 3. Can I transfer my merchant account to another business? Kindly be aware that if you dispose of your business in any manner or there is any alteration in the Authorized Account Holder, principal, partner, proprietor, or owner of your business, you will be required to notify your payment processor in writing about this change and submit all relevant FICA Documentation again. Failure to do so will result in the suspension of your access to the Services, and you will have to complete the merchant onboarding process once more to receive the Services provided by your payment processor. Digitize your Merchant Onboarding Process Take the first step towards modernizing your business by digitizing your merchant onboarding process. By leveraging technology to streamline your workflows, you can improve efficiency, reduce costs, and provide a better experience for your merchants. Don't let manual processes hold you back - make the switch to digital onboarding today and stay ahead of the curve! Join 100+ leading companies to automate your merchant onboarding process with the Youverify workflow automation tool. Try our product to get started. Related ArticlesKnow Your Customer (KYC)Emmanuel Agwu•April 26, 2022What is KYC in Finance?Read MoreKnow Your Customer (KYC)Temitope Lawal•November 2, 2022CBN Tiered KYC Requirements: What Banks and Fintechs Must Verify at Each TierRead MoreKnow Your Customer (KYC)Lola, Edited by Emmanuel Agwu•April 25, 2023Why is Negative News Screening (NNS) Important?Read More","title":"Merchant Onboarding Process in South Africa","url":"https://youverify.co/en/blogs/merchant-onboarding-process-in-south-africa","id":722},{"content_hash":"906cbde76ffb2eb9808487d7c15e3ca85b102b1c8bf2e21cdba6d68aedf7c900","domain":"developers.google.com","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:32.922472+00:00","final_url":"https://developers.google.com/photos/picker/reference/rest/v1/mediaItems/list?hl=pl","language":"","text":"Method: mediaItems.list Zadbaj o dobrą organizację dzięki kolekcji Zapisuj i kategoryzuj treści zgodnie ze swoimi preferencjami. Żądanie HTTP Parametry zapytania Treść żądania Treść odpowiedziZapis JSON Zakresy autoryzacji Zwraca listę elementów multimedialnych wybranych przez użytkownika podczas określonej sesji.Jeśli użytkownik nie wybrał jeszcze wszystkich elementów multimedialnych na potrzeby określonej sesji, zwracany jest błąd FAILED_PRECONDITION. W tym scenariuszu aplikacja powinna sprawdzać wartość sessions.get, aż sesja będzie gotowa, a potem ponownie użyć tej metody. Żądanie HTTP GET https://photospicker.googleapis.com/v1/mediaItemsAdres URL używa składni transkodowania gRPC. Parametry zapytania Parametry sessionId string Wymagany. Wygenerowany przez Google identyfikator tej sesji. pageSize integer Opcjonalnie: Maksymalna liczba elementów multimedialnych do zwrócenia.Usługa może zwrócić mniej niż tę wartość (w tym zero wyników). Jeśli nie podasz tej wartości lub ustawisz ją na 0, zwróci się maksymalnie 50 elementów multimediów. Maksymalna wartość to 100. Wartości powyżej 100 zostaną sformatowane na 100. Wartości ujemne spowodują błąd INVALID_ARGUMENT. pageToken string Opcjonalnie: Token strony otrzymany z poprzedniego wywołania funkcji mediaItems.list. Podaj ten parametr, aby pobrać kolejną stronę. Treść żądania Treść żądania musi być pusta. Treść odpowiedzi Odpowiedź na metodę mediaItems.list. W przypadku powodzenia treść żądania zawiera dane o następującej strukturze: Zapis JSON { \"mediaItems\": [ { object (PickedMediaItem) } ], \"nextPageToken\": string } Pola mediaItems[] object (PickedMediaItem) Strona z wybranymi elementami multimedialnymi. nextPageToken string Jeśli to pole jest ustawione, można użyć go jako pageToken w kolejnym wywołaniu mediaItems.list, aby pobrać kolejną stronę wybranych elementów multimedialnych.Jeśli pominiesz to pole, nie będzie kolejnych stron. Zakresy autoryzacji Wymaga następującego zakresu OAuth: https://www.googleapis.com/auth/photospicker.mediaitems.readonly","title":"Method: mediaItems.list\n\n    \n    \n      \n    \n\n    \n      \n      Zadbaj o dobrą organizację dzięki kolekcji\n    \n    \n      \n      Zapisuj i kategoryzuj treści zgodnie ze swoimi preferencjami.","url":"https://developers.google.com/photos/picker/reference/rest/v1/mediaItems/list?hl=pl","id":723},{"content_hash":"b6e90786675dc62f4c151cc986f8318c9432f52d41ad1a64162bb5dafe214459","domain":"www.lemonde.fr","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:32.765374+00:00","final_url":"https://www.lemonde.fr/archives/article/1951/11/08/l-istiqlal-annonce-qu-il-poursuivra-son-action-dans-la-legalite_2072149_1819218.html","language":"","text":"Cet article vous est offert Pour lire gratuitement cet article réservé aux abonnés, connectez-vous Se connecter Vous n'êtes pas inscrit sur Le Monde ? Inscrivez-vous gratuitement Archives Archives Archives L'ISTIQLAL ANNONCE QU'IL POURSUIVRA son action dans la légalité Le Monde Publié le 08 novembre 1951 à 00h00, modifié le 08 novembre 1951 à 00h00 Article réservé aux abonnés Lire plus tard Mettre Le Monde en favori sur Google Partager Partager sur Messenger Partager sur Facebook Envoyer par e-mail Partager sur Linkedin Copier le lien","title":"L'ISTIQLAL ANNONCE QU'IL POURSUIVRA son action dans la légalité","url":"https://www.lemonde.fr/archives/article/1951/11/08/l-istiqlal-annonce-qu-il-poursuivra-son-action-dans-la-legalite_2072149_1819218.html","id":724},{"content_hash":"7b5aad5f2783fff644ac24afbfb78755a9cc28a1c67685fbd7299b1424ad8321","domain":"www.theconversation.com","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:32.704537+00:00","final_url":"https://theconversation.com/african-americans-place-a-great-value-in-postsecondary-education-20206","language":"","text":"African Americans place a great value in postsecondary education Published: November 12, 2013 7:32pm EST https://theconversation.com/african-americans-place-a-great-value-in-postsecondary-education-20206 https://theconversation.com/african-americans-place-a-great-value-in-postsecondary-education-20206 Link copied Share article Share article Copy link Email Bluesky Facebook WhatsApp Messenger LinkedIn X (Twitter) Print article A Houston area survey has indicated that African Americans are the most likely of all ethnic groups to emphasise post-secondary education. The survey offered a comprehensive look at Harris County’s residents attitudes’ towards higher education. This research indicates that Harris County residents now clearly understand the new realities of today’s knowledge economy. Read more at Kinder Institute Source Kinder Institute Tags Higher education, Knowledge economy, African Americans","title":"African Americans place a great value in postsecondary education","url":"https://theconversation.com/african-americans-place-a-great-value-in-postsecondary-education-20206","id":725},{"content_hash":"aa2c2713359f493018f26646e7af78fdc7278a8537d7c4ee784b5870606f6cbd","domain":"timesofindia.indiatimes.com","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:32.087297+00:00","final_url":"https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/sports/nfl/news/the-geno-smith-assault-case-takes-another-twist-as-detectives-are-back-on-it/articleshow/131949533.cms","language":"","text":"The Geno Smith assault case takes another twist as detectives are back on it | NFL News - The Times of IndiaEditionININUSGCCEnglishEnglishहिन्दीमराठीಕನ್ನಡதமிழ்বাংলাമലയാളംతెలుగుગુજરાતીWeatherSign InTOIsportsNFLCricketWomen's T20 WC 2026IND vs AFGFIFA 2026NBANHLMLBInternational SportsWWETennisLive Cricket ScoreEsportsWPLAshesFormula ENFL ScheduleF1Saudi FootballBadmintonHockeyMMAVideosRacingAthleticsWrestlingShootingBoxingChessIND vs SACollege FootballMLCIND Vs NZT20 World CupT20 World Cup ScheduleT20 World Cup Points TableIPL 2026IPL ScheduleIND vs ENGIPL Points Table 2026IPL Live ScoreIPL Orange Cap 2026IPL Purple Cap 2026Today's ePaperLiveNewsSports NewsNFL NewsThe Geno Smith assault case takes another twist as detectives are back on itTrendingFIFA Golden BootHardik PandyaFIFA World CupCristiano RonaldoVaibhav SooryavanshiErling HaalandJay ShahNitish Kumar ReddyTom BradyLionel MessiFIFA Golden BootHardik PandyaFIFA World CupCristiano RonaldoVaibhav SooryavanshiErling HaalandJay ShahNitish Kumar ReddyTom BradyLionel MessiFIFA Golden BootHardik PandyaFIFA World CupCristiano RonaldoVaibhav SooryavanshiErling HaalandJay ShahNitish Kumar ReddyTom BradyLionel MessiThe Geno Smith assault case takes another twist as detectives are back on itAmisha Pandey / TIMESOFINDIA.COM / Jun 24, 2026, 01:08 ISTCommentsShareAA+Text SizeSmallMediumLarge (Image via Getty Images) New York Jets quarterback Geno Smith is at the center of an active police investigation in Florida, after a woman accused him of assault over the weekend, and after 48 hours of conflicting statements from police about whether the case was even open. Here's the full timeline, as confirmed by police and multiple outlets.Davie police confirm the case is now \"active\"It started Sunday, when a woman who identified herself as \"Kristen\" posted a roughly 85-second video on Instagram accusing Smith of attacking her at his Davie, Florida, home. Police confirmed officers responded to a battery call at Smith's residence around 4:40 p.m. ET that day, but no one was arrested at the scene.What happened next got messy fast. On Monday, police told one outlet the case was \"closed.\" Hours later, a different police statement called it \"not an active case, but still being reviewed.\" By Tuesday morning, the department reversed course entirely, confirming in an official statement that the case is now active: \"We were informed yesterday evening that, during review, it was determined that this case is being further investigated by detectives. It is active and we cannot release any additional information at this time.\" As of the latest reporting, that investigation is ongoing, with multiple detectives now involved.What happens next — for Smith, and for the JetsNo charges have been filed, and Smith hasn't publicly addressed the allegation himself. The Jets also haven't commented. Separately, the woman behind the original post followed up on Monday with another claim, accusing Smith of refusing to hand over his home security footage to police, which hasn't been independently confirmed.Even if the police case eventually closes without charges, that's not the end of the story for the NFL. The league can investigate independently under its Personal Conduct Policy, on its own timeline, regardless of what happens criminally. That matters here: Smith, who returned to the Jets via trade in March, is currently the team's expected Week 1 starter, with a thin and unproven group - Brady Cook, Bailey Zappe, and rookie Cade Klubnik behind him. Training camp opens in about five weeks.This is very much a developing story, and it's already changed shape twice in two days, from \"case closed\" to \"still being reviewed\" to now fully active with detectives digging in. The police report itself still hasn't been made public, Smith hasn't said a word, and the Jets are staying silent too. Until one of those things changes, the safest bet is to treat anything you read here as a snapshot, not the finish line. Get the latest Sports News and Live updates. Download the TOI app.About the AuthorAmisha PandeyAmisha Pandey has been covering the NFL since 2024, with her eyes always locked on the latest buzz — from dating rumors to Instagram posts. With a Bachelor of Commerce degree and a flair for storytelling, she mixes quirky words with an easy, consumable style that keeps readers hooked. Beyond football, Amisha dives into pop culture, viral trends, and celebrity drama, while her personal passions include music, rap, movies, and content creation. Whether it’s breaking down an NFL controversy or vibing to the latest track, she brings the same energy and curiosity to everything she does.Read MoreEnd of ArticleFollow Us On Social MediaVideos'Protectors Became Predators': Dharmendra Pradhan Reacts To NEET Paper Leak Row, Student SuicidesTMC Expels Firhad Hakim, Arup Roy And Six Others As Mamata Cracks Down On Rebel CampUpto 80% Jump in Green Card Fee? Proposition Made; What Would Be Indians' Stake?'Pakistan's Desperate Attempt To Deflect': India Snubs Khawaja Asif's 'War Over Indus' RemarkAliganj Fire: Jyoti's Brother Alleges Corruption, Seeks Murder Charges Against OfficialsMaharashtra RTI Rules 2026 Under Scrutiny: Anna Hazare Demands Changes; Signals Possible Strike'We Expect...': India Reacts To Alleged Desecration Of Lord Ram Photo In BangladeshLucknow Fire: 15 Dead, No NOC, One Exit — India's Decade-Long Fire Safety Failure ExplainedPune's Ketan Agarwal's Death Was No Accident: Police | Fiancée & Alleged Lover Arrested For MurderMinority Affairs MoS George Kurian Resigns; BJP Veteran's Exit Sparks Kerala Political Buzz | Watch123International SportsBrendan Sorsby's NFL dream just got cancelled — Here's the letter that did itLogan Paul challenges NFL stars to wrestle while his brother Jake Paul has NFL aspirations and wants to play for Dallas Cowboys or Cleveland BrownsJalen Hurts goes to DeVonta Smith’s wedding but skips A.J. Brown’s wedding and now WR1 is a New England PatriotESPN NFL Draft analyst loses arm in life-saving surgery after horror crash in MissouriNBC Sports’ Mike Florio predicts Dianna Russini’s interview with Oprah Winfrey just a day before Mike Vrabel’s Patriots vs SeahawksShedeur Sanders trade rumors: Cleveland Browns Year 2 QB’s availability inquired amid quarterback competition with Deshaun Watson12Top Sports NewsLionel MessiAustralia Cricket Team CelebrationNitish Kumar ReddySuryansh ShedgeGeoffrey BoycottWomens T20 World CupTop TrendingGeorge KurianUS-Iran WarKunal ShahFIFA World Cup 2026Stock market crashCUET UG Result 2026Ketan AgarwalGold rate todayDelhi weatherMumbai rainTired of too many ads?go ad free nowTrending StoriesIn NFLIn SportsFIFA WC: Ronaldo back with a brace, leads Portugal to dominant 5-0 win vs UzbekistanIndia survive late Pakistan scare to seal thrilling 4-3 Pro League winRohit Sharma conferred Padma Shri for outstanding contribution to Indian cricketHow hydration breaks are reshaping matches at the 2026 FIFA World CupNot just Japan: Rui Hachimura wants Asia's basketball dream to grow biggerENG XI vs NZ for 3rd Test: Stokes, Atkinson among the four chang