Supersonic Diplomacy: BrahMos Powers Strategic Masterstroke In Gulf, Europe, South AsiaLatest NewsCM claims 10,000 infiltrators expelled, accuses former govt of misleading MuslimsGB boost to service roads in Warje, approach ways to new bridge on Sinhagad RoadRTO clerical staff end 7-day strike after minister promises promotion fixThree months of excess load, no action: Why MVVNL suspended its engineerHaryana launches auto mutation to curb fraud in land recordsIMC issues notices to 47 over building permit fraudScreenings soon of Kirti Chakra awardee’s story Shourya DeepSIT inspects fire incident site, meets injured victimsSchool suspends dining service, asks students to bring lunch from homeWoman alleges gang rape on promise of husband’s release; FIR lodged in ZirakpurRain brings cool relief in Indore as monsoon nears MPPanchkula MC offers 100% interest waiver on property tax dues till June 30Borewell drilling leads to rupture in PNG pipeline, blaze injures 4Relief in sight: new three-lane Edappally Railway Overbridge set to open by SeptIndia seniors take lead in Asia Cup Bridge ChampionshipsUP mandated 3-year electrical safety checks for commercial buildings in 2023‘There was a ball of fire & burning woman fell on me’MD drug factory busted, Rs 4 crore haul seized ; 2 heldCopyright © 2026 Bennett, Coleman & Co. Ltd. All rights reserved. For reprint rights: Times Syndication ServiceFollow Us On","title":"The Geno Smith assault case takes another twist as detectives are back on it","url":"https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/sports/nfl/news/the-geno-smith-assault-case-takes-another-twist-as-detectives-are-back-on-it/articleshow/131949533.cms","id":726},{"content_hash":"9d903ab21b040423de5a282f71d9550df35a2b56be3e2e69254072e7e12e4d39","domain":"reallygoodemails.com","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:31.914585+00:00","final_url":"https://reallygoodemails.com/features/ai/mcp","language":"","text":"Connect your AI tools to RGE Studio's email MCP server.Use Claude, ChatGPT, n8n, or other AI tools to work with your existing RGE Studio designs, create new emails, save them to the right workspace, and export the HTML.Talk to our teamOr start freeWorks withThe problemAI platforms don't understand your email complexityAI platforms can spit out an email pretty quickly. But is it ready to ship? The typical AI-generated email still needs work to be sent out from your ESP. And it’s not just you. We asked the email community what gets in the way when using AI, and two answers came back the loudest: lack of trust and scattered tools.54%of respondents don't fully trust AI-generated email outputThey want confidence that what ships is accurate and safe to send, not another draft to double-check.40%want AI built into the tools they already useNot one more tab to copy in and out of. The workflow should stay in one place.Source: RGE Survey 2026, 855 email professionalsThe solutionMeet RGE Studio MCPRGE Studio MCP is a remote MCP server that gives compatible AI tools access to the Studio actions your team already uses. Just ask your AI tool to find, create, update, preview, save, or export an email. No copy-paste, no rebuild required.And because of RGE Studio's brand settings and permissions, on-brand emails are much easier to ensure for every output.Discover helpful promptsFind an emailPull up a design by asking in plain language, and without needing to open RGE Studio.Create from contextStart from an approved email or use your saved workspace styles as a starting point.Save & ExportSave the email to the right account, workspace, and folder.Why connect itKeep the workflow in one place1Works with your AI toolsCall up RGE Studio inside Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, n8n, custom agents, or any other AI tool.2Perfect codeBecause it relies on your existing designs and brand styles, the MCP creates something that's actually ready to ship - no broken code.3No tool-switchingFind, act on, and distribute designs conversationally, without leaving the AI environment or breaking the workflow.Game-changing, right?Here is everything you can doFind existing designsSearch across workspaces and folders without digging through them manually.Create from an approved emailUse an existing design as the starting point for a new one.Use saved workspace stylesAsk the AI to use your workspace's saved styles when creating a new design.Save to the right placeChoose the account, workspace, and folder conversationally.Preview without opening the builderSee a saved email preview inside the connected AI tool.Update an existing emailReplace the content of a saved email with a new version.Clone and editRetrieve an existing email, duplicate it, make changes, and save the new version back to RGE Studio.Export the HTMLGet the finished HTML when it is time to move the email into your sending platform.Talk to our teamOr start freeWho it is forBuilt for teams already working with AIMeet your new helpful AI co-worker. Don’t know where to start? Pick from a whole library of plug-and-play prompts.Marketing teamsYou run ongoing campaigns, work with more than one cook in the kitchen, and follow structured approval steps. RGE Studio MCP connects fast AI creation to the place where email becomes editable, reviewable, and ready to ship.Talk to our teamDevelopers and technical teamsYou build email from code or work inside tools like Cursor. Because RGE Studio MCP uses a standard interface, you can connect it to the same AI workflows as the rest of your stack.Start free and connect your toolsPlug & PlayConnect once, then just askRGE Studio MCP is a remote server, so there is nothing to install and no API key to copy. Add the server URL to your MCP-compatible tool, sign in with your RGE Studio account, and you are ready to go. Your existing Studio roles and permissions still apply.Talk to our teamRead the setup docsAI + email: where we standAI can make the draft. Your team still ships the email.AI is good at speed. Your team is good at judgment. RGE Studio connects the two: fast creation up front, human review before anything goes out the door ✨Our AI manifestoReally good questionsEverything you probably want to knowWhat is an email MCP server? MCP stands for Model Context Protocol, an open standard that lets AI tools like Claude or ChatGPT connect to external software (in this case, RGE Studio) and act inside it, not just talk about it. The AI tool's MCP client uses the protocol to reach that software and call its actions directly, so the two can actually work together. An email MCP applies that to an email platform. Once the connection is live, you can work with your emails just by asking your AI tool to find a design, build a new one, preview it, and export it. No switching tabs, no copy-paste. RGE Studio's MCP Server is our version of that. It connects RGE Studio to the AI tools you already use, so you can create, edit, and export emails right from Claude, ChatGPT, n8n, or your own agent, without ever leaving that tool.Is the RGE Studio MCP Server included with my current plan, or does it cost extra? RGE Studio MCP is free to connect on all plans. It is available to all RGE Studio user types, except viewers.Are there usage limits or rate limits? No limits. The AI tokens you're using are your own, from the AI service you connect. They won't be metered or monitored in RGE Studio.Which AI tools does the RGE Studio MCP Server work with? Any AI tool can connect. Claude is the most tested option today. ChatGPT, Cursor, n8n, Microsoft Copilot, and custom agents can also be connected.Do I need to install anything? Nope. Add the remote server URL, sign in with your RGE Studio credentials once, and you are connected. Step-by-step instructions on how to connect the RGE Studio MCP are available in the support docs.Does RGE Studio MCP replace my ESP? No. The RGE Studio MCP helps you create, manage, review, and export the email, making the most of the AI capabilities your team works with. Your ESP still handles the send.Is connecting the RGE Studio MCP server secure? Security, authentication, and the right permissions are key tenets of the way we built the RGE Studio MCP. You connect by signing in through a secure authorization link (OAuth): you log in with your RGE Studio credentials, so your AI tool is linked to your account without you pasting a password or API key. Your RGE Studio role comes with you, so the MCP can only do what your role already allows. Viewers, for instance, can't create emails through it.Are my existing permissions respected? Yes. Your RGE Studio roles and permissions still apply. A viewer does not suddenly become an admin because Claude asked nicely.Can I review or undo changes made to an email design through the MCP Server? When the AI updates an existing email, it replaces that email with the new version. If you want to keep the original as-is, ask it to clone the design instead: the MCP can clone an existing email and let you edit the copy in your AI tool, then save that back. Also, just asking the AI agent to undo the last changes in the same chat usually works.Are exported designs compatible with all major email service providers? The MCP connects with RGE Studio, which allows you to export your finished email design into your ESP. Because it's a standard HTML export, you can use it even with an ESP that RGE Studio has no native connector for.What support is available if the MCP Server connection stops working? If something stops working, you can reach the RGE Studio team through the usual support channels. For tool-specific setup snags, it's always helpful to consult your AI tool's own documentation (Claude, ChatGPT, n8n, Claude Code, or a custom agent), since these interfaces change often and the current steps live there.RGE Studio + your AI tool = a better way of making emails.Want to see what this looks like when tailored to your team, stack and needs? We are here to help.Talk to an expertOr start free","title":"Connect your AI tools to RGE Studio's email MCP server.","url":"https://reallygoodemails.com/features/ai/mcp","id":727},{"content_hash":"4a79ee861b5646d0e8f7527246e1db46c4b9030c3351258ba9d956a56bc486d9","domain":"www.abc.net.au","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:31.863317+00:00","final_url":"https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-09-21/earl-spencer-prince-harry-meghan-princess-diana-media-treatment/107175286","language":"","text":"Harry and Meghan's media treatment echoes what happened to Diana, Charles Spencer tells BBCTopic:RoyaltyPosted Mon 21 Sep 2026 at 9:31amMon 21 Sep 2026 at 9:31amMon 21 Sep 2026 at 9:31am, updated Mon 21 Sep 2026 at 11:02amMon 21 Sep 2026 at 11:02amMon 21 Sep 2026 at 11:02amLoading...In short:Princess Diana's brother says the Duke and Duchess of Sussex should be given official security.Charles Spencer said the media treated Harry and Meghan the same way it treated Diana in the years leading up to her death.His upcoming book about Princess Diana is highly critical of King Charles. abc.net.au/news/earl-spencer-prince-harry-meghan-princess-diana-media-treatment/107175286Link copiedShareShare articlePrincess Diana's brother says Prince Harry and his wife Meghan should be given official security because the media now treats them much the same way as it treated his sister in the years leading up to her death. Diana was 36 when she was killed in a 1997 Paris car crash while being pursued by photographers on motorbikes.Her death sparked an outpouring of grief and a reckoning over whether the media, which splashed details of her life across front pages for years, bore some responsibility.Prince Harry and his wife Meghan recently returned to the United Kingdom after six years in California. (AP: Jonathan Brady)Charles Spencer has been speaking to the media in the lead-up to the publication of his book about his sister, which is critical of her former husband, the now-King Charles. \"From a security aspect, as an uncle who's seen his sister die in very, very preventable circumstances, I would veer towards protection,\" Earl Spencer said of Harry and Meghan when speaking to the BBC. He said the tabloid treatment of Diana, and Harry and Meghan, could be \"really, really unpleasant\", and that it was \"beholden on people\" to learn from that experience.Spencer's book makes international headlinesEarl Spencer's book, Swan Song: Diana, My Sister, has made headlines around the world because it includes accusations about Charles making incendiary comments in the days after the princess's death.In the book, Earl Spencer accuses Diana's former husband, the then-prince of Wales, of sounding \"giddily elated\" in the hours after her death. Loading...Earl Spencer also writes that an angry Charles had told him that the world would forget Diana soon enough.In a rare move, the palace has hit back by saying the king is \"mindful that the pain of fraternal grief can cloud reason, affect judgement and colour memory in ⁠ways others do not recognise, even many years after such a loss\".Asked by the BBC how he could prove the conversations had taken place, Earl Spencer said he had included a specific line in his much-lauded eulogy at Diana's funeral to counter the comments, ending it by saying she would \"never be extinguished from our minds\".Earl Spencer said he had written the book, ahead of the 30th anniversary of her death, to celebrate her life.'I'm telling the truth': Diana's brother on king's 'monstrous' phone callPrincess Diana's brother has doubled down on his swathe of explosive claims about Britain's royal family, insisting he is \"telling the truth\", and suggesting the king is \"embarrassed\".He said their childhood never had a dull moment. \"We both have ADHD,\" he said. \"She was never diagnosed, but clearly we did.\"The publication of the book and the surprise return of Harry and Meghan to Britain after six years living in the US pose a challenge for King Charles, who is still undergoing treatment for cancer.Princess Diana's family accused the royals of showing a lack of support or care towards her before her death, a charge that was repeated by Harry and Meghan about their personal experience before they quit royal duties in 2020 to move abroad.Prince Harry has criticised the British government's decision to strip him and his family of automatic police protection afforded to other senior royals since he quit royal duties. Following a long-running legal battle, that is now under review.Earl Spencer, who recently hosted the couple, has serialised his book through The Daily Mail, just months after Prince Harry lost an expensive privacy lawsuit against the tabloid.Earl Spencer said his revelations about King Charles would not come as a surprise to Prince Harry or his older brother, heir-to-the-throne Prince William, and he said while he knew many more details about the king, he had chosen not to include them.ReutersShare optionsCopy linkFacebookX (formerly Twitter)See more ABC coverage in your search resultsMake ABC a preferred source in GoogleTop StoriesVictorian language charity with $16m kitty has links to white nationalistsTopic:ExtremismFormer Bachelor Sam Wood to fight for bail application on domestic violence chargesTopic:Law, Crime and JusticeFamilies of men killed on Mexico surf trip call for maximum sentencesTopic:CrimeATO delays credit card ban as government backs down after business backlashTopic:Federal GovernmentHow the card surcharge ban could change our relationship with cashTopic:ExplainerPopular nowHow the card surcharge ban could change our relationship with cashTopic:ExplainerUS army's first firing squad execution since WW2 to be publicTopic:HomicideMcLaren driver clocked allegedly doing 259km/h on WA highway Topic:Traffic OffencesRelated topicsEnglandMediaRoyaltyUnited KingdomTop StoriesVictorian language charity with $16m kitty has links to white nationalistsTopic:ExtremismFamilies of men killed on Mexico surf trip call for maximum sentencesTopic:CrimeFormer Bachelor Sam Wood to fight for bail application on domestic violence chargesTopic:Law, Crime and JusticeATO delays credit card ban as government backs down after business backlashTopic:Federal GovernmentHow the card surcharge ban could change our relationship with cashTopic:ExplainerJust InFamilies of men killed on Mexico surf trip call for maximum sentencesTopic:CrimeFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:05pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:05pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:05pmAmbulance ramping data casts doubt over LNP promise to reduce wait timesTopic:Ambulance ServiceFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:05pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:05pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:05pmHow the card surcharge ban could change our relationship with cashTopic:ExplainerFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:01pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:01pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:01pmThe fruit and vegetables to look out for this monthTopic:Food and DrinkFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:04pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:04pmFri 9 Oct 2026 at 4:04pmMore Just InBack to top","title":"Harry and Meghan's media treatment echoes what happened to Diana, Charles Spencer tells BBC","url":"https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-09-21/earl-spencer-prince-harry-meghan-princess-diana-media-treatment/107175286","id":728},{"content_hash":"b624fea4632c2e9a3acd92fb70da1bccb18ce9fcf3db8d66319e1eaa86efb4f2","domain":"healthline.com","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:31.857601+00:00","final_url":"https://www.healthline.com/health/drugs/vyepti","language":"","text":"Key takeaways Vyepti infusions are prescribed to help prevent migraine episodes in adults. The infusions are given every 3 months and take about 30 minutes. Vyepti works by blocking the activity of a protein in the brain called calcitonin gene-related peptide (CGRP). This can help reduce migraine pain and other symptoms. The cost of Vyepti can vary based on where you receive your infusions and other factors. The manufacturer offers some financial assistance and support options that may help reduce your costs. Vyepti contains the active ingredient eptinezumab-jjmr and is a biologic medication. A biologic is made from parts of living cells.Learn more about how Vyepti works for migraine prevention, how it’s given, and what to expect while receiving the medication.Is Vyepti used for migraine?Yes, Vyepti is an infusion used to prevent migraine episodes in adults. Headaches that result can be moderate to severe and may last anywhere from 4 to 72 hours. Migraine pain usually affects one side of a person’s head.Besides headaches, other symptoms can occur with a migraine episode, such as:nauseavomitingsensitivity to light or soundaura symptoms, such as flashes of light or trouble seeingQuick note: Vyepti is not used to treat migraine symptoms when they occur, only to help prevent them in the first place. Your doctor or pharmacist can suggest other medications for treating migraine symptoms as they happen.Mechanism of action: How does Vyepti work?Vyepti is an antibody, and it’s part of a group of drugs called calcitonin gene-related peptide (CGRP) blockers.CGRPs bind to other proteins in the brain called receptors, which act as docking stations. It’s thought that this binding results in migraine pain.Vyepti attaches to CGRPs so that these proteins can’t bind to their receptors. This helps to prevent migraine pain.Â»FIND CARE:Find a neurologist in your area today.What are Vyeptiâs side effects?Side effects of Vyepti that have been reported include:cold-like symptomsallergic reactionWhat can you do?Mild side effects of many drugs may go away within a few days to a couple of weeks. But if they become bothersome, talk with your doctor or pharmacist.If you have serious side effects from Vyepti, call your doctor right away. But if you think you’re having a medical emergency, you should call 911 or your local emergency number.Experiencing side effects? After the Food and Drug Administration (FDA) approves a drug, it tracks and reviews side effects of the medication. If you develop a side effect while taking this drug and want to tell the FDA about it, visit MedWatch or call 800-FDA-1088.Â»Read more:Managing Vyepti Side Effects: How to Stay Safe and ComfortableWhat are some frequently asked questions about Vyepti?Does Vyepti cause weight gain?No, it’s not likely. Weight gain wasn’t one of the side effects reported in studies of Vyepti.Does Vyepti cause hair loss?No, hair loss wasn’t reported as a side effect in studies of Vyepti.Stress from chronic migraine episodes may also lead to hair thinning. But hair loss isn’t an expected side effect of Vyepti.What should I know about Vyepti vs. Aimovig?Vyepti and Aimovig both belong to the same group of medications, CGRP blockers. CGRP blockers help prevent migraine episodes. But the active ingredients of these two medications are different: Aimovig contains erenumab-aooe, and Vyepti contains eptinezumab-jjmr.Read more: An Overview of Aimovig, Including Uses, Dosage, and Side EffectsQ: Will I have withdrawal symptoms if I stop receiving Vyepti?AnonymousA:No, you won’t have withdrawal symptoms if you stop receiving Vyepti. Withdrawal symptoms can occur when a person suddenly stops taking a drug their body is dependent on. Dependence refers to the body needing a drug to function as usual.But it’s possible that you’ll see an increase in migraine episodes when you stop Vyepti treatment. Before you stop Vyepti treatment, talk with your doctor.The Healthline Pharmacist TeamAnswers represent the opinions of our medical experts. All content is strictly informational and should not be considered medical advice.What does Vyepti cost?What you’ll pay for Vyepti may depend on several things, such as your treatment plan and where you receive your Vyepti infusion.If you have questions about how to pay for your prescription, talk with your doctor or pharmacist. You might also want to visit the Vyepti manufacturer’s website to see whether it has support options that you’re eligible for.Â»Read more:Vyepti and Cost: What You Need to KnowWhat is Vyeptiâs dosage?Your doctor will tell you how much Vyepti you’ll need. You’ll receive your dose of Vyepti once every 3 months. Depending on how well Vyepti works and how severe your migraine episodes are, you might need a higher dose.How it’s givenVyepti comes as a solution that a healthcare professional will inject directly into a vein over a period of time. This is known as an IV infusion. Vyepti IV infusions take about 30 minutes.What if I miss a dose of Vyepti?If you miss a Vyepti infusion appointment, call your doctor’s office to reschedule. Missing a dose of Vyepti may cause migraine episodes to return. If you’ve missed a dose of Vyepti, talk with your doctor to find out when you’ll need to receive your next dose.How long does Vyepti take to work?Vyepti works quickly, but it may take a few weeks for you to notice. In studies, people saw a decrease in their migraine episodes within the first 3 months.Improvement was measured by how many migraine days a person had over 3 months.Â»Read more:Dosage Details for VyeptiWhat should be considered before taking Vyepti?Some important things to discuss with your doctor when considering treatment with Vyepti include your overall health and any medical conditions you may have.InteractionsSo far, there aren’t any known interactions between Vyepti and other drugs, vitamins, supplements, or herbs. But this doesn’t mean interactions with Vyepti can’t happen.To be safe, talk with your doctor before taking any drugs, vitamins, herbs, or supplements during Vyepti treatment.Â»Read more:Drug Interactions: A Guide for ConsumersWarningsVyepti may not be right for you if you have certain medical conditions or other factors that affect your health. Talk with your doctor about your health history before you start Vyepti treatment. Here are some factors to consider:Raynaud phenomenonTell your doctor if you have a personal or family history of Raynaud phenomenon. This condition occurs when blood vessels in your hands and feet constrict, reducing blood flow to those body parts.Raynaud phenomenon wasn’t reported with Vyepti, but there have been postmarket reports of this side effect occurring with similar drugs. You may have a higher risk of Raynaud phenomenon if you’ve previously had it. If you develop symptoms of this condition, your doctor will likely recommend stopping treatment with Vyepti.High blood pressureIf you have high blood pressure, talk with your doctor before starting treatment with Vyepti. There have been postmarket reports of Vyepti and similar drugs causing new or worsening high blood pressure. This may happen at any point during treatment, but it’s most common within 1 week of the first Vyepti dose. During treatment, your doctor will monitor your blood pressure. In some cases, they may recommend stopping treatment with Vyepti.AgeVyepti hasn’t been studied much in adults ages 65 years and older. Due to this, it’s not known for sure whether older adults respond differently to the medication. If you’re age 65 or older, talk with your doctor about your health factors and whether Vyepti is safe for you.Constipation with serious complicationsWhile not reported in Vyepti’s studies, constipation with serious complications, such as hospitalization, has happened with Vyepti and similar drugs after it was made available. Your doctor will monitor you closely during your treatment with Vyepti.Allergic reactionIf you’ve had a serious allergic reaction to Vyepti or any of its ingredients, your doctor will likely recommend that you don’t receive Vyepti. Ask your doctor what other medications are better options for you.Pregnancy and breastfeedingIt’s unknown whether Vyepti is safe to use during pregnancy or while breastfeeding.Migraine episodes can be dangerous during pregnancy. Someone who’s pregnant and has a migraine may be at higher risk of high blood pressure and a severe pregnancy complication called preeclampsia. If you’re pregnant, considering pregnancy, breastfeeding, or considering breastfeeding while receiving Vyepti, talk with your doctor. You can discuss the best treatment option to prevent migraine episodes during this time.Â»Read more:Vyepti and Pregnancy: What You Need to KnowNext steps: What you can do todayYou may have questions about Vyepti and your treatment plan. It’s important to discuss all your concerns with your doctor. Here are a few tips that might help guide your discussion:Before your appointment, write down any questions you have.Bring someone with you to your appointment if doing so will help you feel more comfortable.If you don’t understand something related to your condition or treatment, ask your doctor to explain it to you.Â»Read more:Relief from Chronic Migraine: Current and Emerging TreatmentsDisclaimer: While Healthline strives for factual, comprehensive, and current consumer drug information, this article is not a substitute for a licensed healthcare professional’s expertise. Always consult a doctor before taking or discontinuing any medication. Drug information is subject to change and may not cover all uses, directions, precautions, warnings, interactions, reactions, or adverse effects. The lack of a warning does not guarantee a drug’s safety, effectiveness, or appropriateness for all patients or specific uses. Learn more about our approach to content integrity.","title":"Everything You Need to Know About Vyepti for Migraine Prevention","url":"https://www.healthline.com/health/drugs/vyepti","id":729},{"content_hash":"c39cae8ed7f03f0523b794b22abbf8885913f6a7d6a7407b0047f378da679654","domain":"prnigeria.com","fetched_at":"2026-10-09T05:27:31.816125+00:00","final_url":"https://i0.wp.com/prnigeria.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/ICPC-Operatives-1024x660-1.jpg?fit=800%2C515&ssl=1","language":"","text":"ÿØÿà�\u0010JFIF�\u0001\u0001\u0001�`�`��ÿÛ�C� \u0007\u0007\b\u0007\u0006 \b\b\b \u000e\u0018\u0010\u000e \u000e \u0015\u0016\u0011\u0018# %$\" \"!&+7/&)4)!\"0A149;>>>%.DIC;ÿÛ�C\u0001 \u000e \u000e \u0010\u0010 ;(\"(;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;ÿÂ�\u0011\b\u0002\u0003\u0003 \u0003\u0001!�\u0002\u0011\u0001\u0003\u0011\u0001ÿÄ�\u001